edium shark, velociraptor, warpony, dire badger, dire bat, dire weasel, monitor lizard; aquatic only: hippocampus, porpoise, sea tiger, sharks, sea cat. (Offered here: the creatures in the core data; it replaces nothing.)
Sword of Celestia	KEY:Paladin ACF ~ Sword of Celestia (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PaladinACF.PaladinSpecialMount	PRECLASS:1,Paladin=5	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Sword of Celestia (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.447	DESC:Alternative class feature (paladin, 5th level). Celestial weaponsmiths forge a weapon of a kind you choose (such as longsword), which you must name and are bound by oath never to sell, give or loan. You can summon it to your hand or return it as a free action, even after being disarmed, %1 times per day (1 + Wisdom modifier, minimum 1). It is a +1 weapon at 5th level, +2 at 10th, +2 holy at 15th and +2 holy lawful at 20th; it overcomes damage reduction as if good-aligned, healing magic repairs it as a living creature, and you may enhance it as if you had Craft Magic Arms and Armor. If destroyed, a new one is presented a year and a day later. Replaces the special mount.
Sword of Celestia	KEY:ACF ~ Sword of Celestia (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Paladin Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.447	DESC:Celestial weaponsmiths forge a weapon of a kind you choose (such as longsword), which you must name and are bound by oath never to sell, give or loan. You can summon it to your hand or return it as a free action, even after being disarmed, %1 times per day (1 + Wisdom modifier, minimum 1). It is a +1 weapon at 5th level, +2 at 10th, +2 holy at 15th and +2 holy lawful at 20th; it overcomes damage reduction as if good-aligned, healing magic repairs it as a living creature, and you may enhance it as if you had Craft Magic Arms and Armor. If destroyed, a new one is presented a year and a day later. Replaces the special mount.|max(1,1+WIS)
Warded Special Mount	KEY:Paladin ACF ~ Warded Special Mount (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PaladinACF.PaladinWardedMount	PRECLASS:1,Paladin=6	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Warded Special Mount (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.449	DESC:Alternative class feature (paladin, 6th level). Lightbringer paladin: in addition to its standard qualities, his special mount is immune to all death spells, magical death effects, energy drain and any negative energy effects (such as inflict spells or chill touch). Replaces one weekly use of remove disease (reduce the uses by hand).
Warded Special Mount	KEY:ACF ~ Warded Special Mount (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Paladin Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.449	DESC:Lightbringer paladin: in addition to its standard qualities, his special mount is immune to all death spells, magical death effects, energy drain and any negative energy effects (such as inflict spells or chill touch). Replaces one weekly use of remove disease (reduce the uses by hand).
Inquisitor	KEY:Paladin ACF ~ Inquisitor (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PaladinACF.PaladinLayOnHands.PaladinTurnUndead.PaladinRemoveDisease	PRECLASS:1,Paladin=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Inquisitor (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.433	DESC:Alternative class feature (paladin, 1st level). The paladin who takes an active role in hunting her foul enemies gives up her defensive powers: she gains favored enemy as the ranger ability, at the levels a ranger gains it by her paladin level (1st, 5th, 10th, 15th, 20th; chosen in the Favored Enemy categories), but may only select aberrations, dragons, giants, monstrous humanoids, evil outsiders or undead (the limit is not enforced). Replaces lay on hands, turn undead and remove disease.
Inquisitor	KEY:ACF ~ Inquisitor (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Paladin Class Feature	ABILITY:Ranger Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Ranger ~ Favored Enemy	BONUS:VAR|RangerFavoredEnemyLVL|PaladinLVL	SOURCEPAGE:p.433	DESC:The paladin who takes an active role in hunting her foul enemies gives up her defensive powers: she gains favored enemy as the ranger ability, at the levels a ranger gains it by her paladin level (1st, 5th, 10th, 15th, 20th; chosen in the Favored Enemy categories), but may only select aberrations, dragons, giants, monstrous humanoids, evil outsiders or undead (the limit is not enforced). Replaces lay on hands, turn undead and remove disease.
Wyrmslayer	KEY:Paladin ACF ~ Wyrmslayer (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PaladinACF.PaladinRemoveDisease	PRECLASS:1,Paladin=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Wyrmslayer (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.452	DESC:Alternative class feature (paladin, 1st level). Wyrmslayer paladins dedicate their lives to learning about dragons and how to combat them: Knowledge (arcana) replaces Knowledge (nobility and royalty) as a class skill (the removal is not enforced); instead of remove disease she casts resist energy 1/day from 6th level at her paladin level, gaining an additional daily use whenever she would gain a use of remove disease (9th, 12th, 15th, 18th). She may multiclass freely as a ranger, provided she selects dragons as her first favored enemy. Replaces remove disease.
Wyrmslayer	KEY:ACF ~ Wyrmslayer (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Paladin Class Feature	CSKILL:Knowledge (Arcana)	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=floor((PaladinLVL-3)/3)|CASTERLEVEL=PaladinLVL|Resist Energy|PREVARGTEQ:PaladinLVL,6	SOURCEPAGE:p.452	DESC:Wyrmslayer paladins dedicate their lives to learning about dragons and how to combat them: Knowledge (arcana) replaces Knowledge (nobility and royalty) as a class skill (the removal is not enforced); instead of remove disease she casts resist energy 1/day from 6th level at her paladin level, gaining an additional daily use whenever she would gain a use of remove disease (9th, 12th, 15th, 18th). She may multiclass freely as a ranger, provided she selects dragons as her first favored enemy. Replaces remove disease.

###Block: Druid alternative class features
Animal Companions	KEY:Druid ACF ~ Animal Companions (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.DruidACF.DruidCompanionList	PRECLASS:1,Druid=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Druid Animal Companions (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.216	DESC:Alternative class feature (druid, 1st level). The compendium's compilation of all animals eligible as animal companions, by minimum druid level (apply the adjustment to the druid's level for the companion's characteristics and abilities): 1st - baazrag, badger, bat, camel, caribou, climbdog, dogs, donkey, eagle, elk, hawk, horses, hyena, jackal, owl, pony, dire rat, raven, vipers, wolf and others; 4th (-3) - ape, dire badger, dire bat, black bear, bison, boar, cheetah, leopard, monitor lizard, constrictor, Large viper, dire weasel, wolverine and others; 7th (-6) - dire ape, brown bear, dire boar, giant crocodile, deinonychus, lion, rhinoceros, tiger, dire wolf, dire wolverine and others; 10th (-9) - polar bear, hippopotamus, dire lion, megaraptor, giant constrictor, saber-toothed tiger and others; 13th (-12) - dire bear, elephant, giant banded lizard, giant octopus; 16th (-15) - dire elephant, woolly mammoth, mastodon, dire rhinoceros, roc, dire tiger, triceratops, tyrannosaurus and others; 19th (-18) - horrid elephant/rhinoceros/tiger, mosasaur, plesiosaur; 21st (-20) - diplodocus, giganotosaurus; 24th (-23) - liopleurodon. Aquatic animals (barracuda, eels, porpoise, seals, sharks, squid, whales ...) only in an aquatic environment, some only underground, and brixashulty/hawk variants only for halfling or raptoran druids. (Offered here: the creatures in the core data; it replaces nothing.)
Animal Companions	KEY:ACF ~ Druid Animal Companions (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Druid Class Feature	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Badger,Companion ~ Bat,Companion ~ Camel,Companion ~ Dog,Companion ~ Dog (Riding),Donkey,Companion ~ Eagle,Companion ~ Hawk,Companion ~ Horse (Light),Companion ~ Horse (Heavy),Hyena,Companion ~ Owl,Companion ~ Pony,Companion ~ Porpoise,Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Rat),Companion ~ Raven,Companion ~ Shark (Medium),Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Tiny),Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Small),Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Medium),Companion ~ Squid,Companion ~ Wolf	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Ape,Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Badger),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Bat),Companion ~ Bear (Black),Companion ~ Bison,Companion ~ Boar,Companion ~ Cheetah,Companion ~ Leopard,Companion ~ Lizard (Monitor),Companion ~ Shark (Large),Companion ~ Snake (Constrictor),Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Large),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Weasel),Companion ~ Wolverine|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-3	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Ape),Companion ~ Bear (Brown),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Boar),Companion ~ Crocodile (Giant),Companion ~ Dinosaur (Deinonychus),Companion ~ Dinosaur (Elasmosaurus),Companion ~ Lion,Companion ~ Rhinoceros,Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Huge),Companion ~ Tiger,Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Wolf),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Wolverine)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-6	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Bear (Polar),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Lion),Companion ~ Dinosaur (Megaraptor),Companion ~ Shark (Huge),Companion ~ Snake (Constrictor/Giant),Companion ~ Whale (Orca)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-9	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Bear),Companion ~ Elephant,Companion ~ Octopus (Giant)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-12	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Roc,Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Shark),Companion ~ Squid (Giant),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Tiger),Companion ~ Dinosaur (Triceratops),Companion ~ Dinosaur (Tyrannosaurus)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-15	SOURCEPAGE:p.216	DESC:The compendium's compilation of all animals eligible as animal companions, by minimum druid level (apply the adjustment to the druid's level for the companion's characteristics and abilities): 1st - baazrag, badger, bat, camel, caribou, climbdog, dogs, donkey, eagle, elk, hawk, horses, hyena, jackal, owl, pony, dire rat, raven, vipers, wolf and others; 4th (-3) - ape, dire badger, dire bat, black bear, bison, boar, cheetah, leopard, monitor lizard, constrictor, Large viper, dire weasel, wolverine and others; 7th (-6) - dire ape, brown bear, dire boar, giant crocodile, deinonychus, lion, rhinoceros, tiger, dire wolf, dire wolverine and others; 10th (-9) - polar bear, hippopotamus, dire lion, megaraptor, giant constrictor, saber-toothed tiger and others; 13th (-12) - dire bear, elephant, giant banded lizard, giant octopus; 16th (-15) - dire elephant, woolly mammoth, mastodon, dire rhinoceros, roc, dire tiger, triceratops, tyrannosaurus and others; 19th (-18) - horrid elephant/rhinoceros/tiger, mosasaur, plesiosaur; 21st (-20) - diplodocus, giganotosaurus; 24th (-23) - liopleurodon. Aquatic animals (barracuda, eels, porpoise, seals, sharks, squid, whales ...) only in an aquatic environment, some only underground, and brixashulty/hawk variants only for halfling or raptoran druids. (Offered here: the creatures in the core data; it replaces nothing.)
Aquatic Druid	KEY:Druid ACF ~ Aquatic Druid (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.DruidACF.DruidWoodlandStride	PRECLASS:1,Druid=2	PREMOVE:1,Swim=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Aquatic Druid (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.218	DESC:Alternative class feature (druid, 2nd level). Druids of the waters tend sacred pools and streams, coral reefs, kelp forests and deep places of mystery. A druid with a racial swim speed can apply woodland stride to difficult aquatic terrain (shallow coral, kelp beds, ice-choked waters, sargasso and similar obstacles) rather than woodland terrain, chosen when the class feature is gained: she moves through it at normal speed without damage or impairment (magically manipulated terrain still affects her). Replaces woodland stride.
Aquatic Druid	KEY:ACF ~ Aquatic Druid (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Druid Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.218	DESC:Druids of the waters tend sacred pools and streams, coral reefs, kelp forests and deep places of mystery. A druid with a racial swim speed can apply woodland stride to difficult aquatic terrain (shallow coral, kelp beds, ice-choked waters, sargasso and similar obstacles) rather than woodland terrain, chosen when the class feature is gained: she moves through it at normal speed without damage or impairment (magically manipulated terrain still affects her). Replaces woodland stride.
Aspect of Nature	KEY:Druid ACF ~ Aspect of Nature (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.DruidACF.DruidWildShape	PRECLASS:1,Druid=5	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Aspect of Nature (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.219	DESC:Alternative class feature (druid, 5th level). Instead of taking animal form, she takes on aspects of nature: each aspect costs one daily use of wild shape (%1 uses per day now - as many as her wild shape would give), up to %2 simultaneously (1 at 5th level, 2 at 8th, 3 at 11th, 4 at 15th; multiple versions of one aspect don't stack); a standard action without attacks of opportunity, lasting 1 minute per druid level (%3 minutes). Unless noted she keeps her type, abilities, speech and spellcasting, and is proficient with granted natural attacks. Aspects: agility (+8 Dex, -4 Str; 8th); aquatic (gills, swim 40 ft. or 30 in medium/heavy armor or load, +8 Swim); elemental air (gaseous, fly 100 ft. perfect, immune to poison, sleep, paralysis, stunning; no spellcasting; only with agility or endurance; 16th); elemental earth (stony, same immunities, slam as a morningstar of her size, natural armor +8, DR 10/magic; no spellcasting; only with endurance or vigor; 16th); elemental fire (immune to fire and the same, +1d6 fire and catching fire on melee hits and to those striking her, Reflex DC %4, DR 10/magic; no spellcasting; only with agility or endurance; 16th); elemental water (semifluid, +10 Escape Artist, fire resistance 10, same immunities, swim 90 ft., +8 Swim, puts out open flames, dispels magical fire as greater dispel magic, DR 10/magic; no spellcasting; only with endurance or vigor; 16th); endurance (+4 Con; 8th); flight (wings, fly 40 ft. average, 30 in medium/heavy armor or load); plant (+10 Hide in vegetation, immune to poison, sleep, paralysis, stunning, slam as a light mace of her size, natural armor 4; only with vigor; 12th); poison (bite as a dagger of her size with venom, Fortitude DC %4, 1d6 Con initial and secondary); scent; speed (+30 ft. enhancement to land speed); tooth and claw (primary bite as a short sword, two secondary claws as daggers of her size); vigor (+8 Str, -4 Dex; 8th). Replaces wild shape (including the elemental forms).
Aspect of Nature	KEY:ACF ~ Aspect of Nature (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Druid Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.219	DESC:Instead of taking animal form, she takes on aspects of nature: each aspect costs one daily use of wild shape (%1 uses per day now - as many as her wild shape would give), up to %2 simultaneously (1 at 5th level, 2 at 8th, 3 at 11th, 4 at 15th; multiple versions of one aspect don't stack); a standard action without attacks of opportunity, lasting 1 minute per druid level (%3 minutes). Unless noted she keeps her type, abilities, speech and spellcasting, and is proficient with granted natural attacks. Aspects: agility (+8 Dex, -4 Str; 8th); aquatic (gills, swim 40 ft. or 30 in medium/heavy armor or load, +8 Swim); elemental air (gaseous, fly 100 ft. perfect, immune to poison, sleep, paralysis, stunning; no spellcasting; only with agility or endurance; 16th); elemental earth (stony, same immunities, slam as a morningstar of her size, natural armor +8, DR 10/magic; no spellcasting; only with endurance or vigor; 16th); elemental fire (immune to fire and the same, +1d6 fire and catching fire on melee hits and to those striking her, Reflex DC %4, DR 10/magic; no spellcasting; only with agility or endurance; 16th); elemental water (semifluid, +10 Escape Artist, fire resistance 10, same immunities, swim 90 ft., +8 Swim, puts out open flames, dispels magical fire as greater dispel magic, DR 10/magic; no spellcasting; only with endurance or vigor; 16th); endurance (+4 Con; 8th); flight (wings, fly 40 ft. average, 30 in medium/heavy armor or load); plant (+10 Hide in vegetation, immune to poison, sleep, paralysis, stunning, slam as a light mace of her size, natural armor 4; only with vigor; 12th); poison (bite as a dagger of her size with venom, Fortitude DC %4, 1d6 Con initial and secondary); scent; speed (+30 ft. enhancement to land speed); tooth and claw (primary bite as a short sword, two secondary claws as daggers of her size); vigor (+8 Str, -4 Dex; 8th). Replaces wild shape (including the elemental forms).|(DruidLVL>=5)+(DruidLVL>=6)+(DruidLVL>=7)+(DruidLVL>=10)+(DruidLVL>=14)+(DruidLVL>=18)|(DruidLVL>=5)+(DruidLVL>=8)+(DruidLVL>=11)+(DruidLVL>=15)|DruidLVL|10+floor(DruidLVL/2)+CON
Dead Levels	KEY:Druid ACF ~ Dead Levels (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.DruidACF.DruidDeadLevels	PRECLASS:1,Druid=17	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Druid Dead Levels (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.221	DESC:Alternative class feature (druid, 17th level). Optional abilities filling the druid's dead levels (it replaces nothing). Woodland Sprint (Ex), 17th level: she moves at normal speed through thorns, briars and overgrown areas that have been magically manipulated, without damage or impairment - she becomes immune to such magical effects. Repel Nature's Lure (Ex), 19th level: spell resistance %1 (druid level + 10) against the spell-like abilities of fey (dryads, pixies, sprites ...).
Dead Levels	KEY:ACF ~ Druid Dead Levels (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Druid Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.221	DESC:Optional abilities filling the druid's dead levels (it replaces nothing). Woodland Sprint (Ex), 17th level: she moves at normal speed through thorns, briars and overgrown areas that have been magically manipulated, without damage or impairment - she becomes immune to such magical effects. Repel Nature's Lure (Ex), 19th level: spell resistance %1 (druid level + 10) against the spell-like abilities of fey (dryads, pixies, sprites ...).|DruidLVL+10
Domain Druid	KEY:Druid ACF ~ Domain Druid (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.DruidACF.DruidDomainDruid	PRECLASS:1,Druid=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Domain Druid (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.222	DESC:Alternative class feature (druid, 1st level). The druid chooses a single domain: Air, Animal, Earth, Fire, Plant, Sun or Water (Domains tab). She gains a bonus spell of each spell level, usable only to prepare a domain spell of that level (or lower with metamagic), and the domain's granted power, except: Animal or Plant gives Skill Focus (Knowledge (nature)) instead (Knowledge (nature) is already a druid class skill); Sun gives turn undead once per day as a cleric of her level, without greater turning. Replaces nothing.
Domain Druid	KEY:ACF ~ Domain Druid (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Druid Class Feature	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Skill Focus(Knowledge (Nature))|PREDOMAIN:1,Animal,Plant	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Basic Turning|Turn Undead|PREDOMAIN:1,Sun	BONUS:VAR|TurnLevelBase,TurnDamagePlusBase|DruidLVL|PREDOMAIN:1,Sun	BONUS:VAR|TurnTimesBase|1|PREDOMAIN:1,Sun	BONUS:VAR|TurnCheckBase|CHA|TYPE=Base|PREDOMAIN:1,Sun	SOURCEPAGE:p.222	DESC:The druid chooses a single domain: Air, Animal, Earth, Fire, Plant, Sun or Water (Domains tab). She gains a bonus spell of each spell level, usable only to prepare a domain spell of that level (or lower with metamagic), and the domain's granted power, except: Animal or Plant gives Skill Focus (Knowledge (nature)) instead (Knowledge (nature) is already a druid class skill); Sun gives turn undead once per day as a cleric of her level, without greater turning. Replaces nothing.
Focused Animal	KEY:Druid ACF ~ Focused Animal (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.DruidACF.DruidTracklessStep.DruidWildShape.DruidWoodlandStride	PRECLASS:1,Druid=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Focused Animal (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.225	DESC:Alternative class feature (druid, 1st level). A druid who no longer reveres the entirety of nature learns to communicate with his closest ally: continuous speak with animals, usable only with his animal companion; for its bonus Hit Dice, natural armor, Strength and Dexterity adjustment, bonus tricks and special abilities he counts as a druid two levels higher - this does not allow a more powerful alternative companion earlier. Replaces trackless step, wild shape and woodland stride.
Focused Animal	KEY:ACF ~ Focused Animal (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Druid Class Feature	BONUS:VAR|AnimalCompanionLVL|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.225	DESC:A druid who no longer reveres the entirety of nature learns to communicate with his closest ally: continuous speak with animals, usable only with his animal companion; for its bonus Hit Dice, natural armor, Strength and Dexterity adjustment, bonus tricks and special abilities he counts as a druid two levels higher - this does not allow a more powerful alternative companion earlier. Replaces trackless step, wild shape and woodland stride.
Golarion Druid	KEY:Druid ACF ~ Golarion Druid (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.DruidACF.DruidWoodlandStride	PRECLASS:1,Druid=2	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Golarion Druid (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.226	DESC:Alternative class feature (druid, 2nd level). Mountain Stride (Ex): druids who took to the mountains during the Age of Enthronement move through rocky terrain at normal speed without damage or impairment; magically manipulated terrain (such as spike stones) affects them normally. Replaces woodland stride.
Golarion Druid	KEY:ACF ~ Golarion Druid (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Druid Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.226	DESC:Mountain Stride (Ex): druids who took to the mountains during the Age of Enthronement move through rocky terrain at normal speed without damage or impairment; magically manipulated terrain (such as spike stones) affects them normally. Replaces woodland stride.
Plant Companion	KEY:Druid ACF ~ Plant Companion (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.DruidACF.DruidAnimalCompanion	PRECLASS:1,Druid=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Plant Companion (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.232	DESC:Alternative class feature (druid, 1st level). Instead of an animal, she rouses a plant companion (the base plant companion: Medium plant, 1 HD, slam 1d4, plant traits) that improves as an animal companion of her level (bonus HD, natural armor and so on); Handle Animal works on it without the -5 penalty. Natural selection: instead of choosing more powerful companions she evolves this one in a 24-hour ritual, selecting a new ability at any level in which a previous one does not manifest; each manifests after a delay: alacrity (bonus melee attack in a full attack; after 2 levels), bioluminescent (torchlight at will; 1), blindsight 30 ft. (2), blunting mold (slashing/piercing weapons that hit it deal half damage until cleaned; 3), bonus feat (1), cactus spurs (1), darkvision (1), distracting pollen (2), eldritch fibers (1), growth spurt (3), ironbark* (2), mirrored bark* (2), oakenbough* (2), poisonous (3), powerful* (1), roots (3), scent (1), spines (1), sticky sap (5), swift* (+10 ft. speed; 2), tendrils (reach doubles; 2), thorns* (+1 damage, piercing; 1), tremorsense 60 ft. (1) - * may be taken repeatedly, stacking. Replaces the animal companion (only the plant companion is offered).
Plant Companion	KEY:ACF ~ Plant Companion (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Druid Class Feature	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Animal Companion	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|DMC ~ Animal Companion Alternate	BONUS:VAR|AnimalCompanionLVL|DruidLVL	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Plant Companion (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.232	DESC:Instead of an animal, she rouses a plant companion (the base plant companion: Medium plant, 1 HD, slam 1d4, plant traits) that improves as an animal companion of her level (bonus HD, natural armor and so on); Handle Animal works on it without the -5 penalty. Natural selection: instead of choosing more powerful companions she evolves this one in a 24-hour ritual, selecting a new ability at any level in which a previous one does not manifest; each manifests after a delay: alacrity (bonus melee attack in a full attack; after 2 levels), bioluminescent (torchlight at will; 1), blindsight 30 ft. (2), blunting mold (slashing/piercing weapons that hit it deal half damage until cleaned; 3), bonus feat (1), cactus spurs (1), darkvision (1), distracting pollen (2), eldritch fibers (1), growth spurt (3), ironbark* (2), mirrored bark* (2), oakenbough* (2), poisonous (3), powerful* (1), roots (3), scent (1), spines (1), sticky sap (5), swift* (+10 ft. speed; 2), tendrils (reach doubles; 2), thorns* (+1 damage, piercing; 1), tremorsense 60 ft. (1) - * may be taken repeatedly, stacking. Replaces the animal companion (only the plant companion is offered).
Shapeshift	KEY:Druid ACF ~ Shapeshift (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.DruidACF.DruidAnimalCompanion.DruidWildShape	PRECLASS:1,Druid=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Shapeshift (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.234	DESC:Alternative class feature (druid, 1st level). At will, as a swift action, she shapeshifts into powerful nature-oriented forms (look chosen each time, from her home terrain), switching directly between forms, without limit of uses or duration (supernatural). She keeps her HD, hit points, base attack, base saves, skill ranks, ability scores (plus each form's Strength bonus), type and size unless noted, and her extraordinary, supernatural and spell-like abilities; gear melds; she cannot speak, wield weapons, cast spells or activate items (even with Natural Spell). Her forms' natural weapons have a +%1 enhancement bonus (1/4 druid level) and count as magic from 4th level; damage for Medium (adjust by size). Forms: predator (1st: bite 1d6, +4 Str, natural armor +4, land speed 50 ft.; Mobility from 4th); aerial (5th: talon 1d6, +2 Str, +2 Reflex, natural armor +2, fly 40 ft. good; Flyby Attack from 7th); ferocious slayer (8th: one size larger, bite 1d8 and two claws 1d6, +8 Str, +4 Fort, natural armor +8, land speed 40 ft.; Improved Critical (bite, claw) from 10th); forest avenger (12th: one size larger, two slams 1d8, tall reach, +12 Str, +4 Fort and Will, natural armor +12, land speed 20 ft., DR 5/slashing; Improved Overrun from 14th); elemental fury (16th: two sizes larger, two slams 2d6, +16 Str, +4 on all saves, natural armor +16, immune to critical hits and to the element's energy, no breathing; Great Cleave from 18th). She reverts if knocked unconscious or slain. Replaces the animal companion and wild shape with all its later variations (Player's Handbook II; its repository entry is an unfinished stub).
Shapeshift	KEY:ACF ~ Shapeshift (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Druid Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.234	DESC:At will, as a swift action, she shapeshifts into powerful nature-oriented forms (look chosen each time, from her home terrain), switching directly between forms, without limit of uses or duration (supernatural). She keeps her HD, hit points, base attack, base saves, skill ranks, ability scores (plus each form's Strength bonus), type and size unless noted, and her extraordinary, supernatural and spell-like abilities; gear melds; she cannot speak, wield weapons, cast spells or activate items (even with Natural Spell). Her forms' natural weapons have a +%1 enhancement bonus (1/4 druid level) and count as magic from 4th level; damage for Medium (adjust by size). Forms: predator (1st: bite 1d6, +4 Str, natural armor +4, land speed 50 ft.; Mobility from 4th); aerial (5th: talon 1d6, +2 Str, +2 Reflex, natural armor +2, fly 40 ft. good; Flyby Attack from 7th); ferocious slayer (8th: one size larger, bite 1d8 and two claws 1d6, +8 Str, +4 Fort, natural armor +8, land speed 40 ft.; Improved Critical (bite, claw) from 10th); forest avenger (12th: one size larger, two slams 1d8, tall reach, +12 Str, +4 Fort and Will, natural armor +12, land speed 20 ft., DR 5/slashing; Improved Overrun from 14th); elemental fury (16th: two sizes larger, two slams 2d6, +16 Str, +4 on all saves, natural armor +16, immune to critical hits and to the element's energy, no breathing; Great Cleave from 18th). She reverts if knocked unconscious or slain. Replaces the animal companion and wild shape with all its later variations (Player's Handbook II; its repository entry is an unfinished stub).|floor(DruidLVL/4)
Spontaneous Affliction	KEY:Druid ACF ~ Spontaneous Affliction (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.DruidACF.DruidSpontaneousCasting	PRECLASS:1,Druid=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Spontaneous Affliction (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.239	DESC:Alternative class feature (druid, 1st level). She calls on nature's smallest beings to punish despoilers: as a standard action she sacrifices a prepared spell, and all humanoids within 30 feet must succeed on a Fortitude save (DC %1 = 10 + half her druid level + Charisma modifier) or be sickened for rounds equal to the spell's level. Replaces spontaneous summon nature's ally.
Spontaneous Affliction	KEY:ACF ~ Spontaneous Affliction (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Druid Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.239	DESC:She calls on nature's smallest beings to punish despoilers: as a standard action she sacrifices a prepared spell, and all humanoids within 30 feet must succeed on a Fortitude save (DC %1 = 10 + half her druid level + Charisma modifier) or be sickened for rounds equal to the spell's level. Replaces spontaneous summon nature's ally.|10+floor(DruidLVL/2)+CHA
Weapon Proficiencies	KEY:Druid ACF ~ Weapon Proficiencies (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.DruidACF.DruidProficiencies	PRECLASS:1,Druid=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Druid Weapon Proficiencies (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.244	DESC:Alternative class feature (druid, 1st level). A druid from a desert, the arctic, a coast or another region uses a regional weapon list instead of the druid's usual weapons (chosen in the category below); she keeps the druid's armor and shield proficiencies (still bound by the druid's restriction on metal armor). Replaces the druid's weapon proficiencies.
Weapon Proficiencies	KEY:ACF ~ Druid Weapon Proficiencies (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Druid Class Feature	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=ArmorProfMedium|TYPE=ShieldProf	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|TYPE=Auto	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Druid ACF Weapon Proficiencies|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.244	DESC:A druid from a desert, the arctic, a coast or another region uses a regional weapon list instead of the druid's usual weapons (chosen in the category below); she keeps the druid's armor and shield proficiencies (still bound by the druid's restriction on metal armor). Replaces the druid's weapon proficiencies.
Weapon Proficiencies (Aquatic or Coastal)	KEY:ACF ~ Druid Weapon Proficiencies (DMC) ~ Aquatic or Coastal	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DruidACFWeaponProficiencies.SpecialQuality	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Club|Dagger|Dart|Longspear|Net|Quarterstaff|Sling|Spear|Shortspear|Trident	SOURCEPAGE:p.244	DESC:Aquatic/Coastal druids are proficient with club, dagger, dart, longspear, net, quarterstaff, sling, spear, shortspear, trident (piercing weapons for spearing fish, easier to wield underwater).
Weapon Proficiencies (Arctic or Tundra)	KEY:ACF ~ Druid Weapon Proficiencies (DMC) ~ Arctic or Tundra	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DruidACFWeaponProficiencies.SpecialQuality	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Club|Dagger|Handaxe|Pick (Light)|Morningstar|Quarterstaff|Scythe|Sickle|Sling|Spear|Axe (Throwing)	SOURCEPAGE:p.244	DESC:Arctic/Tundra druids are proficient with club, dagger, handaxe, pick (light), morningstar, quarterstaff, scythe, sickle, sling, spear, axe (throwing) (weapons mimicking the deadly land or easily crafted there (ice picks for climbing)).
Weapon Proficiencies (Desert or Wasteland)	KEY:ACF ~ Druid Weapon Proficiencies (DMC) ~ Desert or Wasteland	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DruidACFWeaponProficiencies.SpecialQuality	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Falchion|Javelin|Kukri|Scimitar|Shortspear|Sling|Spear|Whip	SOURCEPAGE:p.244	DESC:Desert/Wasteland druids are proficient with falchion, javelin, kukri, scimitar, shortspear, sling, spear, whip (wood is scarce: no club or quarterstaff, several more exotic weapons).
Weapon Proficiencies (Grassland or Savannah)	KEY:ACF ~ Druid Weapon Proficiencies (DMC) ~ Grassland or Savannah	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DruidACFWeaponProficiencies.SpecialQuality	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Bolas|Javelin|Longspear|Scythe|Shortbow|Shortspear|Sickle|Sling|Spear	SOURCEPAGE:p.244	DESC:Grassland/Savannah druids are proficient with bolas, javelin, longspear, scythe, shortbow, shortspear, sickle, sling, spear (more ranged weapons for vast open spaces).
Weapon Proficiencies (Mountain)	KEY:ACF ~ Druid Weapon Proficiencies (DMC) ~ Mountain	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DruidACFWeaponProficiencies.SpecialQuality	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Battleaxe|Club|Dagger|Handaxe|Pick (Heavy)|Pick (Light)|Quarterstaff|Sling|Warhammer	SOURCEPAGE:p.244	DESC:Mountain druids are proficient with battleaxe, club, dagger, handaxe, pick (heavy), pick (light), quarterstaff, sling, warhammer (a more warlike array, some doubling as mining tools (many dwarven druids)).
Weapon Proficiencies (Subterranean or Underdark)	KEY:ACF ~ Druid Weapon Proficiencies (DMC) ~ Subterranean or Underdark	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DruidACFWeaponProficiencies.SpecialQuality	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Club|Dagger|Pick (Heavy)|Pick (Light)|Shortspear|Sword (Short)|Sling|Whip	SOURCEPAGE:p.244	DESC:Subterranean/Underdark druids are proficient with club, dagger, pick (heavy), pick (light), shortspear, sword (short), sling, whip (weapons for tight, confining quarters).
Wasteland Druid	KEY:Druid ACF ~ Wasteland Druid (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.DruidACF.DruidWoodlandStride.DruidResistNaturesLure	PRECLASS:1,Druid=2	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Wasteland Druid (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.244	DESC:Alternative class feature (druid, 2nd level). A druid of the waste (Sandstorm's variant), choosing her animal companion from Sandstorm's Wasteland Animal Companions sidebar (not in the compendium): Sandskimmer as a bonus feat at 2nd level instead of woodland stride; Heat Endurance as a bonus feat at 4th level (Improved Heat Endurance if she already has it, without its prerequisites) instead of resist nature's lure - both are Sandstorm feats, not in the repository's Sandstorm data, so add them by hand; from 10th level she can wild shape into Small to Large waste vermin (brine swimmer, giant ant lion, giant termite, monstrous scorpion, monstrous spider; larger sizes as her level increases), replacing the fourth daily use of wild shape gained at 10th level - from then on one fewer daily use (by hand). Replaces woodland stride and resist nature's lure.
Wasteland Druid	KEY:ACF ~ Wasteland Druid (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Druid Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.244	DESC:A druid of the waste (Sandstorm's variant), choosing her animal companion from Sandstorm's Wasteland Animal Companions sidebar (not in the compendium): Sandskimmer as a bonus feat at 2nd level instead of woodland stride; Heat Endurance as a bonus feat at 4th level (Improved Heat Endurance if she already has it, without its prerequisites) instead of resist nature's lure - both are Sandstorm feats, not in the repository's Sandstorm data, so add them by hand; from 10th level she can wild shape into Small to Large waste vermin (brine swimmer, giant ant lion, giant termite, monstrous scorpion, monstrous spider; larger sizes as her level increases), replacing the fourth daily use of wild shape gained at 10th level - from then on one fewer daily use (by hand). Replaces woodland stride and resist nature's lure.

###Block: Cleric alternative class features
Blasphemous Incantation	KEY:Cleric ACF ~ Blasphemous Incantation (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.ClericACF.ClericTurnUndead	PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1	PREALIGN:LE,NE,CE	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Blasphemous Incantation (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.154	DESC:Alternative class feature (cleric, 1st level). You call on your evil master to smite your enemies: all good creatures within 30 feet must succeed on a Fortitude save (DC %1 = 10 + half your caster level + Charisma modifier; +2 with 5 or more ranks in Knowledge (religion)) or be sickened for rounds equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum 1); %2 times per day (3 + Charisma modifier). Supernatural. Evil only: you lose access if your alignment changes. Replaces rebuke undead.
Blasphemous Incantation	KEY:ACF ~ Blasphemous Incantation (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Cleric Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.154	DESC:You call on your evil master to smite your enemies: all good creatures within 30 feet must succeed on a Fortitude save (DC %1 = 10 + half your caster level + Charisma modifier; +2 with 5 or more ranks in Knowledge (religion)) or be sickened for rounds equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum 1); %2 times per day (3 + Charisma modifier). Supernatural. Evil only: you lose access if your alignment changes. Replaces rebuke undead.|10+floor(ClericLVL/2)+CHA|3+CHA
Champion	KEY:Cleric ACF ~ Champion (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.ClericACF.ClericTurnUndead	PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Champion (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.154	DESC:Alternative class feature (cleric, 1st level). A champion of good (or evil) standing at the forefront of battle: smite evil, if you would normally channel positive energy, or smite good, if you would channel negative energy (as the paladin, by cleric level: 1/day, +1 per five levels; Charisma on the attack, +1 damage per level - smite good described here for evil clerics), and from 3rd level aura of courage (as the paladin: immune to fear, allies within 10 feet +4 on saves against fear). Replaces turn undead.
Champion	KEY:ACF ~ Champion (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Cleric Class Feature	ABILITY:Paladin Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Paladin ~ Smite Evil|!PREALIGN:LE,NE,CE	BONUS:VAR|PaladinSmiteEvilLVL|ClericLVL	ABILITY:Paladin Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Paladin ~ Aura of Courage|PREVARGTEQ:ClericLVL,3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Immunity to Fear|PREVARGTEQ:ClericLVL,3	SOURCEPAGE:p.154	DESC:A champion of good (or evil) standing at the forefront of battle: smite evil, if you would normally channel positive energy, or smite good, if you would channel negative energy (as the paladin, by cleric level: 1/day, +1 per five levels; Charisma on the attack, +1 damage per level - smite good described here for evil clerics), and from 3rd level aura of courage (as the paladin: immune to fear, allies within 10 feet +4 on saves against fear). Replaces turn undead.
Dead Levels	KEY:Cleric ACF ~ Dead Levels (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.ClericACF.ClericDeadLevels	PRECLASS:1,Cleric=2	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Cleric Dead Levels (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.156	DESC:Alternative class feature (cleric, 2nd level). Undead Intuition (Ex): from 2nd level she can identify undead creatures during an encounter from any distance, with a +%1 bonus on Knowledge (religion) checks to identify them (+2 at 2nd level, +1 per cleric level after 2nd), untrained; it gives no insight into their powers or vulnerabilities. Optional dead level ability; replaces nothing.
Dead Levels	KEY:ACF ~ Cleric Dead Levels (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Cleric Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.156	DESC:Undead Intuition (Ex): from 2nd level she can identify undead creatures during an encounter from any distance, with a +%1 bonus on Knowledge (religion) checks to identify them (+2 at 2nd level, +1 per cleric level after 2nd), untrained; it gives no insight into their powers or vulnerabilities. Optional dead level ability; replaces nothing.|ClericLVL
Destroy Undead	KEY:Cleric ACF ~ Destroy Undead (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.ClericACF.ClericTurnUndead	PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Destroy Undead (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.157	DESC:Alternative class feature (cleric, 1st level). Lightbringer cleric: instead of turning or rebuking, as a standard action she channels positive energy dealing %1d6 points of damage (1d6 per cleric level) to all undead within 30 feet, Will DC %2 (10 + cleric level + Charisma modifier) for half; undead subtract their turn resistance from the damage. (Uses per day as her turn attempts would be: %3.) Replaces turn undead.
Destroy Undead	KEY:ACF ~ Destroy Undead (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Cleric Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.157	DESC:Lightbringer cleric: instead of turning or rebuking, as a standard action she channels positive energy dealing %1d6 points of damage (1d6 per cleric level) to all undead within 30 feet, Will DC %2 (10 + cleric level + Charisma modifier) for half; undead subtract their turn resistance from the damage. (Uses per day as her turn attempts would be: %3.) Replaces turn undead.|ClericLVL|10+ClericLVL+CHA|3+CHA
Domain Focus	KEY:Cleric ACF ~ Domain Focus (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.ClericACF.ClericSpontaneousCasting	PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Domain Focus (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.158	DESC:Alternative class feature (cleric, 1st level). A cleric who sees only the pure version of his deity focuses on a single aspect: he loses one of his domains (and its spells from all his spell lists - he chooses only one domain) and gains double the benefit of the remaining domain's granted power: twice the uses per day (not counting ability-based extra uses), or a doubled bonus, or for powers with both, one of the two (apply by hand). Replaces spontaneous cure/inflict casting and one domain.
Domain Focus	KEY:ACF ~ Domain Focus (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Cleric Class Feature	BONUS:VAR|DomainCount|-1	SOURCEPAGE:p.158	DESC:A cleric who sees only the pure version of his deity focuses on a single aspect: he loses one of his domains (and its spells from all his spell lists - he chooses only one domain) and gains double the benefit of the remaining domain's granted power: twice the uses per day (not counting ability-based extra uses), or a doubled bonus, or for powers with both, one of the two (apply by hand). Replaces spontaneous cure/inflict casting and one domain.
Golarion Cleric	KEY:Cleric ACF ~ Golarion Cleric (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.ClericACF.ClericGolarion	PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Golarion Cleric (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.163	DESC:Alternative class feature (cleric, 1st level). Holy Warrior (Ex): a cleric who sees herself as a holy warrior gives up both her domains, with their powers and spells: she is proficient with her deity's favored weapon, her base attack bonus as a cleric equals her cleric level, and her cleric Hit Die becomes a d10 (hit points by hand). Replaces both domains.
Golarion Cleric	KEY:ACF ~ Golarion Cleric (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Cleric Class Feature	BONUS:VAR|DomainCount|-2	BONUS:COMBAT|BASEAB|ClericLVL-floor(ClericLVL*3/4)	SOURCEPAGE:p.163	DESC:Holy Warrior (Ex): a cleric who sees herself as a holy warrior gives up both her domains, with their powers and spells: she is proficient with her deity's favored weapon, her base attack bonus as a cleric equals her cleric level, and her cleric Hit Die becomes a d10 (hit points by hand). Replaces both domains.
Improved Domain Power (instead of turning)	KEY:Cleric ACF ~ Improved Domain Power (instead of turning) (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.ClericACF.ClericTurnUndead	PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Cleric Improved Domain Power (instead of turning) (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.163	DESC:Alternative class feature (cleric, 1st level). Instead of turning or rebuking undead, the cleric gains one of the improved granted powers of her chosen domains (Improved Domain Power category); she keeps both standard granted powers and chooses domain spells normally. Chosen at 1st cleric level; turning from other classes is unaffected. Replaces turn or rebuke undead.
Improved Domain Power (instead of turning)	KEY:ACF ~ Cleric Improved Domain Power (instead of turning) (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Cleric Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Improved Domain Power|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.163	DESC:Instead of turning or rebuking undead, the cleric gains one of the improved granted powers of her chosen domains (Improved Domain Power category); she keeps both standard granted powers and chooses domain spells normally. Chosen at 1st cleric level; turning from other classes is unaffected. Replaces turn or rebuke undead.
One Power	KEY:Cleric ACF ~ One Power (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.ClericACF.ClericOnePower	PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ One Power (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.163	DESC:Alternative class feature (cleric, 1st level). Instead of gaining two standard granted domain powers, the cleric chooses one domain and gains its improved granted power (Improved Domain Power category) in place of both standard powers (remove the standard powers by hand); she chooses domain spells from both domains normally. Chosen at 1st cleric level.
One Power	KEY:ACF ~ One Power (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Cleric Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Improved Domain Power|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.163	DESC:Instead of gaining two standard granted domain powers, the cleric chooses one domain and gains its improved granted power (Improved Domain Power category) in place of both standard powers (remove the standard powers by hand); she chooses domain spells from both domains normally. Chosen at 1st cleric level.

###Block: Paladin alternative class features
Improved Domain Power (instead of turning)	KEY:Paladin ACF ~ Improved Domain Power (instead of turning) (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PaladinACF.PaladinTurnUndead	PRECLASS:1,Paladin=4	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Paladin Improved Domain Power (instead of turning) (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.163	DESC:Alternative class feature (paladin, 4th level). At 4th level, instead of turning undead, the paladin gains one improved granted power of a domain of her deity (of her chosen domains if she has cleric levels), using it as a cleric three levels lower (%1); a paladin with cleric levels cannot gain improved powers by giving up turning in both classes. Replaces turn undead.
Improved Domain Power (instead of turning)	KEY:ACF ~ Paladin Improved Domain Power (instead of turning) (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Paladin Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Improved Domain Power|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.163	DESC:At 4th level, instead of turning undead, the paladin gains one improved granted power of a domain of her deity (of her chosen domains if she has cleric levels), using it as a cleric three levels lower (%1); a paladin with cleric levels cannot gain improved powers by giving up turning in both classes. Replaces turn undead.|PaladinLVL-3

###Block: Cleric alternative class features
No Turning	KEY:Cleric ACF ~ No Turning (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.ClericACF.ClericTurnUndead	PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ No Turning (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.166	DESC:Alternative class feature (cleric, 1st level). Not every cleric learns to turn undead: some focus the divine energy on their own area of expertise and identify themselves by their calling (cultist, evangelist, fanatic, healer, justicar, mystic, relic hunter, sage, scribe, shaman, theologian, wanderer, warrior priest, weaponmaster - chosen in the category below). Replaces turn or rebuke undead.
No Turning	KEY:ACF ~ No Turning (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Cleric Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Cleric ACF No Turning|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.166	DESC:Not every cleric learns to turn undead: some focus the divine energy on their own area of expertise and identify themselves by their calling (cultist, evangelist, fanatic, healer, justicar, mystic, relic hunter, sage, scribe, shaman, theologian, wanderer, warrior priest, weaponmaster - chosen in the category below). Replaces turn or rebuke undead.
No Turning (Cultist)	KEY:ACF ~ No Turning (DMC) ~ Cultist	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClericACFNoTurning.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Bluff|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.166	DESC:You are secretly a worshiper of a dark god, plotting foul intrigues with others of your secretive cult. Level: 1st. Replaces: Turn or rebuke undead. Benefit: You gain a +2 bonus on Bluff checks. As long as you carry your holy symbol, you are immune to magical attempts to uncover falsehoods, such as discern lies, zone of truth, and similar effects.
No Turning (Evangelist)	KEY:ACF ~ No Turning (DMC) ~ Evangelist	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClericACFNoTurning.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Diplomacy|2	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=2|CASTERLEVEL=1|Comprehend Languages	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=1|CASTERLEVEL=7|Tongues|PREVARGTEQ:ClericLVL,7	SOURCEPAGE:p.166	DESC:You travel far and wide, making showy public sermons and seeking converts to your religion. Level: 1st. Replaces: Turn or rebuke undead. Benefit: You gain a +2 bonus on diplomacy checks. An innate talent for magic grants you the following spell-like ability as a 1st-level caster: 2/day - comprehend languages. At 7th level, you gain the following spell-like ability as a 7th-level caster: 1/day - tongues.
No Turning (Fanatic)	KEY:ACF ~ No Turning (DMC) ~ Fanatic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClericACFNoTurning.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Intimidate|2	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=1|CASTERLEVEL=1|True Strike	SOURCEPAGE:p.166	DESC:You are willing to die in the name of your deity, but you're even quicker to kill in his name. Level: 1st. Replaces: Turn or rebuke undead. Benefit: You gain a +2 bonus on Intimidate checks. An innate talent for magic grants you the following spell-like ability as a 1st-level caster: 1/day - true strike.
No Turning (Healer)	KEY:ACF ~ No Turning (DMC) ~ Healer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClericACFNoTurning.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Heal|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.166	DESC:You care most about curing the sick and injured, no matter whom they serve or what the circumstance. Level: 1st. Replaces: Turn or rebuke undead. Benefit: You gain a +2 bonus on Heal checks. Whenever you cast a conjuration (healing) spell on a creature other than yourself, you gain a +2 sacred bonus to Armor Class and a +2 sacred bonus on Concentration checks to cast defensively until the end of your next turn.
No Turning (Justicar)	KEY:ACF ~ No Turning (DMC) ~ Justicar	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClericACFNoTurning.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Sense Motive|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.166	DESC:The cleric of a deity of honor, justice, or truth, you seek to take prisoners alive for interrogation and fair punishment. Level: 1st. Replaces: Turn or rebuke undead. Benefit: You gain a +2 bonus on Sense Motive checks. Whenever you deal enough damage to reduce a creature to negative hit points, the creature automatically and immediately stabilizes.
No Turning (Mystic)	KEY:ACF ~ No Turning (DMC) ~ Mystic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClericACFNoTurning.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.166	DESC:Deities operate beyond the understanding of most men. So do you. Level: 1st. Replaces: Turn or rebuke undead. Benefit: You gain an extra spell one level lower than the highest level spell you can currently cast. This extra spell is always one level lower than the highest-level spell you can cast, so when you gain the ability to cast a higher-level spell the level of the spell slot gained through this ability also increases. (Add the extra slot by hand.)
No Turning (Relic Hunter)	KEY:ACF ~ No Turning (DMC) ~ Relic Hunter	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClericACFNoTurning.SpecialQuality	CSKILL:Knowledge (Dungeoneering)|Search	SOURCEPAGE:p.166	DESC:Your church tasks you to hunt down and reclaim holy - or perhaps unholy - relics. Level: 1st. Replaces: Turn or rebuke undead. Benefit: You gain a bonus on Reflex saves made to avoid traps equal to 1 + your Wisdom modifier (minimum +1). Additionally, Knowledge (dungeoneering) and Search are always considered class skills for you. (The trap save bonus by hand: +%%1.)|max(1,1+WIS)
No Turning (Sage)	KEY:ACF ~ No Turning (DMC) ~ Sage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClericACFNoTurning.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Knowledge (Religion)|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.166	DESC:The keeper of ancient truths and lores, you frequently study the antiquarian writings of your faith. Level: 1st. Replaces: Turn or rebuke undead. Benefit: You gain a +2 bonus on Knowledge (religion) checks. In addition, once per day, you may reroll a Knowledge check. You must take the second roll, even if it isn't as good as the original.
No Turning (Scribe)	KEY:ACF ~ No Turning (DMC) ~ Scribe	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClericACFNoTurning.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Scribe Scroll	SOURCEPAGE:p.166	DESC:After a career of scribing sacred doctrine and composing prayers, writing religious texts is second nature to you. Level: 1st. Replaces: Turn or rebuke undead. Benefit: You gain Scribe Scroll as a bonus feat. In addition, the experience point cost to scribe a scroll is reduced by 25%%, to a minimum of 1 XP.
No Turning (Shaman)	KEY:ACF ~ No Turning (DMC) ~ Shaman	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClericACFNoTurning.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Animal Companion	BONUS:VAR|AnimalCompanionLVL|floor(ClericLVL/2)	SOURCEPAGE:p.166	DESC:You are the wise elder and healer of a of a wilderness-dwelling tribe. Level: 1st. Replaces: Turn or rebuke undead and literacy (you are illiterate). Benefit: You gain an animal companion as a druid of half your cleric level. Half your cleric levels stack with levels of any other classes entitled to an animal companion (such as the druid and ranger) for the purpose of determining your companion's abilities and the alternative lists available to you. (Illiteracy by hand.)
No Turning (Theologian)	KEY:ACF ~ No Turning (DMC) ~ Theologian	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClericACFNoTurning.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Knowledge (Religion)|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.166	DESC:You are a wise and respected philosopher, frequently meditating to comprehend the nature of the divine. Level: 1st. Replaces: Turn or rebuke undead. Benefit: You gain a +2 bonus on Knowledge (religion) checks. As long as you conspicuously wear or carry your deity's holy symbol you gain a +2 bonus on saving throws made to resist divine spells, as well as the spells and spell-like abilities of outsiders.
No Turning (Wanderer)	KEY:ACF ~ No Turning (DMC) ~ Wanderer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClericACFNoTurning.SpecialQuality	CSKILL:Knowledge (Geography)|Knowledge (Local)|Speak Language|Survival	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Endurance	SOURCEPAGE:p.166	DESC:Never staying in one plate for long, you travel the world on an endless religious quest, following the subtle signs and portents your deity leaves you. Level: 1st. Replaces: Turn or rebuke undead. Benefit: Knowledge (geography), Knowledge (local), Speak Language, and Survival are class skills for you. You gain Endurance as a bonus feat at 1st level.
No Turning (Warrior Priest)	KEY:ACF ~ No Turning (DMC) ~ Warrior Priest	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClericACFNoTurning.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.166	DESC:As much a soldier as a member of the clergy, you fight to protect your church, your fellow worshipers, and your ideals. Level: 1st. Replaces: Turn or rebuke undead. Benefit: Once per day, you may cast a quickened version of a spell you have prepared (that wasn't prepared as a quickened spell) targeting your weapon, shield, or armor. The spell's level does not increase because of this ability.
No Turning (Weaponmaster)	KEY:ACF ~ No Turning (DMC) ~ Weaponmaster	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClericACFNoTurning.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Craft (Weaponsmithing)|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.166	DESC:You have devoted yourself to the mastery of your deity's favored weapon. Level: 1st. Replaces: Turn or rebuke undead. Benefit: You gain a +2 bonus on Craft (weaponsmith). As long as you wield your deity's favored weapon you no longer need a free hand in order to cast spells. Essentially, you substitute movements of your weapon for the somatic components of spells.
Peripheral Beliefs	KEY:Cleric ACF ~ Peripheral Beliefs (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.ClericACF.ClericPeripheralBeliefs	PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Peripheral Beliefs (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.168	DESC:Alternative class feature (cleric, 1st level). Traditions of the faith: the cleric chooses up to two peripheral beliefs (category below), each a restriction with a benefit; if he violates a belief for any reason he loses its benefit until he receives an atonement spell. Replaces nothing.
Peripheral Beliefs	KEY:ACF ~ Peripheral Beliefs (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Cleric Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Cleric ACF Peripheral Beliefs|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.168	DESC:Traditions of the faith: the cleric chooses up to two peripheral beliefs (category below), each a restriction with a benefit; if he violates a belief for any reason he loses its benefit until he receives an atonement spell. Replaces nothing.
Peripheral Beliefs (Daily Prayer)	KEY:ACF ~ Peripheral Beliefs (DMC) ~ Daily Prayer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClericACFPeripheralBeliefs.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.168	DESC:At specific times (at least dawn, noon and sunset, 5 minutes each; stricter lawful deities also mid-morning and mid-afternoon) you must stop and pray facing a specific direction. Benefit: you always discern true north as with 5 ranks in Survival; with 5 or more ranks you gain +2 on Survival checks instead.
Peripheral Beliefs (Day of Rest)	KEY:ACF ~ Peripheral Beliefs (DMC) ~ Day of Rest	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClericACFPeripheralBeliefs.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.168	DESC:Every seventh day you refrain from all physical activity: no attack actions, no spells with somatic components, no activating mechanical devices, no load heavier than light. Benefit: +4 on saves against sleep effects, and no -10 penalty on Listen checks while asleep.
Peripheral Beliefs (Dietary Restriction)	KEY:ACF ~ Peripheral Beliefs (DMC) ~ Dietary Restriction	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClericACFPeripheralBeliefs.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.168	DESC:Some food is unclean to you (and the utensils that touched it); food prepared by anyone but a devout follower, or potions you did not create, break the rule (detect poison detects such fare). Benefit: +1 on Fortitude saves against poisons and diseases.
Peripheral Beliefs (Sacred Animal)	KEY:ACF ~ Peripheral Beliefs (DMC) ~ Sacred Animal	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClericACFPeripheralBeliefs.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.168	DESC:A kind of animal is sacred to you: you cannot harm or impede one, even in self-defense, must keep it alive if allies fight it in self-defense, and cannot cast beneficial spells on allies for 24 hours if they were the aggressors. Benefit: such animals avoid attacking you unless defending themselves or compelled, and you gain +4 on Charisma-based checks with them.
Peripheral Beliefs (Sacred Clothing)	KEY:ACF ~ Peripheral Beliefs (DMC) ~ Sacred Clothing	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClericACFPeripheralBeliefs.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.168	DESC:You must always wear and display a particular item of clothing occupying a magic item slot (head covering, ceremonial glove ...), forgoing magic items in that slot. Benefit: the item is masterwork (at least 25 gp) and grants +2 on Charisma-based checks with followers of your religion.
Planar Banishment	KEY:Cleric ACF ~ Planar Banishment (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.ClericACF.ClericTurnUndead	PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Planar Banishment (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.169	DESC:Alternative class feature (cleric, 1st level). Instead of turning or rebuking undead, the cleric channels energy to banish outsiders: a cleric who would turn undead affects evil outsiders, one who would rebuke affects good outsiders (the DM may allow lawful/chaotic variants). Turning check as normal (an outsider counts its HD + Charisma modifier); turning damage 2d6 + %1 (cleric level + Charisma modifier) total HD of outsiders within 60 feet are banished to their home plane and cannot travel between planes for 10 rounds; with twice their effective HD in levels she destroys them instead. Uses per day as turning (%2). Replaces turn or rebuke undead.
Planar Banishment	KEY:ACF ~ Planar Banishment (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Cleric Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.169	DESC:Instead of turning or rebuking undead, the cleric channels energy to banish outsiders: a cleric who would turn undead affects evil outsiders, one who would rebuke affects good outsiders (the DM may allow lawful/chaotic variants). Turning check as normal (an outsider counts its HD + Charisma modifier); turning damage 2d6 + %1 (cleric level + Charisma modifier) total HD of outsiders within 60 feet are banished to their home plane and cannot travel between planes for 10 rounds; with twice their effective HD in levels she destroys them instead. Uses per day as turning (%2). Replaces turn or rebuke undead.|ClericLVL+CHA|3+CHA
Positive Healing	KEY:Cleric ACF ~ Positive Healing (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.ClericACF.ClericPositiveHealing	PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Positive Healing (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.171	DESC:Alternative class feature (cleric, 1st level). Lightbringer cleric: by spending one of his daily turn undead uses he internalizes the positive energy and gains fast healing 2 for 5 rounds (supernatural). Replaces one domain granted power (by hand).
Positive Healing	KEY:ACF ~ Positive Healing (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Cleric Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.171	DESC:Lightbringer cleric: by spending one of his daily turn undead uses he internalizes the positive energy and gains fast healing 2 for 5 rounds (supernatural). Replaces one domain granted power (by hand).
True Daylight	KEY:Cleric ACF ~ True Daylight (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.ClericACF.ClericTrueDaylight	PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ True Daylight (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.175	DESC:Alternative class feature (cleric, 1st level). Lightbringer cleric: by spending one daily turn undead use he empowers a daylight spell he casts with positive energy - true daylight in a 10-foot radius for 1d4 rounds (rolled each time), counting as real daylight against creatures harmed by bright light such as vampires (extraordinary). Replaces one domain granted power (by hand).
True Daylight	KEY:ACF ~ True Daylight (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Cleric Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.175	DESC:Lightbringer cleric: by spending one daily turn undead use he empowers a daylight spell he casts with positive energy - true daylight in a 10-foot radius for 1d4 rounds (rolled each time), counting as real daylight against creatures harmed by bright light such as vampires (extraordinary). Replaces one domain granted power (by hand).
Turning Presence	KEY:Cleric ACF ~ Turning Presence (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.ClericACF.ClericTurningPresence	PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Turning Presence (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.175	DESC:Alternative class feature (cleric, 1st level). Variant turning rule (a battle of personality strength): the cleric checks against the closest creature first, then the next closest (ties: lowest HD first), up to 60 feet. Each turning check is a level check plus Charisma modifier (effective turning level: cleric level, or paladin level - 3) against DC 10 + the creature's HD + its turn resistance + its Charisma modifier. Replaces nothing (it changes how turning is resolved).
Turning Presence	KEY:ACF ~ Turning Presence (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Cleric Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.175	DESC:Variant turning rule (a battle of personality strength): the cleric checks against the closest creature first, then the next closest (ties: lowest HD first), up to 60 feet. Each turning check is a level check plus Charisma modifier (effective turning level: cleric level, or paladin level - 3) against DC 10 + the creature's HD + its turn resistance + its Charisma modifier. Replaces nothing (it changes how turning is resolved).

###Block: Ranger alternative class features
Aquatic Ranger (Track in Water)	KEY:Ranger ACF ~ Aquatic Ranger (Track in Water) (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RangerACF.RangerAquaticTrack	PRECLASS:1,Ranger=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Aquatic Ranger (Track in Water) (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.477	DESC:Alternative class feature (ranger, 1st level). Rangers of the rivers and seas: he can follow a trail across streams or underwater using faint scent traces and lingering disturbances - Survival DC +10 for tracking in water, +1 per minute since the trail was made (+5 per minute in flowing water); impossible in rushing or stormy water except under wake trailing. Replaces nothing.
Aquatic Ranger (Track in Water)	KEY:ACF ~ Aquatic Ranger (Track in Water) (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Ranger Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.477	DESC:Rangers of the rivers and seas: he can follow a trail across streams or underwater using faint scent traces and lingering disturbances - Survival DC +10 for tracking in water, +1 per minute since the trail was made (+5 per minute in flowing water); impossible in rushing or stormy water except under wake trailing. Replaces nothing.
Aquatic Ranger (Woodland Stride)	KEY:Ranger ACF ~ Aquatic Ranger (Woodland Stride) (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RangerACF.RangerWoodlandStride	PRECLASS:1,Ranger=7	PREMOVE:1,Swim=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Aquatic Ranger (Woodland Stride) (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.477	DESC:Alternative class feature (ranger, 7th level). A ranger with a racial swim speed applies woodland stride to difficult aquatic terrain (shallow coral, kelp beds, ice-choked waters, sargasso and similar obstacles) rather than woodland terrain, chosen when the class feature is gained. Replaces woodland stride.
Aquatic Ranger (Woodland Stride)	KEY:ACF ~ Aquatic Ranger (Woodland Stride) (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Ranger Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.477	DESC:A ranger with a racial swim speed applies woodland stride to difficult aquatic terrain (shallow coral, kelp beds, ice-choked waters, sargasso and similar obstacles) rather than woodland terrain, chosen when the class feature is gained. Replaces woodland stride.
Celestial Slayer	KEY:Ranger ACF ~ Celestial Slayer (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RangerACF.RangerWildEmpathy.RangerAnimalCompanion.RangerWoodlandStride	PRECLASS:1,Ranger=1	PREALIGN:LE,NE,CE	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Celestial Slayer (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.477	DESC:Alternative class feature (ranger, 1st level). Drawing the dread attention of the Lower Planes: spell resistance %1 (10 + ranger level) against spells and spell-like effects with the good descriptor, and a +4 competence bonus on rolls to confirm critical hits against creatures of the good subtype. Evil only: you lose access if your alignment changes. Replaces wild empathy, the animal companion and woodland stride.
Celestial Slayer	KEY:ACF ~ Celestial Slayer (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Ranger Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.477	DESC:Drawing the dread attention of the Lower Planes: spell resistance %1 (10 + ranger level) against spells and spell-like effects with the good descriptor, and a +4 competence bonus on rolls to confirm critical hits against creatures of the good subtype. Evil only: you lose access if your alignment changes. Replaces wild empathy, the animal companion and woodland stride.|10+RangerLVL
Dead Levels	KEY:Ranger ACF ~ Dead Levels (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RangerACF.RangerDeadLevels	PRECLASS:1,Ranger=12	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Ranger Dead Levels (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.479	DESC:Alternative class feature (ranger, 12th level). Optional abilities for the ranger's dead levels (they replace nothing): Woodland Hunter (Ex), 12th - "get along in the wild" Survival checks while moving at full overland speed; Perceptive Tracker (Ex), 14th - never more than a full-round action to find tracks with Survival (a second roll still follows them); Seasoned Explorer (Ex), 16th - Survival checks for the bonus on Fortitude saves against severe weather while moving at full overland speed; Instinctive Tracker (Ex), 18th - a standard action to find tracks, moving at his speed at the same time; Survivalist (Ex), 19th - take 10 on Survival even under stress and distraction.
Dead Levels	KEY:ACF ~ Ranger Dead Levels (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Ranger Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.479	DESC:Optional abilities for the ranger's dead levels (they replace nothing): Woodland Hunter (Ex), 12th - "get along in the wild" Survival checks while moving at full overland speed; Perceptive Tracker (Ex), 14th - never more than a full-round action to find tracks with Survival (a second roll still follows them); Seasoned Explorer (Ex), 16th - Survival checks for the bonus on Fortitude saves against severe weather while moving at full overland speed; Instinctive Tracker (Ex), 18th - a standard action to find tracks, moving at his speed at the same time; Survivalist (Ex), 19th - take 10 on Survival even under stress and distraction.
Favored Environment	KEY:Ranger ACF ~ Favored Environment (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RangerACF.RangerFavoredEnemy	PRECLASS:1,Ranger=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Favored Environment (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.482	DESC:Alternative class feature (ranger, 1st level). Instead of favored enemies the ranger selects natural environments (category below): one at 1st level and another at 5th, 10th, 15th and 20th (%1 now); he gains +2 on Hide, Listen, Move Silently, Spot and Survival checks in each, and on associated Knowledge (nature) checks (Knowledge (dungeoneering) underground). At 5th level and every five levels he also gains an extra +2 to allocate to any favored environment (%2 extra points now; e.g. +4/+2 at 5th - by hand). Desert and forest require a climate choice; the DM may forbid environments he has never visited. Replaces favored enemy.
Favored Environment	KEY:ACF ~ Favored Environment (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Ranger Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Ranger ACF Favored Environment|1+floor(RangerLVL/5)	SOURCEPAGE:p.482	DESC:Instead of favored enemies the ranger selects natural environments (category below): one at 1st level and another at 5th, 10th, 15th and 20th (%1 now); he gains +2 on Hide, Listen, Move Silently, Spot and Survival checks in each, and on associated Knowledge (nature) checks (Knowledge (dungeoneering) underground). At 5th level and every five levels he also gains an extra +2 to allocate to any favored environment (%2 extra points now; e.g. +4/+2 at 5th - by hand). Desert and forest require a climate choice; the DM may forbid environments he has never visited. Replaces favored enemy.|1+floor(RangerLVL/5)|2*floor(RangerLVL/5)
Favored Environment (Aquatic)	KEY:ACF ~ Favored Environment (DMC) ~ Aquatic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFFavoredEnvironment.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.482	DESC:Favored environment: aquatic (sea, ocean (on or under water)). +2 (plus any extra bonus allocated here) on Hide, Listen, Move Silently, Spot and Survival checks in this environment, and on Knowledge (nature) checks associated with it.
Favored Environment (Cold Desert)	KEY:ACF ~ Favored Environment (DMC) ~ Cold Desert	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFFavoredEnvironment.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.482	DESC:Favored environment: cold desert (tundra). +2 (plus any extra bonus allocated here) on Hide, Listen, Move Silently, Spot and Survival checks in this environment, and on Knowledge (nature) checks associated with it.
Favored Environment (Temperate or Warm Desert)	KEY:ACF ~ Favored Environment (DMC) ~ Temperate or Warm Desert	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFFavoredEnvironment.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.482	DESC:Favored environment: temperate or warm desert (badlands, sandy desert). +2 (plus any extra bonus allocated here) on Hide, Listen, Move Silently, Spot and Survival checks in this environment, and on Knowledge (nature) checks associated with it.
Favored Environment (Cold or Temperate Forest)	KEY:ACF ~ Favored Environment (DMC) ~ Cold or Temperate Forest	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFFavoredEnvironment.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.482	DESC:Favored environment: cold or temperate forest (forest). +2 (plus any extra bonus allocated here) on Hide, Listen, Move Silently, Spot and Survival checks in this environment, and on Knowledge (nature) checks associated with it.
Favored Environment (Warm Forest)	KEY:ACF ~ Favored Environment (DMC) ~ Warm Forest	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFFavoredEnvironment.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.482	DESC:Favored environment: warm forest (jungle). +2 (plus any extra bonus allocated here) on Hide, Listen, Move Silently, Spot and Survival checks in this environment, and on Knowledge (nature) checks associated with it.
Favored Environment (Hills)	KEY:ACF ~ Favored Environment (DMC) ~ Hills	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFFavoredEnvironment.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.482	DESC:Favored environment: hills (rugged terrain up to 2,000 feet elevation). +2 (plus any extra bonus allocated here) on Hide, Listen, Move Silently, Spot and Survival checks in this environment, and on Knowledge (nature) checks associated with it.
Favored Environment (Marsh)	KEY:ACF ~ Favored Environment (DMC) ~ Marsh	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFFavoredEnvironment.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.482	DESC:Favored environment: marsh (bog, moor, swamp). +2 (plus any extra bonus allocated here) on Hide, Listen, Move Silently, Spot and Survival checks in this environment, and on Knowledge (nature) checks associated with it.
Favored Environment (Mountain)	KEY:ACF ~ Favored Environment (DMC) ~ Mountain	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFFavoredEnvironment.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.482	DESC:Favored environment: mountain (rugged terrain above 2,000 feet elevation). +2 (plus any extra bonus allocated here) on Hide, Listen, Move Silently, Spot and Survival checks in this environment, and on Knowledge (nature) checks associated with it.
Favored Environment (Plains)	KEY:ACF ~ Favored Environment (DMC) ~ Plains	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFFavoredEnvironment.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.482	DESC:Favored environment: plains (farmland, grassland, steppe, prairie). +2 (plus any extra bonus allocated here) on Hide, Listen, Move Silently, Spot and Survival checks in this environment, and on Knowledge (nature) checks associated with it.
Favored Environment (Underground)	KEY:ACF ~ Favored Environment (DMC) ~ Underground	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFFavoredEnvironment.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.482	DESC:Favored environment: underground (dungeons, caverns; Knowledge (dungeoneering) instead of Knowledge (nature)). +2 (plus any extra bonus allocated here) on Hide, Listen, Move Silently, Spot and Survival checks in this environment, and on Knowledge (nature) checks associated with it.
Feign Death	KEY:Ranger ACF ~ Feign Death (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RangerACF.RangerEvasion	PRECLASS:1,Ranger=9	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Ranger Feign Death (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.482	DESC:Alternative class feature (ranger, 9th level). As an immediate action you enter a catatonic state indistinguishable from death: you cannot see or feel, but still smell, hear and follow what goes on; you are immune to mind-affecting spells and abilities, poison, sleep, paralysis, stunning, disease, ability drain, negative levels and death effects; raise dead or reincarnation fail (resurrection and true resurrection end it); status and deathwatch show you dead; a Heal check (DC 15 + half your level + Constitution modifier) reveals you alive. You can remain so indefinitely (still needing food, water and air); emerging is a standard action. Replaces evasion.
Feign Death	KEY:ACF ~ Ranger Feign Death (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Ranger Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.482	DESC:As an immediate action you enter a catatonic state indistinguishable from death: you cannot see or feel, but still smell, hear and follow what goes on; you are immune to mind-affecting spells and abilities, poison, sleep, paralysis, stunning, disease, ability drain, negative levels and death effects; raise dead or reincarnation fail (resurrection and true resurrection end it); status and deathwatch show you dead; a Heal check (DC 15 + half your level + Constitution modifier) reveals you alive. You can remain so indefinitely (still needing food, water and air); emerging is a standard action. Replaces evasion.

###Block: Monk alternative class features
Feign Death	KEY:Monk ACF ~ Feign Death (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.MonkACF.MonkEvasion.MonkImprovedEvasion	PRECLASS:1,Monk=2	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Monk Feign Death (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.482	DESC:Alternative class feature (monk, 2nd level). As an immediate action you enter a catatonic state indistinguishable from death: you cannot see or feel, but still smell, hear and follow what goes on; you are immune to mind-affecting spells and abilities, poison, sleep, paralysis, stunning, disease, ability drain, negative levels and death effects; raise dead or reincarnation fail (resurrection and true resurrection end it); status and deathwatch show you dead; a Heal check (DC 15 + half your level + Constitution modifier) reveals you alive. You can remain so indefinitely (still needing food, water and air); emerging is a standard action. Replaces evasion; at 9th level you gain evasion instead of improved evasion.
Feign Death	KEY:ACF ~ Monk Feign Death (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Monk Class Feature	ABILITY:Monk Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Monk ~ Evasion|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,9	SOURCEPAGE:p.482	DESC:As an immediate action you enter a catatonic state indistinguishable from death: you cannot see or feel, but still smell, hear and follow what goes on; you are immune to mind-affecting spells and abilities, poison, sleep, paralysis, stunning, disease, ability drain, negative levels and death effects; raise dead or reincarnation fail (resurrection and true resurrection end it); status and deathwatch show you dead; a Heal check (DC 15 + half your level + Constitution modifier) reveals you alive. You can remain so indefinitely (still needing food, water and air); emerging is a standard action. Replaces evasion; at 9th level you gain evasion instead of improved evasion.

