Feign Death	KEY:Rogue ACF ~ Feign Death (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RogueACF.RogueEvasion	PRECLASS:1,Rogue=2	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Rogue Feign Death (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.482	DESC:Alternative class feature (rogue, 2nd level). As an immediate action you enter a catatonic state indistinguishable from death: you cannot see or feel, but still smell, hear and follow what goes on; you are immune to mind-affecting spells and abilities, poison, sleep, paralysis, stunning, disease, ability drain, negative levels and death effects; raise dead or reincarnation fail (resurrection and true resurrection end it); status and deathwatch show you dead; a Heal check (DC 15 + half your level + Constitution modifier) reveals you alive. You can remain so indefinitely (still needing food, water and air); emerging is a standard action. Replaces evasion.
Feign Death	KEY:ACF ~ Rogue Feign Death (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Rogue Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.482	DESC:As an immediate action you enter a catatonic state indistinguishable from death: you cannot see or feel, but still smell, hear and follow what goes on; you are immune to mind-affecting spells and abilities, poison, sleep, paralysis, stunning, disease, ability drain, negative levels and death effects; raise dead or reincarnation fail (resurrection and true resurrection end it); status and deathwatch show you dead; a Heal check (DC 15 + half your level + Constitution modifier) reveals you alive. You can remain so indefinitely (still needing food, water and air); emerging is a standard action. Replaces evasion.

###Block: Ranger alternative class features
Golarion Ranger	KEY:Ranger ACF ~ Golarion Ranger (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RangerACF.RangerWildEmpathy	PRECLASS:1,Ranger=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Golarion Ranger (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.484	DESC:Alternative class feature (ranger, 1st level). Rangers of a military unit who focus on a single animal: upon gaining an animal companion at 4th level he chooses a single type of animal from the basic list available at 4th level and can never call a different companion; his effective druid level for it is his ranger level - 2 (%1) instead of half his level (applied). Replaces wild empathy.
Golarion Ranger	KEY:ACF ~ Golarion Ranger (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Ranger Class Feature	BONUS:VAR|AnimalCompanionLVL|(RangerLVL-2)-floor(RangerLVL/2)|PREVARGTEQ:RangerLVL,4	SOURCEPAGE:p.484	DESC:Rangers of a military unit who focus on a single animal: upon gaining an animal companion at 4th level he chooses a single type of animal from the basic list available at 4th level and can never call a different companion; his effective druid level for it is his ranger level - 2 (%1) instead of half his level (applied). Replaces wild empathy.|RangerLVL-2
Natural Born Ranger	KEY:Ranger ACF ~ Natural Born Ranger (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RangerACF.RangerNaturalBorn	PRECLASS:1,Ranger=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Natural Born Ranger (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.487	DESC:Alternative class feature (ranger, 1st level). Alternative racial traits for characters who begin play as 1st-level rangers, scorning their culture's lessons for what they teach themselves (choose your race's in the category below; the DM should understand them well before allowing them).
Natural Born Ranger	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Ranger (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Ranger Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Ranger ACF Natural Born Ranger|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.487	DESC:Alternative racial traits for characters who begin play as 1st-level rangers, scorning their culture's lessons for what they teach themselves (choose your race's in the category below; the DM should understand them well before allowing them).
Natural Born Ranger (Dwarf)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Ranger (DMC) ~ Dwarf	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFNaturalBornRanger.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Dwarf%	SOURCEPAGE:p.487	DESC:The dwarf ranger loses stonecunning, the racial bonuses on Appraise and Craft checks and the dodge bonus to AC against giants (remove by hand); he gains a dodge bonus to AC against his favored enemies equal to half his favored enemy bonus against them.
Natural Born Ranger (Elf)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Ranger (DMC) ~ Elf	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFNaturalBornRanger.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Elf%	SOURCEPAGE:p.487	DESC:Affinity for the terrain of his homeland (choose aquatic, desert, forest, hills, marsh, mountain or plains): +1 on attack and damage rolls in that terrain; outside it, -1 on Wisdom- and Intelligence-based skill checks.
Natural Born Ranger (Gnome)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Ranger (DMC) ~ Gnome	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFNaturalBornRanger.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Gnome%	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=1|CASTERLEVEL=1|Create Water,Detect Poison,Purify Food and Drink	SOURCEPAGE:p.487	DESC:The gnome ranger keeps speak with animals but loses her other spell-like abilities (dancing lights, ghost sound, prestidigitation - remove by hand), casting create water, detect poison and purify food and drink once per day instead (caster level 1st; save DC 10 + Charisma modifier + spell level).
Natural Born Ranger (Half-Elf)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Ranger (DMC) ~ Half-Elf	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFNaturalBornRanger.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Half-Elf%	BONUS:SKILL|Diplomacy,Gather Information|-2	BONUS:SKILL|Handle Animal,Hide|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.487	DESC:The half-elf ranger loses the +2 bonus on Diplomacy and Gather Information checks and gains +2 on Handle Animal and Hide checks instead (applied).
Natural Born Ranger (Half-Orc)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Ranger (DMC) ~ Half-Orc	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFNaturalBornRanger.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Half-Orc%	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Favored Enemy|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.487	DESC:An additional favored enemy at 1st level: humanoid (human) or humanoid (orc) - not the same as his first one - with the normal +2 bonuses, increased like any other favored enemy; but a penalty equal to that favored enemy bonus on all Charisma checks and Charisma-based skills when dealing with members of the despised race (by hand).
Natural Born Ranger (Halfling)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Ranger (DMC) ~ Halfling	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFNaturalBornRanger.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Halfling%	BONUS:VAR|HalflingSaveBonus|-1	SOURCEPAGE:p.487	DESC:The halfling ranger loses the +1 luck bonus on all saving throws (applied); she gains a bonus on saving throws and opposed skill checks against her favored enemies equal to half her favored enemy bonus against them.
Solitary Hunting	KEY:Ranger ACF ~ Solitary Hunting (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RangerACF.RangerAnimalCompanion	PRECLASS:1,Ranger=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Solitary Hunting (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.494	DESC:Alternative class feature (ranger, 1st level). A ranger who loses his faith also loses his animal companion (one he already has abandons him at once), becoming even more self-reliant: his favored enemy bonus also applies to his attack rolls against those enemies. Replaces the animal companion.
Solitary Hunting	KEY:ACF ~ Solitary Hunting (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Ranger Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.494	DESC:A ranger who loses his faith also loses his animal companion (one he already has abandons him at once), becoming even more self-reliant: his favored enemy bonus also applies to his attack rolls against those enemies. Replaces the animal companion.
Wasteland Ranger	KEY:Ranger ACF ~ Wasteland Ranger (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RangerACF.RangerEndurance.RangerWoodlandStride	PRECLASS:1,Ranger=3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Wasteland Ranger (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.498	DESC:Alternative class feature (ranger, 3rd level). Rangers of the waste (Sandstorm's variant): Heat Endurance as a bonus feat at 3rd level instead of Endurance (Improved Heat Endurance if he already has it, without its prerequisites); Sandskimmer as a bonus feat at 7th level instead of woodland stride - both Sandstorm feats, not in the repository's Sandstorm data, so add them by hand. Waste Hunter (Ex), 10th level: he chooses a kind of waste-native creature among his favored enemy types (e.g. dunewinders for magical beasts) and gains +2 on weapon damage and on Bluff, Listen, Sense Motive, Spot and Survival checks against it, +2 on saves against its special abilities and DR 2/- against its physical attacks; this replaces the favored enemy gained at 10th level (applied), though his bonuses against earlier favored enemies still increase as normal. Replaces Endurance and woodland stride.
Wasteland Ranger	KEY:ACF ~ Wasteland Ranger (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Ranger Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Favored Enemy|-1|PREVARGTEQ:RangerLVL,10	SOURCEPAGE:p.498	DESC:Rangers of the waste (Sandstorm's variant): Heat Endurance as a bonus feat at 3rd level instead of Endurance (Improved Heat Endurance if he already has it, without its prerequisites); Sandskimmer as a bonus feat at 7th level instead of woodland stride - both Sandstorm feats, not in the repository's Sandstorm data, so add them by hand. Waste Hunter (Ex), 10th level: he chooses a kind of waste-native creature among his favored enemy types (e.g. dunewinders for magical beasts) and gains +2 on weapon damage and on Bluff, Listen, Sense Motive, Spot and Survival checks against it, +2 on saves against its special abilities and DR 2/- against its physical attacks; this replaces the favored enemy gained at 10th level (applied), though his bonuses against earlier favored enemies still increase as normal. Replaces Endurance and woodland stride.
Animal Companions	KEY:Ranger ACF ~ Animal Companions (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RangerACF.RangerCompanionList	PRECLASS:1,Ranger=4	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Ranger Animal Companions (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.216	DESC:Alternative class feature (ranger, 4th level). The compendium's compilation of all animals eligible as animal companions (p.216) applies to rangers too, by effective druid level (half the ranger's level); the list and its adjustments are described in the druid's Animal Companions entry. (Offered here: the creatures in the core data; it replaces nothing.)
Animal Companions	KEY:ACF ~ Ranger Animal Companions (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Ranger Class Feature	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Badger,Companion ~ Bat,Companion ~ Camel,Companion ~ Dog,Companion ~ Dog (Riding),Donkey,Companion ~ Eagle,Companion ~ Hawk,Companion ~ Horse (Light),Companion ~ Horse (Heavy),Hyena,Companion ~ Owl,Companion ~ Pony,Companion ~ Porpoise,Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Rat),Companion ~ Raven,Companion ~ Shark (Medium),Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Tiny),Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Small),Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Medium),Companion ~ Squid,Companion ~ Wolf	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Ape,Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Badger),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Bat),Companion ~ Bear (Black),Companion ~ Bison,Companion ~ Boar,Companion ~ Cheetah,Companion ~ Leopard,Companion ~ Lizard (Monitor),Companion ~ Shark (Large),Companion ~ Snake (Constrictor),Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Large),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Weasel),Companion ~ Wolverine|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-3	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Ape),Companion ~ Bear (Brown),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Boar),Companion ~ Crocodile (Giant),Companion ~ Dinosaur (Deinonychus),Companion ~ Dinosaur (Elasmosaurus),Companion ~ Lion,Companion ~ Rhinoceros,Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Huge),Companion ~ Tiger,Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Wolf),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Wolverine)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-6	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Bear (Polar),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Lion),Companion ~ Dinosaur (Megaraptor),Companion ~ Shark (Huge),Companion ~ Snake (Constrictor/Giant),Companion ~ Whale (Orca)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-9	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Bear),Companion ~ Elephant,Companion ~ Octopus (Giant)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-12	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Roc,Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Shark),Companion ~ Squid (Giant),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Tiger),Companion ~ Dinosaur (Triceratops),Companion ~ Dinosaur (Tyrannosaurus)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-15	SOURCEPAGE:p.216	DESC:The compendium's compilation of all animals eligible as animal companions (p.216) applies to rangers too, by effective druid level (half the ranger's level); the list and its adjustments are described in the druid's Animal Companions entry. (Offered here: the creatures in the core data; it replaces nothing.)

###Block: Barbarian alternative class features
Aquatic Barbarian	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Aquatic Barbarian (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianFastMovement	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=1	PREMOVE:1,Swim=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Aquatic Barbarian (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.96	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 1st level). Barbarians of the waters and shores, adept swimmers: a barbarian with a racial swim speed applies his fast movement bonus (+10 feet) to his swim speed instead of his land speed (applied; only in no, light or medium armor and not with a heavy load), chosen when the feature is gained. Replaces fast movement on land.
Aquatic Barbarian	KEY:ACF ~ Aquatic Barbarian (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	BONUS:MOVEADD|TYPE.Swim|10|!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Heavy	SOURCEPAGE:p.96	DESC:Barbarians of the waters and shores, adept swimmers: a barbarian with a racial swim speed applies his fast movement bonus (+10 feet) to his swim speed instead of his land speed (applied; only in no, light or medium armor and not with a heavy load), chosen when the feature is gained. Replaces fast movement on land.
Berserker Strength	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Berserker Strength (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianRage.BarbarianGreaterRage.BarbarianMightyRage.BarbarianTirelessRage	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Berserker Strength (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.96	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 1st level). Whenever your current hit points are below 5 x your barbarian level (%1), berserker strength activates automatically, any number of times per day: +4 Strength, +2 on saves, damage reduction 2/- (stacking with similar DR) and -2 AC, with a raging barbarian's limits on actions; you cannot end it voluntarily (it ends when you are unconscious, helpless or healed above the threshold). At 11th level (or when you would gain greater rage) +6 Strength, +3 saves, DR 3/-; at 20th (or mighty rage) +8 Strength, +4 saves, DR 4/-. Effects that apply while raging apply while it is active. (Player's Handbook II's repository entry is an unfinished stub.) Replaces rage and its later improvements.
Berserker Strength	KEY:ACF ~ Berserker Strength (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.96	DESC:Whenever your current hit points are below 5 x your barbarian level (%1), berserker strength activates automatically, any number of times per day: +4 Strength, +2 on saves, damage reduction 2/- (stacking with similar DR) and -2 AC, with a raging barbarian's limits on actions; you cannot end it voluntarily (it ends when you are unconscious, helpless or healed above the threshold). At 11th level (or when you would gain greater rage) +6 Strength, +3 saves, DR 3/-; at 20th (or mighty rage) +8 Strength, +4 saves, DR 4/-. Effects that apply while raging apply while it is active. (Player's Handbook II's repository entry is an unfinished stub.) Replaces rage and its later improvements.|5*BarbarianLVL
City Brawler	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ City Brawler (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianProficiencies	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ City Brawler (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.97	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 1st level). The urban slums you grew up in were as dangerous as any wilderness: Improved Unarmed Strike as a bonus feat (applied) and the effects of Two-Weapon Fighting when fighting unarmed, of Improved Two-Weapon Fighting from 6th level and of Greater Two-Weapon Fighting from 11th; only -2 (not -4) when using improvised weapons. Replaces proficiency with martial weapons, medium armor and shields.
City Brawler	KEY:ACF ~ City Brawler (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=ArmorProfLight|TYPE=WeaponProfSimple	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Improved Unarmed Strike	SOURCEPAGE:p.97	DESC:The urban slums you grew up in were as dangerous as any wilderness: Improved Unarmed Strike as a bonus feat (applied) and the effects of Two-Weapon Fighting when fighting unarmed, of Improved Two-Weapon Fighting from 6th level and of Greater Two-Weapon Fighting from 11th; only -2 (not -4) when using improvised weapons. Replaces proficiency with martial weapons, medium armor and shields.
Dashing Step	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Dashing Step (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianTrapSense	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Dashing Step (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.97	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 3rd level). You have mastered rushing into combat: no -2 AC penalty when charging, and a bonus of +%1 (one-third of your barbarian level) to AC against attacks of opportunity when charging. Replaces trap sense.
Dashing Step	KEY:ACF ~ Dashing Step (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.97	DESC:You have mastered rushing into combat: no -2 AC penalty when charging, and a bonus of +%1 (one-third of your barbarian level) to AC against attacks of opportunity when charging. Replaces trap sense.|floor(BarbarianLVL/3)
Devil's Luck	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Devil's Luck (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianDamageReduction	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=7	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Devil's Luck (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.97	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 7th level). You make up for your lack of heartiness with astounding luck: the points of damage reduction you would otherwise have become a luck bonus on all saving throws (+%1 now; applied). Replaces damage reduction.
Devil's Luck	KEY:ACF ~ Devil's Luck (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	BONUS:SAVE|Fortitude,Reflex,Will|floor((BarbarianLVL-4)/3)|TYPE=Luck	SOURCEPAGE:p.97	DESC:You make up for your lack of heartiness with astounding luck: the points of damage reduction you would otherwise have become a luck bonus on all saving throws (+%1 now; applied). Replaces damage reduction.|floor((BarbarianLVL-4)/3)
Fearsome Gaze	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Fearsome Gaze (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianIndomitableWill	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=6	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Fearsome Gaze (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.99	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 6th level). Your merest glance can break a will to fight: +4 on Intimidate checks, using Strength instead of Charisma as the key ability if better (both applied); you and the target must be within 60 feet and see one another. Replaces indomitable will, and your trap sense bonus is reduced by 1 (applied).
Fearsome Gaze	KEY:ACF ~ Fearsome Gaze (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	BONUS:SKILL|Intimidate|4	BONUS:SKILL|Intimidate|max(0,STR-CHA)	BONUS:VAR|TrapSenseBonus|-1	SOURCEPAGE:p.99	DESC:Your merest glance can break a will to fight: +4 on Intimidate checks, using Strength instead of Charisma as the key ability if better (both applied); you and the target must be within 60 feet and see one another. Replaces indomitable will, and your trap sense bonus is reduced by 1 (applied).
Frostfell Barbarian	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Frostfell Barbarian (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianFrostfell	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Frostfell Barbarian (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.100	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 3rd level). Barbarians at home in the frostfell (often riding dire wolves, megaloceroses, tlalusks or woolly mammoths): their trap sense bonus applies on Reflex saves against natural hazards of the frostfell (avalanches, snow-filled crevasses, other frostfell terrain) and to AC against attacks by such hazards, instead of against traps. Replaces the benefits of trap sense (the bonus itself is unchanged).
Frostfell Barbarian	KEY:ACF ~ Frostfell Barbarian (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.100	DESC:Barbarians at home in the frostfell (often riding dire wolves, megaloceroses, tlalusks or woolly mammoths): their trap sense bonus applies on Reflex saves against natural hazards of the frostfell (avalanches, snow-filled crevasses, other frostfell terrain) and to AC against attacks by such hazards, instead of against traps. Replaces the benefits of trap sense (the bonus itself is unchanged).
Golarion Barbarian	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Golarion Barbarian (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianTrapSense	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Golarion Barbarian (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.100	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 3rd level). Barbarians of cold climates (the Lands of the Linnorm Kings, the Realm of the Mammoth Lords, the Worldwound): cold resistance %1 (2 at 3rd level, +2 every three levels, 12 at 18th; applied). Replaces trap sense.
Golarion Barbarian	KEY:ACF ~ Golarion Barbarian (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	BONUS:VAR|ColdResistanceBonus|2*floor(BarbarianLVL/3)	SOURCEPAGE:p.100	DESC:Barbarians of cold climates (the Lands of the Linnorm Kings, the Realm of the Mammoth Lords, the Worldwound): cold resistance %1 (2 at 3rd level, +2 every three levels, 12 at 18th; applied). Replaces trap sense.|2*floor(BarbarianLVL/3)
Hunter	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Hunter (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianRage.BarbarianGreaterRage.BarbarianIndomitableWill.BarbarianTirelessRage.BarbarianMightyRage	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Hunter (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 1st level). A barbarian who prefers crafty hunting over pure ferocity (swap): favored enemy as the ranger, by barbarian level (1st, 5th, 10th ...), and the ranger's archery combat style with improved archery combat style and archery combat style mastery at 2nd, 6th and 11th (Rapid Shot, Manyshot, Improved Precise Shot - only in light or no armor). Replaces rage, greater rage, indomitable will, tireless rage and mighty rage.
Hunter	KEY:ACF ~ Hunter (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	ABILITY:Ranger Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Ranger ~ Favored Enemy	BONUS:VAR|RangerFavoredEnemyLVL|BarbarianLVL	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Combat Style ~ Archery	DEFINE:RangerCombatTreeTier|0	BONUS:VAR|RangerCombatTreeTier|1|PREVARGTEQ:BarbarianLVL,2	BONUS:VAR|RangerCombatTreeTier|1|PREVARGTEQ:BarbarianLVL,6	BONUS:VAR|RangerCombatTreeTier|1|PREVARGTEQ:BarbarianLVL,11	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:A barbarian who prefers crafty hunting over pure ferocity (swap): favored enemy as the ranger, by barbarian level (1st, 5th, 10th ...), and the ranger's archery combat style with improved archery combat style and archery combat style mastery at 2nd, 6th and 11th (Rapid Shot, Manyshot, Improved Precise Shot - only in light or no armor). Replaces rage, greater rage, indomitable will, tireless rage and mighty rage.
Natural Born Barbarian	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Natural Born Barbarian (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianNaturalBorn	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Natural Born Barbarian (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 1st level). Alternative racial traits for characters who begin play as 1st-level barbarians (choose your race's in the category below; the DM should understand them well before allowing them).
Natural Born Barbarian	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Barbarian (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Barbarian ACF Natural Born Barbarian|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:Alternative racial traits for characters who begin play as 1st-level barbarians (choose your race's in the category below; the DM should understand them well before allowing them).
Natural Born Barbarian (Dwarf)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Barbarian (DMC) ~ Dwarf	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:BarbarianACFNaturalBornBarbarian.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Dwarf%	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:The dwarf barbarian loses stonecunning, the racial bonuses on Appraise and Craft checks and the +1 on attack rolls against orcs and goblins (remove by hand); he gains +1 on attack and damage rolls against aberrations and undead while raging.
Natural Born Barbarian (Elf)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Barbarian (DMC) ~ Elf	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:BarbarianACFNaturalBornBarbarian.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Elf%	BONUS:COMBAT|INITIATIVE|-2	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:The elf barbarian can use Rapid Shot while raging even without its prerequisites, but takes a -2 penalty on initiative checks (applied).
Natural Born Barbarian (Gnome)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Barbarian (DMC) ~ Gnome	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:BarbarianACFNaturalBornBarbarian.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Gnome%	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=1|CASTERLEVEL=1|Cure Minor Wounds,Guidance,Jump,Resistance	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:The gnome barbarian loses speak with animals and the other gnome spell-like abilities (remove by hand), casting cure minor wounds, guidance, jump and resistance (self only) once each per day instead (caster level 1st; save DC 10 + Charisma modifier + spell level).
Natural Born Barbarian (Half-Elf)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Barbarian (DMC) ~ Half-Elf	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:BarbarianACFNaturalBornBarbarian.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Half-Elf%	BONUS:SKILL|Diplomacy,Gather Information|-2	BONUS:SKILL|Intimidate,Survival|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:The half-elf barbarian loses the +2 bonus on Diplomacy and Gather Information checks and gains +2 on Intimidate and Survival checks (applied).
Natural Born Barbarian (Half-Orc)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Barbarian (DMC) ~ Half-Orc	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:BarbarianACFNaturalBornBarbarian.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Half-Orc%	BONUS:SKILL|Intimidate,Survival|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:The half-orc barbarian can never learn to read, even with levels in other classes, nor place ranks in any Knowledge skill (by hand); his contempt for book learning grants +2 on Intimidate and Survival checks (applied).
Natural Born Barbarian (Halfling)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Barbarian (DMC) ~ Halfling	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:BarbarianACFNaturalBornBarbarian.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Halfling%	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:The halfling barbarian loses the racial bonuses on Climb, Jump and Move Silently checks (remove by hand) and gains a bonus on Hide checks in natural surroundings equal to half her barbarian level (minimum +1).
Relentless Smash	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Relentless Smash (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianMightyRage	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=20	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Relentless Smash (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.107	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 20th level). If you score a critical hit against an opponent or strike him at least three times in the same round, he is stunned for 1d3 rounds; an opponent of your size or smaller must also succeed on a Fortitude save (DC 10 + the total damage you dealt him this round) or be knocked prone. Replaces mighty rage.
Relentless Smash	KEY:ACF ~ Relentless Smash (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.107	DESC:If you score a critical hit against an opponent or strike him at least three times in the same round, he is stunned for 1d3 rounds; an opponent of your size or smaller must also succeed on a Fortitude save (DC 10 + the total damage you dealt him this round) or be knocked prone. Replaces mighty rage.
Unholy Fury	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Unholy Fury (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianFastMovement	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=1	PREALIGN:CE	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Unholy Fury (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.111	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 1st level). Once during a rage, you can unleash your unholy fury to smite a nonchaotic evil creature: add your Charisma bonus to the attack roll and deal +%1 damage (1 per barbarian level); against a chaotic evil creature the smite has no effect but is still used up. Chaotic evil only: with another alignment it reverts to standard rage until your alignment is restored. Replaces fast movement.
Unholy Fury	KEY:ACF ~ Unholy Fury (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.111	DESC:Once during a rage, you can unleash your unholy fury to smite a nonchaotic evil creature: add your Charisma bonus to the attack roll and deal +%1 damage (1 per barbarian level); against a chaotic evil creature the smite has no effect but is still used up. Chaotic evil only: with another alignment it reverts to standard rage until your alignment is restored. Replaces fast movement.|BarbarianLVL
Unshakable	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Unshakable (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianImprovedUncannyDodge	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=5	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Unshakable (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.111	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 5th level). You fear nothing: immunity to fear effects (applied). Replaces improved uncanny dodge.
Unshakable	KEY:ACF ~ Unshakable (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Immunity to Fear	SOURCEPAGE:p.111	DESC:You fear nothing: immunity to fear effects (applied). Replaces improved uncanny dodge.

###Block: Rogue alternative class features
Criminal Specialist	KEY:Rogue ACF ~ Criminal Specialist (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RogueACF.RogueCriminalSpecialist	PRECLASS:1,Rogue=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Criminal Specialist (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.504	DESC:Alternative class feature (rogue, 1st level). A rogue (or a member of any class with all six listed skills as class skills) may specialize in one type of crime, as a wizard specializes in a school: four mandatory skills, two prohibited skills (never ranks, untrained use allowed), and with the right Skill Focus a unique ability at the listed level, usable only while keeping maximum ranks in the listed skills (choose in the category below). Replaces nothing.
Criminal Specialist	KEY:ACF ~ Criminal Specialist (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Rogue Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Rogue ACF Criminal Specialist|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.504	DESC:A rogue (or a member of any class with all six listed skills as class skills) may specialize in one type of crime, as a wizard specializes in a school: four mandatory skills, two prohibited skills (never ranks, untrained use allowed), and with the right Skill Focus a unique ability at the listed level, usable only while keeping maximum ranks in the listed skills (choose in the category below). Replaces nothing.
Criminal Specialist (Beggar)	KEY:ACF ~ Criminal Specialist (DMC) ~ Beggar	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RogueACFCriminalSpecialist.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Skill Focus (Disguise)	PRELEVEL:MIN=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.504	DESC:Beggar specialist (1st level). Prerequisites: Bluff, Disguise, Sleight of Hand, Spot, Skill Focus (Disguise). Forbidden skills (never ranks; untrained use allowed): Disable Device and Open Lock. Playing Possum (Ex): You may attempt to gain a temporary edge in combat by shamming a debilitating injury, such as blindness or a missing limb. This requires 1 minute of advance preparation, a disguise kit, and a Disguise check. The next intelligent foe you encounter must succeed at an opposed Spot check or else he is flat-footed against your first attack. Your first attack in the combat must be made against this foe. If you encounter multiple foes, they all get a chance to see through your disguise, but you only gain the benefit of this ability on the first attack you make. Usable only while you keep maximum ranks in the four listed skills (by hand).
Criminal Specialist (Blackmailer)	KEY:ACF ~ Criminal Specialist (DMC) ~ Blackmailer	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RogueACFCriminalSpecialist.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Skill Focus (Intimidate)	PRELEVEL:MIN=3	SOURCEPAGE:p.504	DESC:Blackmailer specialist (3rd level). Prerequisites: Decipher Script, Gather Information, Intimidate, Search, Skill Focus (Intimidate). Forbidden skills (never ranks; untrained use allowed): Disable Device and Open Lock. Vilify (Ex): You can attempt to uncover some secret humiliation of a particular foe by carefully sifting through rumor and idle Speculation. You must spend at least 8 hours chasing gossip in an area your target has frequented within the last month followed by a Gather Information check (DC 10 + target's CR). If you succeed at this Gather Information check you may, at any time in the following month, make an Intimidate check against your target as a full-round action. At any time in the next hour, as long as you are not in combat, you may issue a command (as the spell) at your target as a standard action. The save DC of your command effect equals the result of your Intimidate check. This is a language- dependant, mind-affecting ability. If your Gather Information check fails you must wait at least six months before trying again against that particular target. If your target simply has no humiliating indiscretions in her past (as determined by the DM) you cannot use this ability against that target. Usable only while you keep maximum ranks in the four listed skills (by hand).
Criminal Specialist (Fence)	KEY:ACF ~ Criminal Specialist (DMC) ~ Fence	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RogueACFCriminalSpecialist.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Skill Focus (Appraise)	PRELEVEL:MIN=6	SOURCEPAGE:p.504	DESC:Fence specialist (6th level). Prerequisites: Appraise, Bluff, Forgery, Sense Motive, Skill Focus (Appraise). Forbidden skills (never ranks; untrained use allowed): Climb and Tumble. Fracture (Ex): Your trained eye can identify and exploit the subtle, hidden defects of objects. After your first successful attack against a construct or object, you may make an Appraise check (DC 15 for an object or DC 15 + creature's CR for a construct). For every point by which you succeed at this check you can ignore one point of hardness or one point of DR for all later attacks against that construct or object. You can only use this ability with melee attacks. Usable only while you keep maximum ranks in the four listed skills (by hand).
Criminal Specialist (Goon)	KEY:ACF ~ Criminal Specialist (DMC) ~ Goon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RogueACFCriminalSpecialist.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Skill Focus (Intimidate)	PRELEVEL:MIN=6	SOURCEPAGE:p.504	DESC:Goon specialist (6th level). Prerequisites: Bluff, Gather Information, Intimidate, Sense Motive, Skill Focus (Intimidate). Forbidden skills (never ranks; untrained use allowed): Decipher Script and Use Magic Device. Browbeat (Ex): You can, as a full-round action, make a single melee attack against an opponent. If you hit and deal damage, you can immediately follow it with an Intimidate check (DC 15 + target's CR). If you succeed in this check your foe becomes shaken until the end of your next turn. For each round you continue to attack the same target, you gain a cumulative +1 bonus on your Intimidate checks. This is a mind-affecting fear effect. Usable only while you keep maximum ranks in the four listed skills (by hand).
Criminal Specialist (Kidnapper)	KEY:ACF ~ Criminal Specialist (DMC) ~ Kidnapper	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RogueACFCriminalSpecialist.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Skill Focus (Use Rope)	PRELEVEL:MIN=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.504	DESC:Kidnapper specialist (1st level). Prerequisites: Climb, Disguise, Move Silently, Use Rope, Skill Focus (Use Rope). Forbidden skills (never ranks; untrained use allowed): Diplomacy and Tumble. Hobble (Ex): You can attempt to restrict or bind any foe you manage to catch unawares. Whenever you face a flat- footed opponent no more than one size category larger than you, you may attempt a melee touch attack as a full-round action. You must have a length of rope at least 20 feet long in hand when you make this touch attack. If you succeed, you can wrap your target's arms and legs in rope. Make a Use Rope check with a -4 penalty. Your target moves at half his normal speed and takes a -2 penalty to Strength and Dexterity scores until he escapes your knots, requiring a full- round action and an Escape Artist check (DC equals your Use Rope check). Usable only while you keep maximum ranks in the four listed skills (by hand).
Criminal Specialist (Lookout)	KEY:ACF ~ Criminal Specialist (DMC) ~ Lookout	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RogueACFCriminalSpecialist.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Skill Focus (Spot)	PRELEVEL:MIN=3	SOURCEPAGE:p.504	DESC:Lookout specialist (3rd level). Prerequisites: Hide, Listen, Move Silently, Spot, Skill Focus (Spot). Forbidden skills (never ranks; untrained use allowed): Appraise and Disable Device. Perceive (Su): As a full-round action, you can gain one of the following effects until your next turn: blindsense, low- light vision, scent, or tremorsense. You cannot gain an effect you already possess. This ability requires you to concentrate the entire time. If you are attacked or otherwise distracted, you must succeed at a DC 20 Concentration check or lose the effect. Usable only while you keep maximum ranks in the four listed skills (by hand).
Criminal Specialist (Pickpocket)	KEY:ACF ~ Criminal Specialist (DMC) ~ Pickpocket	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RogueACFCriminalSpecialist.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Skill Focus (Sleight of Hand)	PRELEVEL:MIN=6	SOURCEPAGE:p.504	DESC:Pickpocket specialist (6th level). Prerequisites: Hide, Move Silently, Sleight of Hand, Spot, Skill Focus (Sleight of Hand). Forbidden skills (never ranks; untrained use allowed): Disable Device and Sense Motive. Snatch Weapon (Ex): You can attempt to strip a creature of a sheathed weapon by making a Sleight of Hand check (DC 20 + target's CR) as a full-round action. Your target must be flat-footed to you. You can snatch a light weapon (based on your size, not your target's) without penalty, a one-handed weapon with a -4 penalty, and a two-handed weapon with a -8 penalty. You cannot snatch a weapon too large for you to wield. If you succeed in this check, you gain possession of the weapon. You must have enough free hands available when you attempt the snatch to wield the weapon properly (i.e., you must have at least one free hand when attempting to snatch a light or one-handed weapon and two free hands when attempting to snatch a two-handed weapon). When you use this ability, your Sleight of Hand check is opposed by the Spot checks of those nearby. The success of observers (including your victim) doesn't prevent you from performing the snatch, just from doing it unnoticed.  Usable only while you keep maximum ranks in the four listed skills (by hand).
Dead Levels	KEY:Rogue ACF ~ Dead Levels (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RogueACF.RogueDeadLevels	PRECLASS:1,Rogue=14	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Rogue Dead Levels (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.506	DESC:Alternative class feature (rogue, 14th level). The rogue's dead levels (replacing nothing): Makeshift Tools (Ex), 14th level - Disable Device checks without thieves' tools at no penalty; Skilled Saboteur (Ex), 20th level - disabling devices takes half the normal time (1 round becomes a standard action, leaving a move action).
Dead Levels	KEY:ACF ~ Rogue Dead Levels (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Rogue Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.506	DESC:The rogue's dead levels (replacing nothing): Makeshift Tools (Ex), 14th level - Disable Device checks without thieves' tools at no penalty; Skilled Saboteur (Ex), 20th level - disabling devices takes half the normal time (1 round becomes a standard action, leaving a move action).
Adventurer	KEY:Rogue ACF ~ Adventurer (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RogueACF.RogueSneakAttack	PRECLASS:1,Rogue=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Adventurer (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.503	DESC:Alternative class feature (rogue, 1st level). A rogue who favors martial training over stealth and cunning (swap): bonus feats as a fighter of her rogue level - at 1st, 2nd and every even level (%1 now; Fighter Feat category). Replaces sneak attack.
Adventurer	KEY:ACF ~ Adventurer (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Rogue Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Fighter Feat|1+floor(RogueLVL/2)	SOURCEPAGE:p.503	DESC:A rogue who favors martial training over stealth and cunning (swap): bonus feats as a fighter of her rogue level - at 1st, 2nd and every even level (%1 now; Fighter Feat category). Replaces sneak attack.|1+floor(RogueLVL/2)
Golarion Rogue	KEY:Rogue ACF ~ Golarion Rogue (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RogueACF.RogueTrapSense	PRECLASS:1,Rogue=3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Golarion Rogue (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.509	DESC:Alternative class feature (rogue, 3rd level). Poison Master (Ex): rogues trained in shadow-shrouded Nidal use poison without any chance of poisoning themselves, and for every three rogue levels beyond 3rd the DC of a poison on their weapons increases by +1 when the target is poisoned as part of a sneak attack (+%1 now). Replaces trap sense.
Golarion Rogue	KEY:ACF ~ Golarion Rogue (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Rogue Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.509	DESC:Poison Master (Ex): rogues trained in shadow-shrouded Nidal use poison without any chance of poisoning themselves, and for every three rogue levels beyond 3rd the DC of a poison on their weapons increases by +1 when the target is poisoned as part of a sneak attack (+%1 now). Replaces trap sense.|max(0,floor((RogueLVL-3)/3))
Lightbringer Strike	KEY:Rogue ACF ~ Lightbringer Strike (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RogueACF.RogueTrapSense	PRECLASS:1,Rogue=3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Lightbringer Strike (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.512	DESC:Alternative class feature (rogue, 3rd level). Whenever you flank a creature immune to sneak attack damage you still deal half your sneak attack dice as bonus damage (%1d6 now); not against creatures you cannot flank, nor merely flat-footed ones. Replaces trap sense.
Lightbringer Strike	KEY:ACF ~ Lightbringer Strike (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Rogue Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.512	DESC:Whenever you flank a creature immune to sneak attack damage you still deal half your sneak attack dice as bonus damage (%1d6 now); not against creatures you cannot flank, nor merely flat-footed ones. Replaces trap sense.|floor(SneakAttackDice/2)
Mimic	KEY:Rogue ACF ~ Mimic (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RogueACF.RogueTrapfinding	PRECLASS:1,Rogue=1	PRESTAT:1,CHA=12	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Mimic (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.513	DESC:Alternative class feature (rogue, 1st level). Masking your appearance at the expense of foiling traps: once per day disguise self as a caster of your class level (applied); at 3rd level and every three levels you can reduce your trap sense bonus by 1 for an additional use (by hand); two uses together produce it as a swift action. Requires Charisma 12. Replaces trapfinding.
Mimic	KEY:ACF ~ Mimic (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Rogue Class Feature	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=1|CASTERLEVEL=RogueLVL|Disguise Self	SOURCEPAGE:p.513	DESC:Masking your appearance at the expense of foiling traps: once per day disguise self as a caster of your class level (applied); at 3rd level and every three levels you can reduce your trap sense bonus by 1 for an additional use (by hand); two uses together produce it as a swift action. Requires Charisma 12. Replaces trapfinding.

###Block: Bard alternative class features
Dead Levels	KEY:Bard ACF ~ Dead Levels (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BardACF.BardDeadLevels	PRECLASS:1,Bard=2	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Bard Dead Levels (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.119	DESC:Alternative class feature (bard, 2nd level). Minor abilities for the bard's dead levels (they replace nothing): Rally Performance (Ex), 2nd level - once per day reroll a Perform check made to earn money (taking the reroll); Refine Performance (Ex), 4th level - considered to have rolled at least 2 on each d10 or d6 for daily Perform earnings, one number higher on each d10 at 5th, 7th, 10th, 11th, 13th, 16th and 17th (at least 3 on each d6 at 7th, 4 at 11th, 5 at 16th), and the maximum at 19th level.
Dead Levels	KEY:ACF ~ Bard Dead Levels (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Bard Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.119	DESC:Minor abilities for the bard's dead levels (they replace nothing): Rally Performance (Ex), 2nd level - once per day reroll a Perform check made to earn money (taking the reroll); Refine Performance (Ex), 4th level - considered to have rolled at least 2 on each d10 or d6 for daily Perform earnings, one number higher on each d10 at 5th, 7th, 10th, 11th, 13th, 16th and 17th (at least 3 on each d6 at 7th, 4 at 11th, 5 at 16th), and the maximum at 19th level.
Fey Bard	KEY:Bard ACF ~ Fey Bard (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BardACF.BardBardicKnowledge.BardInspireCourage.BardInspireCompetence.BardInspireGreatness.BardInspireHeroics	PRECLASS:1,Bard=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Fey Bard (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.120	DESC:Alternative class feature (bard, 1st level). A rare bard with a link to nature and the fey (swap; more aloof and less inspiring than standard bards): animal companion, nature sense, wild empathy and (from 4th level) resist nature's lure, all as the druid of her bard level (applied). Replaces bardic knowledge, inspire courage, inspire competence, inspire greatness and inspire heroics.
Fey Bard	KEY:ACF ~ Fey Bard (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Bard Class Feature	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Nature Sense	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Wild Empathy	BONUS:VAR|WildEmpathyBonus|BardLVL	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Animal Companion	BONUS:VAR|AnimalCompanionLVL|BardLVL	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Resist Nature's Lure|PREVARGTEQ:BardLVL,4	SOURCEPAGE:p.120	DESC:A rare bard with a link to nature and the fey (swap; more aloof and less inspiring than standard bards): animal companion, nature sense, wild empathy and (from 4th level) resist nature's lure, all as the druid of her bard level (applied). Replaces bardic knowledge, inspire courage, inspire competence, inspire greatness and inspire heroics.
Golarion Bard	KEY:Bard ACF ~ Golarion Bard (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BardACF.BardBardicKnowledge	PRECLASS:1,Bard=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Golarion Bard (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.122	DESC:Alternative class feature (bard, 1st level). Specialized Training (Ex): bards of the great schools of the Inner Sea choose a single category of Perform at 1st level; with bardic music using that category they are treated as 2 levels higher for its effects and save DC, and they can use bardic music one additional time per day (by hand). Replaces bardic knowledge.
Golarion Bard	KEY:ACF ~ Golarion Bard (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Bard Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.122	DESC:Specialized Training (Ex): bards of the great schools of the Inner Sea choose a single category of Perform at 1st level; with bardic music using that category they are treated as 2 levels higher for its effects and save DC, and they can use bardic music one additional time per day (by hand). Replaces bardic knowledge.
Inspire Hatred	KEY:Bard ACF ~ Inspire Hatred (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BardACF.BardInspireGreatness	PRECLASS:1,Bard=9	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Inspire Hatred (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.124	DESC:Alternative class feature (bard, 9th level). With 12 ranks in a Perform skill, music, poetics or fiery oratory evoke an unreasoning hatred in %1 living creature(s) within 30 feet with Intelligence 3 or more (one more per three levels beyond 9th) that hear you: Will DC %2 (10 + half your bard level + Charisma modifier) negates; mind-affecting; it lasts while they hear you and 5 rounds more. An affected creature attacks the creature you indicate to the exclusion of others (defending itself if attacked, then resuming); one compelled to attack an ally gets a new save each round. Replaces inspire greatness.
Inspire Hatred	KEY:ACF ~ Inspire Hatred (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Bard Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.124	DESC:With 12 ranks in a Perform skill, music, poetics or fiery oratory evoke an unreasoning hatred in %1 living creature(s) within 30 feet with Intelligence 3 or more (one more per three levels beyond 9th) that hear you: Will DC %2 (10 + half your bard level + Charisma modifier) negates; mind-affecting; it lasts while they hear you and 5 rounds more. An affected creature attacks the creature you indicate to the exclusion of others (defending itself if attacked, then resuming); one compelled to attack an ally gets a new save each round. Replaces inspire greatness.|1+floor((BardLVL-9)/3)|10+floor(BardLVL/2)+CHA
Inspire Turning	KEY:Bard ACF ~ Inspire Turning (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BardACF.BardInspireCompetence	PRECLASS:1,Bard=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Inspire Turning (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.124	DESC:Alternative class feature (bard, 1st level). You spend a daily use of bardic music to help an ally within 30 feet who sees and hears you (and whom you see) turn undead (or destroy undead, for a lightbringer cleric): the ally turns as two levels higher while hearing your performance, up to 2 minutes of concentration; not on yourself. Replaces inspire competence.
Inspire Turning	KEY:ACF ~ Inspire Turning (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Bard Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.124	DESC:You spend a daily use of bardic music to help an ally within 30 feet who sees and hears you (and whom you see) turn undead (or destroy undead, for a lightbringer cleric): the ally turns as two levels higher while hearing your performance, up to 2 minutes of concentration; not on yourself. Replaces inspire competence.
Music of Creation	KEY:Bard ACF ~ Music of Creation (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BardACF.BardMusicOfCreation	PRECLASS:1,Bard=3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Music of Creation (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.125	DESC:Alternative class feature (bard, 3rd level). Eberron bards echo the song with which the Dragon Above sang the world into being: they can take the bardic music feats Haunting Melody, Music of Growth, Music of Making, Song of the Heart and Soothe the Beast whenever they gain a feat, or choose one of them as a bonus feat instead of gaining a new form of bardic music at 3rd, 6th, 9th, 12th, 15th or 18th level (by hand; the feats are in the repository's Eberron data except Soothe the Beast). Replaces nothing (or the forms of bardic music traded).
Music of Creation	KEY:ACF ~ Music of Creation (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Bard Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.125	DESC:Eberron bards echo the song with which the Dragon Above sang the world into being: they can take the bardic music feats Haunting Melody, Music of Growth, Music of Making, Song of the Heart and Soothe the Beast whenever they gain a feat, or choose one of them as a bonus feat instead of gaining a new form of bardic music at 3rd, 6th, 9th, 12th, 15th or 18th level (by hand; the feats are in the repository's Eberron data except Soothe the Beast). Replaces nothing (or the forms of bardic music traded).
Repel Domination	KEY:Bard ACF ~ Repel Domination (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BardACF.BardSuggestion	PRECLASS:1,Bard=6	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Repel Domination (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.126	DESC:Alternative class feature (bard, 6th level). Your study of the undead fortifies your mind: +2 on saves against mind-affecting spells or abilities of undead creatures, and whenever you succeed on such a save the undead that produced it is shaken for the rest of the encounter. Replaces the suggestion bardic music ability.
Repel Domination	KEY:ACF ~ Repel Domination (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Bard Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.126	DESC:Your study of the undead fortifies your mind: +2 on saves against mind-affecting spells or abilities of undead creatures, and whenever you succeed on such a save the undead that produced it is shaken for the rest of the encounter. Replaces the suggestion bardic music ability.
Undead Bardic Knowledge	KEY:Bard ACF ~ Undead Bardic Knowledge (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BardACF.BardBardicKnowledge	PRECLASS:1,Bard=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Undead Bardic Knowledge (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.128	DESC:Alternative class feature (bard, 1st level). Lightbringer bard: a bardic knowledge check (bard level + Intelligence modifier) concerning only the undead, with a +5 circumstance bonus, in addition to a Knowledge (religion) check about undead creatures or lore (items to destroy legendary undead, plagues caused by undead ...). Replaces bardic knowledge.
Undead Bardic Knowledge	KEY:ACF ~ Undead Bardic Knowledge (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Bard Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.128	DESC:Lightbringer bard: a bardic knowledge check (bard level + Intelligence modifier) concerning only the undead, with a +5 circumstance bonus, in addition to a Knowledge (religion) check about undead creatures or lore (items to destroy legendary undead, plagues caused by undead ...). Replaces bardic knowledge.

###Block: Monk alternative class features
Sacred Strike	KEY:Monk ACF ~ Sacred Strike (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.MonkACF.MonkKiStrike.MonkImprovedEvasion	PRECLASS:1,Monk=4	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Sacred Strike (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.374	DESC:Alternative class feature (monk, 4th level). With your deity's favored weapon you smite the sworn enemies of your faith %1 times per day (1 + Wisdom modifier, minimum 1): Charisma bonus on the attack, +1 damage per monk level (+%2); against a creature not an enemy of your faith it has no effect and is spent. Sworn enemies: Heironeous, Moradin, Yondalla - evil creatures; Hextor - good creatures; St. Cuthbert, Wee Jas - chaotic creatures. From 10th level it also stuns for 1 round (Will DC %3 negates); from 16th it stuns and blinds for 1d8 rounds (no save for blindness); creatures immune to critical hits are immune to these. Replaces ki strike and its improvements, and improved evasion.
Sacred Strike	KEY:ACF ~ Sacred Strike (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Monk Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.374	DESC:With your deity's favored weapon you smite the sworn enemies of your faith %1 times per day (1 + Wisdom modifier, minimum 1): Charisma bonus on the attack, +1 damage per monk level (+%2); against a creature not an enemy of your faith it has no effect and is spent. Sworn enemies: Heironeous, Moradin, Yondalla - evil creatures; Hextor - good creatures; St. Cuthbert, Wee Jas - chaotic creatures. From 10th level it also stuns for 1 round (Will DC %3 negates); from 16th it stuns and blinds for 1d8 rounds (no save for blindness); creatures immune to critical hits are immune to these. Replaces ki strike and its improvements, and improved evasion.|max(1,1+WIS)|MonkLVL|10+floor(MonkLVL/2)+WIS
Fighting Styles	KEY:Monk ACF ~ Fighting Styles (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.MonkACF.MonkBonusFeats	PRECLASS:1,Monk=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Fighting Styles (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.360	DESC:Alternative class feature (monk, 1st level). A 1st-level monk may select one of these fighting styles (category below), which dictates her bonus feats at 1st, 2nd and 6th level, gives +2 on checks with one skill, and a bonus ability at 6th level if she meets its prerequisites by then (not later). She can abandon the style by choosing a different bonus feat at 2nd or 6th level, losing the skill bonus and never gaining the bonus ability (by hand). The compendium's fifteen styles are offered here; Unearthed Arcana's eight (Cobra Strike, Denying Stance, Hand and Foot, Invisible Eye, Overwhelming Attack, Passive Way, Sleeping Tiger, Undying Way) are in the repository's Unearthed Arcana data. Replaces the monk's choice of bonus feats.
Fighting Styles	KEY:ACF ~ Fighting Styles (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Monk Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Monk ACF Fighting Styles|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.360	DESC:A 1st-level monk may select one of these fighting styles (category below), which dictates her bonus feats at 1st, 2nd and 6th level, gives +2 on checks with one skill, and a bonus ability at 6th level if she meets its prerequisites by then (not later). She can abandon the style by choosing a different bonus feat at 2nd or 6th level, losing the skill bonus and never gaining the bonus ability (by hand). The compendium's fifteen styles are offered here; Unearthed Arcana's eight (Cobra Strike, Denying Stance, Hand and Foot, Invisible Eye, Overwhelming Attack, Passive Way, Sleeping Tiger, Undying Way) are in the repository's Unearthed Arcana data. Replaces the monk's choice of bonus feats.
Fighting Styles (Buddhist Monk)	KEY:ACF ~ Fighting Styles (DMC) ~ Buddhist Monk	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkACFFightingStyles.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Sense Motive|2|TYPE=FightingStyle	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Iron Will	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Combat Expertise|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,2	SOURCEPAGE:p.360	DESC:Buddhist Monk: +2 on Sense Motive checks; bonus feats Iron Will (1st), Combat Expertise (2nd), Intuitive Attack (6th) - Intuitive Attack by hand (another book or a weapon choice). 6th-level bonus ability (only if its prerequisites are met by 6th level - Concentrations 5 ranks, Sense Motive 9 ranks): mind ability increases to +5.
Fighting Styles (Franciscan Friar)	KEY:ACF ~ Fighting Styles (DMC) ~ Franciscan Friar	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkACFFightingStyles.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Heal|2|TYPE=FightingStyle	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Self-Sufficient	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Diehard|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,6	SOURCEPAGE:p.360	DESC:Franciscan Friar: +2 on Heal checks; bonus feats Self-Sufficient (1st), Vow of Chastity (2nd), Diehard (6th) - Vow of Chastity by hand (another book or a weapon choice). 6th-level bonus ability (only if its prerequisites are met by 6th level - Heal 4 ranks, Survival 4 ranks): gain the ability to cast cure light wounds, purify food and drink, and remove disease once each per day as a spell-like ability (caster level equals half your monk level).
Fighting Styles (Knight Hospitaller)	KEY:ACF ~ Fighting Styles (DMC) ~ Knight Hospitaller	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkACFFightingStyles.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Spot|2|TYPE=FightingStyle	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Combat Expertise|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,2	SOURCEPAGE:p.360	DESC:Knight Hospitaller: +2 on Spot checks; bonus feats Weapon Focus (any) (1st), Combat Expertise (2nd), Weapon Specialization (as Weapon Focus) (6th) - Weapon Focus (any), Weapon Specialization (as Weapon Focus) by hand (another book or a weapon choice). 6th-level bonus ability (only if its prerequisites are met by 6th level - Spot 9 ranks, Combat Reflexes): applies to one adjacent ally of your choice who is not using Combat Expertise.
Fighting Styles (Kyokushinkai Karate)	KEY:ACF ~ Fighting Styles (DMC) ~ Kyokushinkai Karate	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkACFFightingStyles.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Survival|2|TYPE=FightingStyle	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Endurance	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Toughness|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,2	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Weapon Focus(Unarmed Strike)|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,6	SOURCEPAGE:p.360	DESC:Kyokushinkai Karate: +2 on Survival checks; bonus feats Endurance (1st), Toughness (2nd), Weapon Focus (unarmed strike) (6th). 6th-level bonus ability (only if its prerequisites are met by 6th level - Concentration 9 ranks, Die Hard): You permanently gain 6 hit points.
Fighting Styles (Metered Style)	KEY:ACF ~ Fighting Styles (DMC) ~ Metered Style	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkACFFightingStyles.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Concentration|2|TYPE=FightingStyle	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Toughness|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,6	SOURCEPAGE:p.360	DESC:Metered Style: +2 on Concentration checks; bonus feats Defensive Metered Foot (1st), Offensive Metered Foot (2nd), Toughness (6th) - Defensive Metered Foot, Offensive Metered Foot by hand (another book or a weapon choice). 6th-level bonus ability (only if its prerequisites are met by 6th level - Concentration 9 ranks, Skill Focus (any Strength- or Dexterity-based skill)): normally not allow you to do so.
Fighting Styles (Sacred Path of Heironeous)	KEY:ACF ~ Fighting Styles (DMC) ~ Sacred Path of Heironeous	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkACFFightingStyles.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Diplomacy|2|TYPE=FightingStyle	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Endurance	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Negotiator|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,2	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Weapon Specialization(Longsword)|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,6	SOURCEPAGE:p.360	DESC:Sacred Path of Heironeous: +2 on Diplomacy checks; bonus feats Endurance (1st), Negotiator (2nd), Weapon Specialization (longsword) (6th). 6th-level bonus ability (only if its prerequisites are met by 6th level - Diplomacy 4 ranks, proficient with the longsword): When making a flurry of blows attack, you may use a longsword as a monk special weapon.
Fighting Styles (Sacred Path of Hextor)	KEY:ACF ~ Fighting Styles (DMC) ~ Sacred Path of Hextor	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkACFFightingStyles.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Intimidate|2|TYPE=FightingStyle	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Endurance	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Persuasive|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,2	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Weapon Specialization(Flail)|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,6	SOURCEPAGE:p.360	DESC:Sacred Path of Hextor: +2 on Intimidate checks; bonus feats Endurance (1st), Persuasive (2nd), Weapon Specialization (flail) (6th). 6th-level bonus ability (only if its prerequisites are met by 6th level - Intimidate 4 ranks, proficient with the flail): When making a flurry of blows attack, you may use a flail as a monk special weapon.
Fighting Styles (Sacred Path of Moradin)	KEY:ACF ~ Fighting Styles (DMC) ~ Sacred Path of Moradin	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkACFFightingStyles.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Balance|2|TYPE=FightingStyle	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Improved Sunder	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Cleave|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,2	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Diehard|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,6	SOURCEPAGE:p.360	DESC:Sacred Path of Moradin: +2 on Balance checks; bonus feats Improved Sunder (1st), Cleave (2nd), Diehard (6th). 6th-level bonus ability (only if its prerequisites are met by 6th level - Balance 9 ranks, proficient with warharnmer): your monk level.
Fighting Styles (Sacred Path of St. Cuthbert)	KEY:ACF ~ Fighting Styles (DMC) ~ Sacred Path of St. Cuthbert	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkACFFightingStyles.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Survival|2|TYPE=FightingStyle	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Track	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Alertness|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,2	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Power Attack|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,6	SOURCEPAGE:p.360	DESC:Sacred Path of St. Cuthbert: +2 on Survival checks; bonus feats Track (1st), Alertness (2nd), Power Attack (6th). 6th-level bonus ability (only if its prerequisites are met by 6th level - Survival 4 ranks, Spot 9 ranks): Whenever you roll a natural 20 on an attack roll (regardless of whether the attack eventually becomes a critical hit) you strike a blow with such precision that it leaves a small mark on your target. A target bearing this mark takes a -1 penalty on saving throws and a -1 penalty to its Armor Class for a number of rounds equal to one-half your monk level.
Fighting Styles (Sacred Path of Wee Jas)	KEY:ACF ~ Fighting Styles (DMC) ~ Sacred Path of Wee Jas	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkACFFightingStyles.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Use Magic Device|2|TYPE=FightingStyle	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Improved Initiative	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Skill Focus(Use Magic Device)|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,2	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Blind-Fight|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,6	SOURCEPAGE:p.360	DESC:Sacred Path of Wee Jas: +2 on Use Magic Device checks; bonus feats Improved Initiative (1st), Skill Focus (Use Magic Device) (2nd), Blind-Fight (6th). 6th-level bonus ability (only if its prerequisites are met by 6th level - Use Magic Device 4 ranks, Knowledge (religion) 9 ranks): You gain a bonus on Use Magic Device checks equal to one-half your monk level.
Fighting Styles (Sacred Path of Yondalla)	KEY:ACF ~ Fighting Styles (DMC) ~ Sacred Path of Yondalla	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkACFFightingStyles.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Jump|2|TYPE=FightingStyle	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Improved Initiative	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Weapon Finesse|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,2	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Mobility|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,6	SOURCEPAGE:p.360	DESC:Sacred Path of Yondalla: +2 on Jump checks; bonus feats Improved Initiative (1st), Weapon Finesse (2nd), Mobility (6th). 6th-level bonus ability (only if its prerequisites are met by 6th level - Jump 9 ranks, Dodge): the beginning of your next turn.
Fighting Styles (Shinto Monk)	KEY:ACF ~ Fighting Styles (DMC) ~ Shinto Monk	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkACFFightingStyles.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Knowledge (Nature)|2|TYPE=FightingStyle	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Animal Affinity	SOURCEPAGE:p.360	DESC:Shinto Monk: +2 on Knowledge (nature) checks; bonus feats Animal Affinity (1st), Vow of Purity (2nd), Nymph's Kiss (6th) - Vow of Purity, Nymph's Kiss by hand (another book or a weapon choice). 6th-level bonus ability (only if its prerequisites are met by 6th level - Handle Animal 4 ranks, Knowledge (nature) 4 ranks): druid level equals 1/3 your monk level. Levels in multiple classes that provide animal companions stack.
Fighting Styles (Way of The Shackled Beast)	KEY:ACF ~ Fighting Styles (DMC) ~ Way of The Shackled Beast	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkACFFightingStyles.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Jump|2|TYPE=FightingStyle	SOURCEPAGE:p.360	DESC:Way of The Shackled Beast: +2 on Jump checks; bonus feats Fear No Binds (1st), Beast Strike (2nd), Disruptive Strike (6th) - Fear No Binds, Beast Strike, Disruptive Strike by hand (another book or a weapon choice). 6th-level bonus ability (only if its prerequisites are met by 6th level - Jump 9 ranks, Two-Weapon Fighting): You may use your flurry of blows ability at the end of a succesful charge.
Fighting Styles (Wing Chun Kuen)	KEY:ACF ~ Fighting Styles (DMC) ~ Wing Chun Kuen	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkACFFightingStyles.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Listen|2|TYPE=FightingStyle	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Combat Reflexes	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Cleave|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,2	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Improved Critical(Unarmed Strike)|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,6	SOURCEPAGE:p.360	DESC:Wing Chun Kuen: +2 on Listen checks; bonus feats Combat Reflexes (1st), Cleave (2nd), Improved Critical (unarmed strike) (6th). 6th-level bonus ability (only if its prerequisites are met by 6th level - Listen 9 ranks, Improved Initiative): your Wisdom bonus (if any).
Fighting Styles (Wushu)	KEY:ACF ~ Fighting Styles (DMC) ~ Wushu	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkACFFightingStyles.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Tumble|2|TYPE=FightingStyle	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Improved Initiative	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Power Attack|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,2	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Improved Feint|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,6	SOURCEPAGE:p.360	DESC:Wushu: +2 on Tumble checks; bonus feats Improved Initiative (1st), Power Attack (2nd), Improved Feint (6th). 6th-level bonus ability (only if its prerequisites are met by 6th level - Bluff 4 ranks, Sense Motive 9 ranks): half your monk level.
Unwavering Dedication	KEY:Monk ACF ~ Unwavering Dedication (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.MonkACF.MonkStillMind	PRECLASS:1,Monk=3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Unwavering Dedication (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.378	DESC:Alternative class feature (monk, 3rd level). Sacred enforcers may ignore part of the monk multiclass restriction: levels in cleric, paladin or blackguard (by alignment) do not prevent further monk levels, and monk levels do not prevent advancing as a paladin; levels in any other class end monk progression as usual. Replaces still mind.
Unwavering Dedication	KEY:ACF ~ Unwavering Dedication (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Monk Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.378	DESC:Sacred enforcers may ignore part of the monk multiclass restriction: levels in cleric, paladin or blackguard (by alignment) do not prevent further monk levels, and monk levels do not prevent advancing as a paladin; levels in any other class end monk progression as usual. Replaces still mind.
Weapon Proficiencies	KEY:Monk ACF ~ Weapon Proficiencies (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.MonkACF.MonkProficiencies	PRECLASS:1,Monk=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Monk Weapon Proficiencies (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.378	DESC:Alternative class feature (monk, 1st level). Monks from other real-world fighting traditions (choose a style in the category below): each loses proficiency with the kama, nunchaku, sai, shuriken and siangham and gains the style's weapons; the listed special monk weapons can be used with flurry of blows (by hand). Replaces the monk's weapon proficiencies.
Weapon Proficiencies	KEY:ACF ~ Monk Weapon Proficiencies (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Monk Class Feature	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Club|Crossbow (Heavy)|Crossbow (Light)|Dagger|Handaxe|Javelin|Quarterstaff|Sling	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfAuto	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Monk ACF Weapon Proficiencies|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.378	DESC:Monks from other real-world fighting traditions (choose a style in the category below): each loses proficiency with the kama, nunchaku, sai, shuriken and siangham and gains the style's weapons; the listed special monk weapons can be used with flurry of blows (by hand). Replaces the monk's weapon proficiencies.
Weapon Proficiencies (Ghurka)	KEY:ACF ~ Monk Weapon Proficiencies (DMC) ~ Ghurka	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkACFWeaponProficiencies.SpecialQuality	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Kukri|Sword (Short)|Shortbow	SOURCEPAGE:p.378	DESC:The Ghurka monk gains proficiency in the kukri, short sword and shortbow; special monk weapons: kukri, short sword and club.
Weapon Proficiencies (Arnis Kali Escrima)	KEY:ACF ~ Monk Weapon Proficiencies (DMC) ~ Arnis Kali Escrima	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkACFWeaponProficiencies.SpecialQuality	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Sword (Short)|Longsword|Whip	SOURCEPAGE:p.378	DESC:Filipino martial arts (blades and sticks, often in pairs): proficiency in the short sword, longsword and whip; special monk weapons: club, dagger, quarterstaff and short sword.
Weapon Proficiencies (Krabi-Krabong)	KEY:ACF ~ Monk Weapon Proficiencies (DMC) ~ Krabi-Krabong	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkACFWeaponProficiencies.SpecialQuality	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Sword (Short)|Spear|Shortspear	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.378	DESC:Thai weapons-based art: proficiency in the short sword, spear and shortspear (special monk weapons, as are the club and quarterstaff) and in all shields except tower shields (no additional armor proficiency).
Wholeness of Others	KEY:Monk ACF ~ Wholeness of Others (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.MonkACF.MonkWholenessOfBody	PRECLASS:1,Monk=7	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Wholeness of Others (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.379	DESC:Alternative class feature (monk, 7th level). You heal the wounds of others with a touch: %1 hit points per day (twice your class level), divided among several uses and recipients, each a standard action; not yourself. Replaces wholeness of body.
Wholeness of Others	KEY:ACF ~ Wholeness of Others (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Monk Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.379	DESC:You heal the wounds of others with a touch: %1 hit points per day (twice your class level), divided among several uses and recipients, each a standard action; not yourself. Replaces wholeness of body.|2*MonkLVL
Holy Monk	KEY:Monk ACF ~ Holy Monk (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.MonkACF.MonkHolyMonk	PRECLASS:1,Monk=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Holy Monk (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.368	DESC:Alternative class feature (monk, 1st level). Swap: aura of courage (3rd), smite evil, and turn undead (4th, as a paladin - monk level - 3), all as the paladin by monk level (applied). She can multiclass between paladin and monk freely; monk levels stack with paladin levels for smite evil uses and turning level (by hand). Replaces the bonus feats at 1st and 6th level (applied).
Holy Monk	KEY:ACF ~ Holy Monk (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Monk Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Monk Feat LVL 1|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Monk Feat LVL 6|-1|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,6	ABILITY:Paladin Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Paladin ~ Smite Evil	BONUS:VAR|PaladinSmiteEvilLVL|MonkLVL	ABILITY:Paladin Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Paladin ~ Aura of Courage|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Immunity to Fear|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Basic Turning|Turn Undead|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,4	BONUS:VAR|TurnLevelBase,TurnDamagePlusBase|MonkLVL-3|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,4	BONUS:VAR|TurnTimesBase|3+CHA|TYPE=Base|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,4	BONUS:VAR|TurnCheckBase|CHA|TYPE=Base|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,4	SOURCEPAGE:p.368	DESC:Swap: aura of courage (3rd), smite evil, and turn undead (4th, as a paladin - monk level - 3), all as the paladin by monk level (applied). She can multiclass between paladin and monk freely; monk levels stack with paladin levels for smite evil uses and turning level (by hand). Replaces the bonus feats at 1st and 6th level (applied).
Hunter Monk	KEY:Monk ACF ~ Hunter Monk (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.MonkACF.MonkSlowFall	PRECLASS:1,Monk=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Hunter Monk (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.369	DESC:Alternative class feature (monk, 1st level). Swap: favored enemy and swift tracker (8th) as the ranger, by monk level, and Survival as a class skill (applied); she can multiclass between ranger and monk freely, monk levels stacking with ranger levels for new favored enemies (by hand). Replaces the 1st-level bonus feat and slow fall.
Hunter Monk	KEY:ACF ~ Hunter Monk (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Monk Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Monk Feat LVL 1|-1	ABILITY:Ranger Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Ranger ~ Favored Enemy	BONUS:VAR|RangerFavoredEnemyLVL|MonkLVL	ABILITY:Ranger Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Ranger ~ Swift Tracker|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,8	CSKILL:Survival	SOURCEPAGE:p.369	DESC:Swap: favored enemy and swift tracker (8th) as the ranger, by monk level, and Survival as a class skill (applied); she can multiclass between ranger and monk freely, monk levels stacking with ranger levels for new favored enemies (by hand). Replaces the 1st-level bonus feat and slow fall.
Martial Monk	KEY:Monk ACF ~ Martial Monk (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.MonkACF.MonkBonusFeats	PRECLASS:1,Monk=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Martial Monk (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.371	DESC:Alternative class feature (monk, 1st level). Swap: she chooses her bonus feats at 1st, 2nd and 6th level from the fighter bonus feat list (Fighter Feat category; applied) and Intimidate is a class skill (applied); she loses one skill point per level (four at 1st) and Knowledge skills as class skills (by hand); she can multiclass between fighter and monk freely. Replaces the monk bonus feat choices.
Martial Monk	KEY:ACF ~ Martial Monk (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Monk Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Fighter Feat|(MonkLVL>=1)+(MonkLVL>=2)+(MonkLVL>=6)	CSKILL:Intimidate	SOURCEPAGE:p.371	DESC:Swap: she chooses her bonus feats at 1st, 2nd and 6th level from the fighter bonus feat list (Fighter Feat category; applied) and Intimidate is a class skill (applied); she loses one skill point per level (four at 1st) and Knowledge skills as class skills (by hand); she can multiclass between fighter and monk freely. Replaces the monk bonus feat choices.
Raging Monk	KEY:Monk ACF ~ Raging Monk (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.MonkACF.MonkFlurryOfBlows.MonkStillMind.MonkGreaterFlurry.MonkQuiveringPalm	PRECLASS:1,Monk=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Raging Monk (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.374	DESC:Alternative class feature (monk, 1st level). Swap: rage, greater rage (11th) and mighty rage (20th) as the barbarian, by monk level (applied). If she becomes chaotic and takes barbarian levels she keeps them and adds monk levels to barbarian levels for rage uses and improvements (by hand). Replaces flurry of blows, still mind, greater flurry and quivering palm.
Raging Monk	KEY:ACF ~ Raging Monk (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Monk Class Feature	ABILITY:Barbarian Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Barbarian ~ Rage	BONUS:VAR|BarbarianRageTimesLVL,BarbarianRagePowerLVL,RageTimesLVL,RagePowerLVL|MonkLVL	SOURCEPAGE:p.374	DESC:Swap: rage, greater rage (11th) and mighty rage (20th) as the barbarian, by monk level (applied). If she becomes chaotic and takes barbarian levels she keeps them and adds monk levels to barbarian levels for rage uses and improvements (by hand). Replaces flurry of blows, still mind, greater flurry and quivering palm.
Steadfast Monk	KEY:Monk ACF ~ Steadfast Monk (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.MonkACF.MonkFastMovement.MonkACBonus	PRECLASS:1,Monk=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Steadfast Monk (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.378	DESC:Alternative class feature (monk, 1st level). Swap: damage reduction as the barbarian (1/- at 7th level, +1 every three levels; %1/- now; applied). She keeps her Wisdom bonus to AC when unarmored and unencumbered (applied). Replaces the enhancement bonus to unarmored speed and the level-based AC bonus.
Steadfast Monk	KEY:ACF ~ Steadfast Monk (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Monk Class Feature	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|max(WIS,0)|PREVAREQ:ENCUMBERANCE,0,var("COUNT[EQTYPE.ARMOR.EQUIPPED]"),0	DEFINE:SteadfastMonkDR|0	BONUS:VAR|SteadfastMonkDR|floor((MonkLVL-4)/3)|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,7	DR:SteadfastMonkDR/-|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,7	SOURCEPAGE:p.378	DESC:Swap: damage reduction as the barbarian (1/- at 7th level, +1 every three levels; %1/- now; applied). She keeps her Wisdom bonus to AC when unarmored and unencumbered (applied). Replaces the enhancement bonus to unarmored speed and the level-based AC bonus.|max(0,floor((MonkLVL-4)/3))
Vigilant Monk	KEY:Monk ACF ~ Vigilant Monk (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.MonkACF.MonkStillMind	PRECLASS:1,Monk=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Vigilant Monk (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.378	DESC:Alternative class feature (monk, 1st level). Swap: detect chaos at will as the paladin's detect evil, uncanny dodge (2nd) and improved uncanny dodge (5th) as the barbarian, by monk level (applied). Replaces the bonus feats at 2nd and 6th level (applied) and still mind.
Vigilant Monk	KEY:ACF ~ Vigilant Monk (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Monk Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Monk Feat LVL 2|-1|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,2	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Monk Feat LVL 6|-1|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,6	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=ATWILL|CASTERLEVEL=MonkLVL|Detect Chaos	ABILITY:Barbarian Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Barbarian ~ Uncanny Dodge|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,2	BONUS:VAR|UncannyDodgeFlankingLevel|MonkLVL|TYPE=EachClass.REPLACE|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,2	ABILITY:Barbarian Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Barbarian ~ Improved Uncanny Dodge|PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,5	SOURCEPAGE:p.378	DESC:Swap: detect chaos at will as the paladin's detect evil, uncanny dodge (2nd) and improved uncanny dodge (5th) as the barbarian, by monk level (applied). Replaces the bonus feats at 2nd and 6th level (applied) and still mind.
Aquatic Monk	KEY:Monk ACF ~ Aquatic Monk (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.MonkACF.MonkFastMovement	PRECLASS:1,Monk=1	PREMOVE:1,Swim=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Aquatic Monk (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.355	DESC:Alternative class feature (monk, 1st level). A monk with a racial swim speed applies his fast movement bonus (+%1 feet now) to his swim speed instead of his land speed (applied; only with no armor and a light load), chosen when the feature is gained. Replaces fast movement on land.
Aquatic Monk	KEY:ACF ~ Aquatic Monk (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Monk Class Feature	BONUS:MOVEADD|TYPE.Swim|floor(MonkLVL/3)*10|TYPE=Enhancement|PREVAREQ:ENCUMBERANCE,0,var("COUNT[EQTYPE.ARMOR.EQUIPPED]"),0	SOURCEPAGE:p.355	DESC:A monk with a racial swim speed applies his fast movement bonus (+%1 feet now) to his swim speed instead of his land speed (applied; only with no armor and a light load), chosen when the feature is gained. Replaces fast movement on land.|floor(MonkLVL/3)*10
Aquatic Monk (Water Step)	KEY:Monk ACF ~ Aquatic Monk (Water Step) (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.MonkACF.MonkSlowFall	PRECLASS:1,Monk=4	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Aquatic Monk (Water Step) (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.355	DESC:Alternative class feature (monk, 4th level). Water Step (Ex): he walks across short distances of water, up to the slow fall distance he would otherwise have (%1 feet now: 20 at 4th level, +10 every two levels, 90 at 18th), divisible between two consecutive turns if he begins or ends each turn on solid ground; beyond it he falls in. Replaces slow fall.
Aquatic Monk (Water Step)	KEY:ACF ~ Aquatic Monk (Water Step) (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Monk Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.355	DESC:Water Step (Ex): he walks across short distances of water, up to the slow fall distance he would otherwise have (%1 feet now: 20 at 4th level, +10 every two levels, 90 at 18th), divisible between two consecutive turns if he begins or ends each turn on solid ground; beyond it he falls in. Replaces slow fall.|min(90,20+10*floor((MonkLVL-4)/2))
Bane of the Clockwork	KEY:Monk ACF ~ Bane of the Clockwork (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.MonkACF.MonkSlowFall.MonkBonusFeat6	PRECLASS:1,Monk=3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Bane of the Clockwork (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.355	DESC:Alternative class feature (monk, 3rd level). Intimately aware of a construct's flaws: you deal critical hit damage against constructs with unarmed strikes (not monk special weapons), and constructs are no longer immune to your Stunning Fist or quivering palm. Replaces slow fall and the 6th-level bonus feat.
