Warrior of Water	KEY:Fighter ACF ~ Warrior of Water (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.FighterACF.FighterWarriorOfWater	PRECLASS:1,Fighter=2	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Warrior of Water (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.293	DESC:Alternative class feature (fighter, 2nd level). You are linked with the elemental power of water: cold resistance %1 (5 at 2nd level, 10 at 12th, 20 at 20th); from 6th level obscuring mist 3/day as a spell-like ability (caster level your fighter level); extra cold damage on a successful critical hit with an unarmed strike or melee weapon (+1d6 at 6th, +2d6 at 12th, +3d6 at 20th); water breathing three times per day at 12th level and at will at 20th (all applied as spell-like abilities). Replaces the fighter bonus feats at 2nd, 6th, 12th and 20th level (applied).
Warrior of Water	KEY:ACF ~ Warrior of Water (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	BONUS:VAR|Pool_FighterFeat|-((FighterLVL>=2)+(FighterLVL>=6)+(FighterLVL>=12)+(FighterLVL>=20))	BONUS:VAR|ColdResistanceBonus|5+5*(FighterLVL>=12)+10*(FighterLVL>=20)	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=3|CASTERLEVEL=FighterLVL|Obscuring Mist|PREVARGTEQ:FighterLVL,6	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=3|CASTERLEVEL=FighterLVL|Water Breathing|PREVARGTEQ:FighterLVL,12|PREVARLT:FighterLVL,20	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=ATWILL|CASTERLEVEL=FighterLVL|Water Breathing|PREVARGTEQ:FighterLVL,20	SOURCEPAGE:p.293	DESC:You are linked with the elemental power of water: cold resistance %1 (5 at 2nd level, 10 at 12th, 20 at 20th); from 6th level obscuring mist 3/day as a spell-like ability (caster level your fighter level); extra cold damage on a successful critical hit with an unarmed strike or melee weapon (+1d6 at 6th, +2d6 at 12th, +3d6 at 20th); water breathing three times per day at 12th level and at will at 20th (all applied as spell-like abilities). Replaces the fighter bonus feats at 2nd, 6th, 12th and 20th level (applied).|5+5*(FighterLVL>=12)+10*(FighterLVL>=20)
Janissary	KEY:Fighter ACF ~ Janissary (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.FighterACF.FighterJanissary	PRECLASS:1,Fighter=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Janissary (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.285	DESC:Alternative class feature (fighter, 1st level). Modeled on the Ottoman janissaries - conscripted children raised as fiercely loyal warriors, learned in arts beyond the martial and often speaking strange tongues; usually lawful. Speak Language and two Knowledge skills of his choice become class skills (applied); Handle Animal, Intimidate and Swim become cross-class skills (by hand - class skills cannot be removed by an alternative class feature in PCGen). The compendium prints only these class skill changes from the janissary article; appropriate feats include Blind-Fight, Combat Expertise, Improved Disarm, Improved Sunder and Combat Engineer.
Janissary	KEY:ACF ~ Janissary (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	CSKILL:Speak Language	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Janissary Knowledge Skills	SOURCEPAGE:p.285	DESC:Modeled on the Ottoman janissaries - conscripted children raised as fiercely loyal warriors, learned in arts beyond the martial and often speaking strange tongues; usually lawful. Speak Language and two Knowledge skills of his choice become class skills (applied); Handle Animal, Intimidate and Swim become cross-class skills (by hand - class skills cannot be removed by an alternative class feature in PCGen). The compendium prints only these class skill changes from the janissary article; appropriate feats include Blind-Fight, Combat Expertise, Improved Disarm, Improved Sunder and Combat Engineer.

###Block: Barbarian alternative class features
Wasteland Barbarian	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Wasteland Barbarian (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianImprovedUncannyDodge	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Wasteland Barbarian (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.112	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 3rd level). Barbarians at home in the waste (Sandstorm's variant): Wastelands Trap Sense (Su), 3rd level - the trap sense bonus applies to Reflex saves and AC against natural hazards of the wastes (lava pools, slipsand, softsand ...) instead of traps. Bonus Feat, 5th level - one of Blazing Berserker, Endurance, Great Fortitude, Heat Endurance, Improved Heat Endurance, Judged by Aurifar, Sandskimmer, Scorpion's Resolve or Self-Sufficient, prerequisites applying (category below; only Endurance, Great Fortitude and Self-Sufficient are in the repository - the Sandstorm feats by hand); replaces improved uncanny dodge. Wastelands Damage Reduction (Su), 8th level - damage reduction 1/- against wasteland creatures and hazards, stacking with his normal damage reduction; replaces the rage use gained at 8th level - from then on one fewer rage per day (applied).
Wasteland Barbarian	KEY:ACF ~ Wasteland Barbarian (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	BONUS:VAR|RageTimes|-1|PREVARGTEQ:BarbarianLVL,8	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Barbarian ACF Wasteland Barbarian|(BarbarianLVL>=5)	SOURCEPAGE:p.112	DESC:Barbarians at home in the waste (Sandstorm's variant): Wastelands Trap Sense (Su), 3rd level - the trap sense bonus applies to Reflex saves and AC against natural hazards of the wastes (lava pools, slipsand, softsand ...) instead of traps. Bonus Feat, 5th level - one of Blazing Berserker, Endurance, Great Fortitude, Heat Endurance, Improved Heat Endurance, Judged by Aurifar, Sandskimmer, Scorpion's Resolve or Self-Sufficient, prerequisites applying (category below; only Endurance, Great Fortitude and Self-Sufficient are in the repository - the Sandstorm feats by hand); replaces improved uncanny dodge. Wastelands Damage Reduction (Su), 8th level - damage reduction 1/- against wasteland creatures and hazards, stacking with his normal damage reduction; replaces the rage use gained at 8th level - from then on one fewer rage per day (applied).
Wasteland Barbarian (Endurance)	KEY:ACF ~ Wasteland Barbarian (DMC) ~ Endurance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:BarbarianACFWastelandBarbarian.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Endurance	SOURCEPAGE:p.112	DESC:Wasteland barbarian bonus feat (5th level).
Wasteland Barbarian (Great Fortitude)	KEY:ACF ~ Wasteland Barbarian (DMC) ~ Great Fortitude	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:BarbarianACFWastelandBarbarian.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Great Fortitude	SOURCEPAGE:p.112	DESC:Wasteland barbarian bonus feat (5th level).
Wasteland Barbarian (Self-Sufficient)	KEY:ACF ~ Wasteland Barbarian (DMC) ~ Self-Sufficient	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:BarbarianACFWastelandBarbarian.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Self-Sufficient	SOURCEPAGE:p.112	DESC:Wasteland barbarian bonus feat (5th level).

###Block: Sorcerer alternative class features
Familiars	KEY:Sorcerer ACF ~ Familiars (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SorcererACF.SorcererFamiliarList	PRECLASS:1,Sorcerer=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Sorcerer Familiars (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.672	DESC:Alternative class feature (sorcerer, 1st level). The compendium's compilation of all creatures eligible as familiars (pp. 672-678, by minimum spellcaster level, with equivalent statistics, requirements and master benefits). Offered here in addition to the familiars already in the repository: dog (1st; master +3 on Sense Motive checks); leopard, wolverine and Medium viper (1st, for a Huge or larger master; master +2 on Move Silently, +2 on Reflex saves, +3 on Bluff checks); with Improved Familiar: badger, Medium and Large viper (3rd), Small air, earth, fire and water elementals (5th - with Complete Mage, which defines them: dmc_acf_completemage.lst). Master benefits of these creatures by hand. Creatures with equivalent statistics (caterpillar as mouse, rabbit as cat, vulture as hawk ...) use their equivalent's familiar entry; creatures not in the repository (albatross, arctic fox, ferret, lynx, worg ...) by hand. Replaces nothing.
Familiars	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer Familiars (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Sorcerer Class Feature	COMPANIONLIST:Familiar|Companion ~ Dog	COMPANIONLIST:Familiar|Companion ~ Leopard,Companion ~ Wolverine,Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Medium)|PRESIZEGTEQ:H	COMPANIONLIST:Familiar|Companion ~ Badger,Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Medium),Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Large)|PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Improved Familiar|PRECLASS:1,SPELLCASTER.Arcane=3	SOURCEPAGE:p.672	DESC:The compendium's compilation of all creatures eligible as familiars (pp. 672-678, by minimum spellcaster level, with equivalent statistics, requirements and master benefits). Offered here in addition to the familiars already in the repository: dog (1st; master +3 on Sense Motive checks); leopard, wolverine and Medium viper (1st, for a Huge or larger master; master +2 on Move Silently, +2 on Reflex saves, +3 on Bluff checks); with Improved Familiar: badger, Medium and Large viper (3rd), Small air, earth, fire and water elementals (5th - with Complete Mage, which defines them: dmc_acf_completemage.lst). Master benefits of these creatures by hand. Creatures with equivalent statistics (caterpillar as mouse, rabbit as cat, vulture as hawk ...) use their equivalent's familiar entry; creatures not in the repository (albatross, arctic fox, ferret, lynx, worg ...) by hand. Replaces nothing.
Aligned Spellcaster	KEY:Sorcerer ACF ~ Aligned Spellcaster (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SorcererACF.SorcererFamiliar.SorcererSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Sorcerer=1	PREALIGN:LG,LN,LE,NG,NE,CG,CN,CE	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Sorcerer Aligned Spellcaster (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.563	DESC:Alternative class feature (sorcerer, 1st level). Choose a non-neutral alignment component you have: your spells gain that alignment descriptor unless they already have the opposite one (a neutral good caster casts all non-evil spells as good spells). Spells you cast that target creatures of the opposite alignment are cast at +1 caster level (+2 against creatures with the opposite alignment as a subtype); area and other untargeted spells gain no bonus. A true neutral caster cannot take it. (Also for wizards, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
Aligned Spellcaster	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer Aligned Spellcaster (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Sorcerer Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.563	DESC:Choose a non-neutral alignment component you have: your spells gain that alignment descriptor unless they already have the opposite one (a neutral good caster casts all non-evil spells as good spells). Spells you cast that target creatures of the opposite alignment are cast at +1 caster level (+2 against creatures with the opposite alignment as a subtype); area and other untargeted spells gain no bonus. A true neutral caster cannot take it. (Also for wizards, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
Arcane Reabsorption	KEY:Sorcerer ACF ~ Arcane Reabsorption (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SorcererACF.SorcererFamiliar.SorcererSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Sorcerer=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Sorcerer Arcane Reabsorption (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.563	DESC:Alternative class feature (sorcerer, 1st level). Whenever a targeted spell you cast fails to penetrate a creature's spell resistance or is countered, and has no effect at all, you can attempt to reabsorb it as an immediate action: a Spellcraft check (DC 20 + 3 x spell level) regains the spell or spell slot as if never cast; either way you take 1 point of nonlethal damage per spell level, bypassing damage reduction and resistances. (Also for wizards, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
Arcane Reabsorption	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer Arcane Reabsorption (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Sorcerer Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.563	DESC:Whenever a targeted spell you cast fails to penetrate a creature's spell resistance or is countered, and has no effect at all, you can attempt to reabsorb it as an immediate action: a Spellcraft check (DC 20 + 3 x spell level) regains the spell or spell slot as if never cast; either way you take 1 point of nonlethal damage per spell level, bypassing damage reduction and resistances. (Also for wizards, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
Beleaguered Spellcaster	KEY:Sorcerer ACF ~ Beleaguered Spellcaster (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SorcererACF.SorcererFamiliar.SorcererSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Sorcerer=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Sorcerer Beleaguered Spellcaster (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.564	DESC:Alternative class feature (sorcerer, 1st level). Whenever you take damage equal to 3 x your spellcaster level (%1) from one attack, the next spell you cast is automatically maximized or extended (your choice) without increasing its level or casting time; %2 times per day (1 + Charisma modifier). (Also for wizards, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
Beleaguered Spellcaster	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer Beleaguered Spellcaster (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Sorcerer Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.564	DESC:Whenever you take damage equal to 3 x your spellcaster level (%1) from one attack, the next spell you cast is automatically maximized or extended (your choice) without increasing its level or casting time; %2 times per day (1 + Charisma modifier). (Also for wizards, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.|3*SorcererLVL|1+CHA
Blood of Eberron	KEY:Sorcerer ACF ~ Blood of Eberron (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SorcererACF.SorcererFamiliar.SorcererSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Sorcerer=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Blood of Eberron (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.564	DESC:Alternative class feature (sorcerer, 1st level). A bond to Eberron, the Dragon Between, mother of natural creatures: your sorcerer class skills are Concentration, Craft, Diplomacy, Handle Animal, Heal, Knowledge (arcana), Knowledge (nature), Profession and Spellcraft (the new ones applied; Bluff no longer a class skill - by hand); an animal companion as a druid of half your sorcerer level (druid, ranger and sorcerer levels stack; applied); Natural Spell works in any animal form (wild shape, polymorph ...). Replaces the normal class skill list and the familiar.
Blood of Eberron	KEY:ACF ~ Blood of Eberron (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Sorcerer Class Feature	CSKILL:Diplomacy|Handle Animal|Heal|Knowledge (Nature)	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Animal Companion	BONUS:VAR|AnimalCompanionLVL|floor(SorcererLVL/2)	SOURCEPAGE:p.564	DESC:A bond to Eberron, the Dragon Between, mother of natural creatures: your sorcerer class skills are Concentration, Craft, Diplomacy, Handle Animal, Heal, Knowledge (arcana), Knowledge (nature), Profession and Spellcraft (the new ones applied; Bluff no longer a class skill - by hand); an animal companion as a druid of half your sorcerer level (druid, ranger and sorcerer levels stack; applied); Natural Spell works in any animal form (wild shape, polymorph ...). Replaces the normal class skill list and the familiar.
Blood of Khyber	KEY:Sorcerer ACF ~ Blood of Khyber (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SorcererACF.SorcererFamiliar.SorcererSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Sorcerer=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Blood of Khyber (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.565	DESC:Alternative class feature (sorcerer, 1st level). A bond to Khyber, the Dragon Below: your sorcerer class skills are Bluff, Concentration, Craft, Intimidate, Knowledge (arcana), Knowledge (dungeoneering), Profession and Spellcraft (applied); +1 caster level for conjuration (summoning) and transmutation spells, -1 (minimum 1st) for abjuration and divination spells (applied); you cannot summon any creature of good alignment. Replaces the normal class skill list and the familiar.
Blood of Khyber	KEY:ACF ~ Blood of Khyber (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Sorcerer Class Feature	CSKILL:Intimidate|Knowledge (Dungeoneering)	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SUBSCHOOL.Summoning,SCHOOL.Transmutation|1	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Abjuration,SCHOOL.Divination|-1	SOURCEPAGE:p.565	DESC:A bond to Khyber, the Dragon Below: your sorcerer class skills are Bluff, Concentration, Craft, Intimidate, Knowledge (arcana), Knowledge (dungeoneering), Profession and Spellcraft (applied); +1 caster level for conjuration (summoning) and transmutation spells, -1 (minimum 1st) for abjuration and divination spells (applied); you cannot summon any creature of good alignment. Replaces the normal class skill list and the familiar.
Blood of Siberys	KEY:Sorcerer ACF ~ Blood of Siberys (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SorcererACF.SorcererFamiliar.SorcererSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Sorcerer=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Blood of Siberys (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.565	DESC:Alternative class feature (sorcerer, 1st level). A bond to Siberys, the Dragon Above, source of arcane magic: your sorcerer class skills are Bluff, Concentration, Craft, Diplomacy, Knowledge (arcana), Knowledge (the planes), Profession and Spellcraft (applied); +4 to your effective Charisma only for bonus sorcerer spells and the maximum spell level you can cast (with Charisma 14 you can still cast 8th-level spells) - not for save DCs, skills or anything else (by hand). Replaces the normal class skill list and the familiar.
Blood of Siberys	KEY:ACF ~ Blood of Siberys (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Sorcerer Class Feature	CSKILL:Diplomacy|Knowledge (The Planes)	SOURCEPAGE:p.565	DESC:A bond to Siberys, the Dragon Above, source of arcane magic: your sorcerer class skills are Bluff, Concentration, Craft, Diplomacy, Knowledge (arcana), Knowledge (the planes), Profession and Spellcraft (applied); +4 to your effective Charisma only for bonus sorcerer spells and the maximum spell level you can cast (with Charisma 14 you can still cast 8th-level spells) - not for save DCs, skills or anything else (by hand). Replaces the normal class skill list and the familiar.
Dead Levels	KEY:Sorcerer ACF ~ Dead Levels (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SorcererACF.SorcererDeadLevels	PRECLASS:1,Sorcerer=2	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Sorcerer Dead Levels (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.565	DESC:Alternative class feature (sorcerer, 2nd level). Magical Affinity (Ex), from 2nd level: he identifies one chosen creature type that includes creatures with arcane spell-like abilities (dragon, magical beast, outsider ...) - the type of his magical heritage, chosen once - with a +%1 bonus on Knowledge (arcana) checks to identify such creatures (+2 at 2nd level, +1 per sorcerer level after), untrained; no insight into their powers or vulnerabilities. Replaces nothing.
Dead Levels	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer Dead Levels (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Sorcerer Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.565	DESC:Magical Affinity (Ex), from 2nd level: he identifies one chosen creature type that includes creatures with arcane spell-like abilities (dragon, magical beast, outsider ...) - the type of his magical heritage, chosen once - with a +%1 bonus on Knowledge (arcana) checks to identify such creatures (+2 at 2nd level, +1 per sorcerer level after), untrained; no insight into their powers or vulnerabilities. Replaces nothing.|SorcererLVL
Disciple of Boccob	KEY:Sorcerer ACF ~ Disciple of Boccob (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SorcererACF.SorcererFamiliar.SorcererSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Sorcerer=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Sorcerer Disciple of Boccob (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.565	DESC:Alternative class feature (sorcerer, 1st level). A pious student of Boccob the Uncaring: you qualify for item creation feats as a character one level higher, and magic items you create are crafted at +1 caster level at no extra cost; if you destroy a permanent magic item you lose all arcane spellcasting for one day per caster level of the item. (Also for wizards, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
Disciple of Boccob	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer Disciple of Boccob (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Sorcerer Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.565	DESC:A pious student of Boccob the Uncaring: you qualify for item creation feats as a character one level higher, and magic items you create are crafted at +1 caster level at no extra cost; if you destroy a permanent magic item you lose all arcane spellcasting for one day per caster level of the item. (Also for wizards, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
Draconic Ray	KEY:Sorcerer ACF ~ Draconic Ray (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SorcererACF.SorcererFamiliar.SorcererSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Sorcerer=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Draconic Ray (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.566	DESC:Alternative class feature (sorcerer, 1st level). Draconic Ray (Su): once per day, a ray as a spell-like ability (ranged touch attack, range %1 feet = 25 + 5 per 2 sorcerer levels) dealing 1d4+%2 points of damage of the energy of your ancestral dragon kind (chosen at 1st level, category below; the same as for Draconic Heritage), and the target must save (DC %3 = 10 + 1 per 2 sorcerer levels + Charisma modifier) or suffer the secondary effect (caster level half your sorcerer level). Optional rule - check with your DM. Replaces the familiar permanently.
Draconic Ray	KEY:ACF ~ Draconic Ray (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Sorcerer Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Sorcerer ACF Draconic Ray|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.566	DESC:Draconic Ray (Su): once per day, a ray as a spell-like ability (ranged touch attack, range %1 feet = 25 + 5 per 2 sorcerer levels) dealing 1d4+%2 points of damage of the energy of your ancestral dragon kind (chosen at 1st level, category below; the same as for Draconic Heritage), and the target must save (DC %3 = 10 + 1 per 2 sorcerer levels + Charisma modifier) or suffer the secondary effect (caster level half your sorcerer level). Optional rule - check with your DM. Replaces the familiar permanently.|25+5*floor(SorcererLVL/2)|SorcererLVL|10+floor(SorcererLVL/2)+CHA
Draconic Ray (Black Dragon)	KEY:ACF ~ Draconic Ray (DMC) ~ Black Dragon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFDraconicRay.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.566	DESC:Ancestral black dragon: the ray deals acid damage; secondary effect shadow eyes (Will save negates): shadows shroud its eyes for 1d6 rounds: everything has concealment (20% miss chance) for it; blindsight and similar senses ignore this.
Draconic Ray (Blue Dragon)	KEY:ACF ~ Draconic Ray (DMC) ~ Blue Dragon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFDraconicRay.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.566	DESC:Ancestral blue dragon: the ray deals electricity damage; secondary effect dehydration (Fortitude save negates): it takes an additional 1d4 nonlethal damage per 2 sorcerer levels.
Draconic Ray (Green Dragon)	KEY:ACF ~ Draconic Ray (DMC) ~ Green Dragon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFDraconicRay.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.566	DESC:Ancestral green dragon: the ray deals acid damage; secondary effect command (Will save negates): it is affected by the command spell.
Draconic Ray (Red Dragon)	KEY:ACF ~ Draconic Ray (DMC) ~ Red Dragon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFDraconicRay.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.566	DESC:Ancestral red dragon: the ray deals fire damage; secondary effect burning (Reflex save negates): it catches on fire, taking 1d4 damage per round for 1 round per 2 sorcerer levels.
Draconic Ray (White Dragon)	KEY:ACF ~ Draconic Ray (DMC) ~ White Dragon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFDraconicRay.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.566	DESC:Ancestral white dragon: the ray deals cold damage; secondary effect rime of ice (Reflex save negates): a rime of ice for 1 round: it drops whatever it holds and falls prone.
Draconic Ray (Brass Dragon)	KEY:ACF ~ Draconic Ray (DMC) ~ Brass Dragon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFDraconicRay.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.566	DESC:Ancestral brass dragon: the ray deals fire damage; secondary effect sleep (Will save negates): it falls asleep for 1d6 rounds.
Draconic Ray (Bronze Dragon)	KEY:ACF ~ Draconic Ray (DMC) ~ Bronze Dragon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFDraconicRay.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.566	DESC:Ancestral bronze dragon: the ray deals electricity damage; secondary effect fear (Will save negates): it becomes panicked for 1d4 rounds.
Draconic Ray (Copper Dragon)	KEY:ACF ~ Draconic Ray (DMC) ~ Copper Dragon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFDraconicRay.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.566	DESC:Ancestral copper dragon: the ray deals acid damage; secondary effect slow (Fortitude save negates): it is slowed for 1d6 rounds.
Draconic Ray (Gold Dragon)	KEY:ACF ~ Draconic Ray (DMC) ~ Gold Dragon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFDraconicRay.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.566	DESC:Ancestral gold dragon: the ray deals fire damage; secondary effect weakening (Fortitude save negates): a 1d4 Strength penalty for 1 round per 2 sorcerer levels.
Draconic Ray (Silver Dragon)	KEY:ACF ~ Draconic Ray (DMC) ~ Silver Dragon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFDraconicRay.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.566	DESC:Ancestral silver dragon: the ray deals cold damage; secondary effect hold person (Will save negates): it is held, as hold person, for 1d4 rounds.
Focus Caster	KEY:Sorcerer ACF ~ Focus Caster (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SorcererACF.SorcererFamiliar.SorcererSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Sorcerer=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Sorcerer Focus Caster (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.569	DESC:Alternative class feature (sorcerer, 1st level). Instead of a familiar you bind yourself (24-hour ritual, 100 gp) to a masterwork item that is a focus for all your spells - held, wielded or worn in addition to their normal components - and enhances one school (category below; a specialist wizard only her specialty). You are proficient with that item (not others of its kind); its hardness increases by half your caster level and its hit points by your caster level (up to double); enhancing it costs you 10%% less XP. If destroyed, you must bind another masterwork, non-magic item. Bonuses stack with Spell Focus and Spell Penetration. (Also for wizards, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
Focus Caster	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer Focus Caster (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Sorcerer Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Sorcerer ACF Focus Caster|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.569	DESC:Instead of a familiar you bind yourself (24-hour ritual, 100 gp) to a masterwork item that is a focus for all your spells - held, wielded or worn in addition to their normal components - and enhances one school (category below; a specialist wizard only her specialty). You are proficient with that item (not others of its kind); its hardness increases by half your caster level and its hit points by your caster level (up to double); enhancing it costs you 10%% less XP. If destroyed, you must bind another masterwork, non-magic item. Bonuses stack with Spell Focus and Spell Penetration. (Also for wizards, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
Focus Caster (Abjuration)	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer Focus Caster (DMC) ~ Abjuration	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFFocusCaster.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.569	DESC:Usually bracers, a buckler or a small shield: nonpersonal abjuration spells with one or more targets gain one additional target, affected for half the duration (full duration from 7th level); from 15th, personal abjuration spells can be cast as touch spells.
Focus Caster (Conjuration)	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer Focus Caster (DMC) ~ Conjuration	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFFocusCaster.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.569	DESC:Usually a gnarled quarterstaff or other polearm: conjuration spells last 1 round longer (2 at 7th, 3 at 15th); concentration spells also continue that long after you stop concentrating.
Focus Caster (Divination)	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer Focus Caster (DMC) ~ Divination	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFFocusCaster.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Divination|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.569	DESC:Usually a large crystal or an ornate holy symbol: +1 caster level for divination spells (applied); from 7th level divination durations double; from 15th a bonus to resist divinations equal to 1 + Intelligence modifier (minimum +1).
Focus Caster (Enchantment)	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer Focus Caster (DMC) ~ Enchantment	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFFocusCaster.SpecialQuality	BONUS:DC|SCHOOL.Enchantment|2|PREVARGTEQ:SorcererLVL,15	SOURCEPAGE:p.569	DESC:Usually an ornate, nonfunctional piece of clothing (sash, hair ribbon): enchantment spells last 1 round longer (2 at 7th); concentration spells also continue that long after you stop; from 15th level +2 to the DC of your enchantment spells (applied).
Focus Caster (Evocation)	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer Focus Caster (DMC) ~ Evocation	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFFocusCaster.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.569	DESC:Usually a bladed weapon (longsword, dagger): +1 damage on evocation spells (a single target of multi-target spells such as magic missile); from 7th level they ignore the first 5 points of energy resistance (not immunity); from 15th, once per day, ignore a creature's immunity with an evocation spell.
Focus Caster (Illusion)	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer Focus Caster (DMC) ~ Illusion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFFocusCaster.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Illusion|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.569	DESC:Usually a mask, shroud or cloak: +1 caster level for illusion spells (applied); from 7th level a bonus equal to half your caster level on caster level checks against spell resistance with illusions; from 15th, personal illusion spells can be cast as touch spells.
Focus Caster (Necromancy)	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer Focus Caster (DMC) ~ Necromancy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFFocusCaster.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.569	DESC:Usually a flail, kama, sickle or scythe: +25% range for necromancy spells; from 7th level spells dealing ability damage or drain or an ability penalty deal 1 more; from 15th, living creatures failing the Fortitude save against your necromancy spells also become fatigued.
Focus Caster (Transmutation)	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer Focus Caster (DMC) ~ Transmutation	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFFocusCaster.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.569	DESC:Usually tools of creation (thieves' tools, a musical instrument, artisan's tools): nonpersonal transmutation spells with one or more targets gain one additional target for half the duration (full duration from 7th level); from 15th, once per day, a transmutation spell granting an ability bonus doubles it.
Githyanki Sorcerer	KEY:Sorcerer ACF ~ Githyanki Sorcerer (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SorcererACF.SorcererFamiliar.SorcererSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Sorcerer=1	PRERACE:1,Githyanki%	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Githyanki Sorcerer (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.570	DESC:Alternative class feature (sorcerer, 1st level). The path of the duthka'ariy: githyanki sorcerers manifest their infernal draconic heritage (from the interbreeding of githyanki and fiendish red dragons) and can never acquire a familiar. Natural Weapons - Improved Unarmed Strike; Keen Senses (1st-4th) - Alertness; Natural Armor (5th-8th) - +1 natural armor; Keen Senses (9th-12th) - darkvision 120 feet; Fire Focus (13th-16th) - fire spells at +1 caster level; Fire Resistance (17th-20th) - fire resistance 10 (all applied, each from the first level of its band; the compendium's table prints no level for natural weapons, read as 1st). Replaces the familiar.
Githyanki Sorcerer	KEY:ACF ~ Githyanki Sorcerer (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Sorcerer Class Feature	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Improved Unarmed Strike	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Alertness	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|1|TYPE=NaturalArmor|PREVARGTEQ:SorcererLVL,5	VISION:Darkvision (120')|PREVARGTEQ:SorcererLVL,9	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|DESCRIPTOR.Fire|1|PREVARGTEQ:SorcererLVL,13	BONUS:VAR|FireResistanceBonus|10|PREVARGTEQ:SorcererLVL,17	SOURCEPAGE:p.570	DESC:The path of the duthka'ariy: githyanki sorcerers manifest their infernal draconic heritage (from the interbreeding of githyanki and fiendish red dragons) and can never acquire a familiar. Natural Weapons - Improved Unarmed Strike; Keen Senses (1st-4th) - Alertness; Natural Armor (5th-8th) - +1 natural armor; Keen Senses (9th-12th) - darkvision 120 feet; Fire Focus (13th-16th) - fire spells at +1 caster level; Fire Resistance (17th-20th) - fire resistance 10 (all applied, each from the first level of its band; the compendium's table prints no level for natural weapons, read as 1st). Replaces the familiar.
Golarion Sorcerer	KEY:Sorcerer ACF ~ Golarion Sorcerer (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SorcererACF.SorcererSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Sorcerer=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Golarion Sorcerer (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.571	DESC:Alternative class feature (sorcerer, 1st level). Sorcerers of the Isle of Hermea: Hidden Reserve (Su) - from 1st level, %1 times per day (Charisma bonus) the sorcerer can cast an additional spell he could normally cast, becoming fatigued afterwards (exhausted if it was of the highest level he can cast); not while fatigued or exhausted. Replaces summon familiar.
Golarion Sorcerer	KEY:ACF ~ Golarion Sorcerer (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Sorcerer Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.571	DESC:Sorcerers of the Isle of Hermea: Hidden Reserve (Su) - from 1st level, %1 times per day (Charisma bonus) the sorcerer can cast an additional spell he could normally cast, becoming fatigued afterwards (exhausted if it was of the highest level he can cast); not while fatigued or exhausted. Replaces summon familiar.|max(0,CHA)
Imbued Staff	KEY:Sorcerer ACF ~ Imbued Staff (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SorcererACF.SorcererFamiliar.SorcererSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Sorcerer=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Sorcerer Imbued Staff (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.571	DESC:Alternative class feature (sorcerer, 1st level). Instead of a familiar, a quarterstaff-length masterwork staff (never enchanted before; 500 gp of materials, usually a gem finial; 24-hour ritual) is imbued with part of your soul and becomes a magic item linked to you: hardness %1, %2 hit points, saves as you even unattended. Powers by your sorcerer level: cantrips (light 3/day, one stored cantrip 1/day, save DC 10) and deliver touch spells through it against normal AC (1st); enhanced weapon +%3 for you only (3rd, +2 at 11th, +3 at 19th); remote viewing - clairvoyance through its finial while concentrating, same plane (5th); vital transfer - forgo natural healing to restore your character level in hit points to it (9th); perfect location - a full round to know its direction and distance (13th); mighty weapon - bane, defending, flaming, frost, merciful, shock or thundering, chosen once (15th); return - summon it to your hand as a standard action (17th). If broken: DC 15 Fortitude save or lose 500 XP per sorcerer level (half on a success), no new staff for a year and a day; it loses its powers if you die. Crafting staff powers into it costs 20% more (50 charges). (Also for wizards.) Replaces the familiar.
Imbued Staff	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer Imbued Staff (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Sorcerer Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.571	DESC:Instead of a familiar, a quarterstaff-length masterwork staff (never enchanted before; 500 gp of materials, usually a gem finial; 24-hour ritual) is imbued with part of your soul and becomes a magic item linked to you: hardness %1, %2 hit points, saves as you even unattended. Powers by your sorcerer level: cantrips (light 3/day, one stored cantrip 1/day, save DC 10) and deliver touch spells through it against normal AC (1st); enhanced weapon +%3 for you only (3rd, +2 at 11th, +3 at 19th); remote viewing - clairvoyance through its finial while concentrating, same plane (5th); vital transfer - forgo natural healing to restore your character level in hit points to it (9th); perfect location - a full round to know its direction and distance (13th); mighty weapon - bane, defending, flaming, frost, merciful, shock or thundering, chosen once (15th); return - summon it to your hand as a standard action (17th). If broken: DC 15 Fortitude save or lose 500 XP per sorcerer level (half on a success), no new staff for a year and a day; it loses its powers if you die. Crafting staff powers into it costs 20% more (50 charges). (Also for wizards.) Replaces the familiar.|5+5*floor((SorcererLVL-1)/6)|15+5*floor((SorcererLVL-1)/6)|(SorcererLVL>=3)+(SorcererLVL>=11)+(SorcererLVL>=19)
Impromptu Metamagic	KEY:Sorcerer ACF ~ Impromptu Metamagic (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SorcererACF.SorcererFamiliar.SorcererSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Sorcerer=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Sorcerer Impromptu Metamagic (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.572	DESC:Alternative class feature (sorcerer, 1st level). Each day choose one metamagic feat you have: you can apply it spontaneously as you cast, without increasing the spell level or casting time, (5 - the feat's level adjustment) times that day (Quicken Spell once, Silent Spell four times); you may use no other metamagic feat that day, and you must still be able to cast spells of the level the spell would have with the feat. Prepared casters need not prepare the metamagic version. (Also for wizards, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
Impromptu Metamagic	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer Impromptu Metamagic (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Sorcerer Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.572	DESC:Each day choose one metamagic feat you have: you can apply it spontaneously as you cast, without increasing the spell level or casting time, (5 - the feat's level adjustment) times that day (Quicken Spell once, Silent Spell four times); you may use no other metamagic feat that day, and you must still be able to cast spells of the level the spell would have with the feat. Prepared casters need not prepare the metamagic version. (Also for wizards, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
School Mastery	KEY:Sorcerer ACF ~ School Mastery (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SorcererACF.SorcererFamiliar.SorcererSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Sorcerer=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Sorcerer School Mastery (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Alternative class feature (sorcerer, 1st level). Choose a school of magic (category below; a specialist wizard only her specialty): you cast its spells at +1 caster level and gain that school's benefit. (Also for wizards, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
School Mastery	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer School Mastery (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Sorcerer Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Sorcerer ACF School Mastery|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Choose a school of magic (category below; a specialist wizard only her specialty): you cast its spells at +1 caster level and gain that school's benefit. (Also for wizards, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
School Mastery (Abjuration)	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer School Mastery (DMC) ~ Abjuration	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFSchoolMastery.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Abjuration|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Mastery of abjuration: +1 caster level for spells of this school (applied). Any non-instantaneous, nonpermanent abjuration spell you cast on someone other than yourself that does not require concentration has double the duration (not combined with other duration changes such as Extend Spell).
School Mastery (Conjuration)	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer School Mastery (DMC) ~ Conjuration	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFSchoolMastery.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Conjuration|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Mastery of conjuration: +1 caster level for spells of this school (applied). Each creature you conjure with any summon spell gains a +2 enhancement bonus to Dexterity and Wisdom for the spell's duration.
School Mastery (Divination)	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer School Mastery (DMC) ~ Divination	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFSchoolMastery.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Divination|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Mastery of divination: +1 caster level for spells of this school (applied). Whenever you cast a divination spell you gain a +2 insight bonus on Listen and Spot checks for 1 hour per spell level (30 minutes for 0-level spells).
School Mastery (Enchantment)	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer School Mastery (DMC) ~ Enchantment	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFSchoolMastery.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Enchantment|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Mastery of enchantment: +1 caster level for spells of this school (applied). For 24 hours after an enchantment spell you cast expires, its target takes -2 on Will saves against your spells and spell-like abilities (one creature at a time).
School Mastery (Evocation)	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer School Mastery (DMC) ~ Evocation	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFSchoolMastery.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Evocation|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Mastery of evocation: +1 caster level for spells of this school (applied). Evocation spells you cast that deal hit point damage deal +1 point of damage.
School Mastery (Illusion)	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer School Mastery (DMC) ~ Illusion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFSchoolMastery.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Illusion|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Mastery of illusion: +1 caster level for spells of this school (applied). Your illusion (shadow) spells creating partially real effects are 10% more real (shadow conjuration creatures 30% as strong instead of 20%).
School Mastery (Necromancy)	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer School Mastery (DMC) ~ Necromancy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFSchoolMastery.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Necromancy|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Mastery of necromancy: +1 caster level for spells of this school (applied). Undead you create with any evil spell gain temporary hit points equal to your caster level, lasting until lost.
School Mastery (Transmutation)	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer School Mastery (DMC) ~ Transmutation	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFSchoolMastery.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Transmutation|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Mastery of transmutation: +1 caster level for spells of this school (applied). The DC to resist your spells that alter a creature's form, kind or type increases by +1.
Poltergeists	KEY:Sorcerer ACF ~ Poltergeists (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SorcererACF.SorcererPoltergeists	PRECLASS:1,Sorcerer=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Poltergeists (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.574	DESC:Alternative class feature (sorcerer, 1st level). A sorcerer who never fully controlled the first flashes of his magic manifests a poltergeist (chosen at 1st level, category below): he gives up two 0-level spells, beginning with three cantrips known instead of five, and can never learn the spells the poltergeist replaces (by hand). Replaces those two 0-level spells known.
Poltergeists	KEY:ACF ~ Poltergeists (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Sorcerer Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Sorcerer ACF Poltergeists|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.574	DESC:A sorcerer who never fully controlled the first flashes of his magic manifests a poltergeist (chosen at 1st level, category below): he gives up two 0-level spells, beginning with three cantrips known instead of five, and can never learn the spells the poltergeist replaces (by hand). Replaces those two 0-level spells known.
Poltergeists (Crawling Coins)	KEY:ACF ~ Poltergeists (DMC) ~ Crawling Coins	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFPoltergeists.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.574	DESC:Your first word likely being "Mine," your loathing of sharing somehow gives life to small objects on your person, sending them scuttling away from those hoping to take them from you. You may use Sleight of Hand to conceal objects on your body even if you put no skill ranks in it. Further, anyone attempting to use Sleight of Hand to take something from you suffers a -4 penalty. Spells lost: Prestidigitation and open/close.
Poltergeists (Fanfare)	KEY:ACF ~ Poltergeists (DMC) ~ Fanfare	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFPoltergeists.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.574	DESC:Perhaps coddled a bit too much as a child, you feel a sense of uniqueness and entitlement that causes you to enter rooms amidst a flourish of glorious sounds and pyrotechnics. You may, as a conscious act of will similar to holding your breath, suppress this ability, allowing you to sneak into a room. Doing so, however, leaves you feeling strangely diminished. When you permit this ability to function normally you gain a +2 bonus on Diplomacy or Intimidate checks for an hour against anyone who witnesses your spectacular entrance. Spells lost: Dancing lights and ghost sounds.
Poltergeists (Frost Fingers)	KEY:ACF ~ Poltergeists (DMC) ~ Frost Fingers	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFPoltergeists.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.574	DESC:Often belabored for your clumsiness as a child, it sometimes seems as if your merest touch causes objects to shatter and crack. Whenever you first touch an object with a hardness of 2 or less it must make a Fortitude save (DC 10 + Charisma modifier) or take damage equal to your Charisma modifier. This damage ignores hardness. If the item makes its saving throw or endures the damage you may handle it normally thereafter.  Spells lost: Ray of frost and touch of fatigue. That'll Leave a Mark! (Su): Called a bully by many, the secret satisfaction you gained from making playmates cry "uncle" somehow caused you to leave a record of their submission visible to all. Whenever you successfully strike an opponent with an unarmed attack or touch attack she must make a Fortitude save (DC 10 + Charisma modifier) or develop a bruise in a shape you desire in the area you struck. This bruise heals normally in a week and is removed by any amount of magical healing. Spells lost: Acid splash and arcane mark.
Poltergeists (The Pinch)	KEY:ACF ~ Poltergeists (DMC) ~ The Pinch	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SorcererACFPoltergeists.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.574	DESC:A solitary and eccentric child, often targeted by bullies with rocks or rotted food, you developed a minor but effective way of distracting your tormentors. Once per day as a standard action you can target a spellcaster concentrating on a spell and force the spellcaster to succeed at a Concentration check (DC 15 + spell level of spell being concentrated on) or lose the spell. This disrupting effect cannot be used on a spell as it is being cast. Spells lost: Flare and mage hand.
Sorcerer Spheres	KEY:Sorcerer ACF ~ Sorcerer Spheres (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SorcererACF.SorcererSpheres	PRECLASS:1,Sorcerer=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Sorcerer Spheres (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Alternative class feature (sorcerer, 1st level). A specialist sorcerer's sphere - an area of magic tied to a powerful magical ancestor, narrower than a school (chosen at 1st level with the DM, never changed): spells of the sphere at +1 caster level (not for spell trigger or completion items); spells of the opposed sphere at -2 caster levels (delaying access to some spells), and no spell trigger or completion items of the opposed sphere (by hand). Replaces nothing.
Sorcerer Spheres	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer Spheres (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Sorcerer Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:A specialist sorcerer's sphere - an area of magic tied to a powerful magical ancestor, narrower than a school (chosen at 1st level with the DM, never changed): spells of the sphere at +1 caster level (not for spell trigger or completion items); spells of the opposed sphere at -2 caster levels (delaying access to some spells), and no spell trigger or completion items of the opposed sphere (by hand). Replaces nothing.
Wilderness Companion	KEY:Sorcerer ACF ~ Wilderness Companion (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SorcererACF.SorcererFamiliar.SorcererSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Sorcerer=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Sorcerer Wilderness Companion (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.577	DESC:Alternative class feature (sorcerer, 1st level). A sorcerer or wizard wanting a more durable companion in the wilderness (swap): an animal companion as a druid of half his class level (applied). Replaces the familiar.
Wilderness Companion	KEY:ACF ~ Sorcerer Wilderness Companion (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Sorcerer Class Feature	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Animal Companion	BONUS:VAR|AnimalCompanionLVL|floor(SorcererLVL/2)	SOURCEPAGE:p.577	DESC:A sorcerer or wizard wanting a more durable companion in the wilderness (swap): an animal companion as a druid of half his class level (applied). Replaces the familiar.

###Block: Wizard alternative class features
Combat Wizard	KEY:Wizard ACF ~ Combat Wizard (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.WizardACF.WizardScribeScroll.WizardBonusFeats	PRECLASS:1,Wizard=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Combat Wizard (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.662	DESC:Alternative class feature (wizard, 1st level). A wizard who trades knowledge of magic and craft for combat prowess (swap): fighter bonus feats (Fighter Feat category) at 1st level and at 5th, 10th, 15th and 20th (%1 now; applied). Replaces Scribe Scroll and the wizard bonus feat list.
Combat Wizard	KEY:ACF ~ Combat Wizard (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Wizard Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Fighter Feat|1+floor(WizardLVL/5)	SOURCEPAGE:p.662	DESC:A wizard who trades knowledge of magic and craft for combat prowess (swap): fighter bonus feats (Fighter Feat category) at 1st level and at 5th, 10th, 15th and 20th (%1 now; applied). Replaces Scribe Scroll and the wizard bonus feat list.|1+floor(WizardLVL/5)
Dead Levels	KEY:Wizard ACF ~ Dead Levels (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.WizardACF.WizardDeadLevels	PRECLASS:1,Wizard=2	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Wizard Dead Levels (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.662	DESC:Alternative class feature (wizard, 2nd level). Animated Script (Su), from 2nd level: the wizard animates the writing in her spellbook, raising the Spellcraft DC for another wizard to decipher or prepare its spells by her Intelligence modifier + 1, at 5 gp per inscribed page; for each level after 2nd without a wizard bonus feat she can raise it by +1 more at +5 gp per page (+2 at 3rd for 10 gp, +3 at 4th, +4 at 6th ...); she can will the script still to read it herself. Replaces nothing.
Dead Levels	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard Dead Levels (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Wizard Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.662	DESC:Animated Script (Su), from 2nd level: the wizard animates the writing in her spellbook, raising the Spellcraft DC for another wizard to decipher or prepare its spells by her Intelligence modifier + 1, at 5 gp per inscribed page; for each level after 2nd without a wizard bonus feat she can raise it by +1 more at +5 gp per page (+2 at 3rd for 10 gp, +3 at 4th, +4 at 6th ...); she can will the script still to read it herself. Replaces nothing.
Eidetic Spellcaster	KEY:Wizard ACF ~ Eidetic Spellcaster (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.WizardACF.WizardFamiliar.WizardSummonFamiliar.WizardScribeScroll	PRECLASS:1,Wizard=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Eidetic Spellcaster (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.670	DESC:Alternative class feature (wizard, 1st level). Your photographic memory acts as your spellbook: you need no spellbook to record or prepare spells; you learn spells normally (from levels or other spellbooks) and pay the normal costs (in special incenses rather than inks), but need not write them down. Replaces the familiar and the Scribe Scroll bonus feat.
Eidetic Spellcaster	KEY:ACF ~ Eidetic Spellcaster (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Wizard Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.670	DESC:Your photographic memory acts as your spellbook: you need no spellbook to record or prepare spells; you learn spells normally (from levels or other spellbooks) and pay the normal costs (in special incenses rather than inks), but need not write them down. Replaces the familiar and the Scribe Scroll bonus feat.
Golarion Wizard	KEY:Wizard ACF ~ Golarion Wizard (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.WizardACF.WizardScribeScroll	PRECLASS:1,Wizard=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Golarion Wizard (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.684	DESC:Alternative class feature (wizard, 1st level). Arcane Duelist (Su), wizards of the Arcanamirum: as a swift action, push a spell - +1 to its save DC, or +2 on the level check to overcome spell resistance, or a +2 morale bonus on attack rolls made with it; %1 times per day (Intelligence bonus). Replaces the Scribe Scroll feat at 1st level.
Golarion Wizard	KEY:ACF ~ Golarion Wizard (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Wizard Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.684	DESC:Arcane Duelist (Su), wizards of the Arcanamirum: as a swift action, push a spell - +1 to its save DC, or +2 on the level check to overcome spell resistance, or a +2 morale bonus on attack rolls made with it; %1 times per day (Intelligence bonus). Replaces the Scribe Scroll feat at 1st level.|max(0,INT)
Wizard of Sun and Moon	KEY:Wizard ACF ~ Wizard of Sun and Moon (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.WizardACF.WizardFamiliar.WizardSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Wizard=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Wizard of Sun and Moon (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.699	DESC:Alternative class feature (wizard, 1st level). Attuned to the cosmos: you designate one slot per spell level above 0 as the union of sun and moon and can prepare two spells in it, one of the moon (castable only underground or aboveground at night) and one of the sun (only aboveground in daylight); casting one uses the slot for both. It gives no more spells per day, only more choice. Replaces the familiar.
Wizard of Sun and Moon	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard of Sun and Moon (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Wizard Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.699	DESC:Attuned to the cosmos: you designate one slot per spell level above 0 as the union of sun and moon and can prepare two spells in it, one of the moon (castable only underground or aboveground at night) and one of the sun (only aboveground in daylight); casting one uses the slot for both. It gives no more spells per day, only more choice. Replaces the familiar.
Familiars	KEY:Wizard ACF ~ Familiars (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.WizardACF.WizardFamiliarList	PRECLASS:1,Wizard=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Wizard Familiars (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.672	DESC:Alternative class feature (wizard, 1st level). The compendium's compilation of all creatures eligible as familiars (pp. 672-678, by minimum spellcaster level, with equivalent statistics, requirements and master benefits). Offered here in addition to the familiars already in the repository: dog (1st; master +3 on Sense Motive checks); leopard, wolverine and Medium viper (1st, for a Huge or larger master; master +2 on Move Silently, +2 on Reflex saves, +3 on Bluff checks); with Improved Familiar: badger, Medium and Large viper (3rd), Small air, earth, fire and water elementals (5th - with Complete Mage, which defines them: dmc_acf_completemage.lst). Master benefits of these creatures by hand. Creatures with equivalent statistics (caterpillar as mouse, rabbit as cat, vulture as hawk ...) use their equivalent's familiar entry; creatures not in the repository (albatross, arctic fox, ferret, lynx, worg ...) by hand. Replaces nothing.
Familiars	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard Familiars (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Wizard Class Feature	COMPANIONLIST:Familiar|Companion ~ Dog	COMPANIONLIST:Familiar|Companion ~ Leopard,Companion ~ Wolverine,Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Medium)|PRESIZEGTEQ:H	COMPANIONLIST:Familiar|Companion ~ Badger,Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Medium),Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Large)|PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Improved Familiar|PRECLASS:1,SPELLCASTER.Arcane=3	SOURCEPAGE:p.672	DESC:The compendium's compilation of all creatures eligible as familiars (pp. 672-678, by minimum spellcaster level, with equivalent statistics, requirements and master benefits). Offered here in addition to the familiars already in the repository: dog (1st; master +3 on Sense Motive checks); leopard, wolverine and Medium viper (1st, for a Huge or larger master; master +2 on Move Silently, +2 on Reflex saves, +3 on Bluff checks); with Improved Familiar: badger, Medium and Large viper (3rd), Small air, earth, fire and water elementals (5th - with Complete Mage, which defines them: dmc_acf_completemage.lst). Master benefits of these creatures by hand. Creatures with equivalent statistics (caterpillar as mouse, rabbit as cat, vulture as hawk ...) use their equivalent's familiar entry; creatures not in the repository (albatross, arctic fox, ferret, lynx, worg ...) by hand. Replaces nothing.
Aligned Spellcaster	KEY:Wizard ACF ~ Aligned Spellcaster (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.WizardACF.WizardFamiliar.WizardSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Wizard=1	PREALIGN:LG,LN,LE,NG,NE,CG,CN,CE	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Wizard Aligned Spellcaster (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.563	DESC:Alternative class feature (wizard, 1st level). Choose a non-neutral alignment component you have: your spells gain that alignment descriptor unless they already have the opposite one (a neutral good caster casts all non-evil spells as good spells). Spells you cast that target creatures of the opposite alignment are cast at +1 caster level (+2 against creatures with the opposite alignment as a subtype); area and other untargeted spells gain no bonus. A true neutral caster cannot take it. (Also for sorcerers, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
Aligned Spellcaster	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard Aligned Spellcaster (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Wizard Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.563	DESC:Choose a non-neutral alignment component you have: your spells gain that alignment descriptor unless they already have the opposite one (a neutral good caster casts all non-evil spells as good spells). Spells you cast that target creatures of the opposite alignment are cast at +1 caster level (+2 against creatures with the opposite alignment as a subtype); area and other untargeted spells gain no bonus. A true neutral caster cannot take it. (Also for sorcerers, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
Arcane Reabsorption	KEY:Wizard ACF ~ Arcane Reabsorption (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.WizardACF.WizardFamiliar.WizardSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Wizard=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Wizard Arcane Reabsorption (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.563	DESC:Alternative class feature (wizard, 1st level). Whenever a targeted spell you cast fails to penetrate a creature's spell resistance or is countered, and has no effect at all, you can attempt to reabsorb it as an immediate action: a Spellcraft check (DC 20 + 3 x spell level) regains the spell or spell slot as if never cast; either way you take 1 point of nonlethal damage per spell level, bypassing damage reduction and resistances. (Also for sorcerers, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
Arcane Reabsorption	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard Arcane Reabsorption (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Wizard Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.563	DESC:Whenever a targeted spell you cast fails to penetrate a creature's spell resistance or is countered, and has no effect at all, you can attempt to reabsorb it as an immediate action: a Spellcraft check (DC 20 + 3 x spell level) regains the spell or spell slot as if never cast; either way you take 1 point of nonlethal damage per spell level, bypassing damage reduction and resistances. (Also for sorcerers, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
Beleaguered Spellcaster	KEY:Wizard ACF ~ Beleaguered Spellcaster (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.WizardACF.WizardFamiliar.WizardSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Wizard=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Wizard Beleaguered Spellcaster (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.564	DESC:Alternative class feature (wizard, 1st level). Whenever you take damage equal to 3 x your spellcaster level (%1) from one attack, the next spell you cast is automatically maximized or extended (your choice) without increasing its level or casting time; %2 times per day (1 + Charisma modifier). (Also for sorcerers, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
Beleaguered Spellcaster	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard Beleaguered Spellcaster (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Wizard Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.564	DESC:Whenever you take damage equal to 3 x your spellcaster level (%1) from one attack, the next spell you cast is automatically maximized or extended (your choice) without increasing its level or casting time; %2 times per day (1 + Charisma modifier). (Also for sorcerers, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.|3*WizardLVL|1+CHA
Disciple of Boccob	KEY:Wizard ACF ~ Disciple of Boccob (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.WizardACF.WizardFamiliar.WizardSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Wizard=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Wizard Disciple of Boccob (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.565	DESC:Alternative class feature (wizard, 1st level). A pious student of Boccob the Uncaring: you qualify for item creation feats as a character one level higher, and magic items you create are crafted at +1 caster level at no extra cost; if you destroy a permanent magic item you lose all arcane spellcasting for one day per caster level of the item. (Also for sorcerers, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
Disciple of Boccob	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard Disciple of Boccob (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Wizard Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.565	DESC:A pious student of Boccob the Uncaring: you qualify for item creation feats as a character one level higher, and magic items you create are crafted at +1 caster level at no extra cost; if you destroy a permanent magic item you lose all arcane spellcasting for one day per caster level of the item. (Also for sorcerers, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
Focus Caster	KEY:Wizard ACF ~ Focus Caster (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.WizardACF.WizardFamiliar.WizardSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Wizard=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Wizard Focus Caster (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.569	DESC:Alternative class feature (wizard, 1st level). Instead of a familiar you bind yourself (24-hour ritual, 100 gp) to a masterwork item that is a focus for all your spells - held, wielded or worn in addition to their normal components - and enhances one school (category below; a specialist wizard only her specialty). You are proficient with that item (not others of its kind); its hardness increases by half your caster level and its hit points by your caster level (up to double); enhancing it costs you 10%% less XP. If destroyed, you must bind another masterwork, non-magic item. Bonuses stack with Spell Focus and Spell Penetration. (Also for sorcerers, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
Focus Caster	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard Focus Caster (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Wizard Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Wizard ACF Focus Caster|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.569	DESC:Instead of a familiar you bind yourself (24-hour ritual, 100 gp) to a masterwork item that is a focus for all your spells - held, wielded or worn in addition to their normal components - and enhances one school (category below; a specialist wizard only her specialty). You are proficient with that item (not others of its kind); its hardness increases by half your caster level and its hit points by your caster level (up to double); enhancing it costs you 10%% less XP. If destroyed, you must bind another masterwork, non-magic item. Bonuses stack with Spell Focus and Spell Penetration. (Also for sorcerers, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
Focus Caster (Abjuration)	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard Focus Caster (DMC) ~ Abjuration	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WizardACFFocusCaster.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.569	DESC:Usually bracers, a buckler or a small shield: nonpersonal abjuration spells with one or more targets gain one additional target, affected for half the duration (full duration from 7th level); from 15th, personal abjuration spells can be cast as touch spells.
Focus Caster (Conjuration)	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard Focus Caster (DMC) ~ Conjuration	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WizardACFFocusCaster.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.569	DESC:Usually a gnarled quarterstaff or other polearm: conjuration spells last 1 round longer (2 at 7th, 3 at 15th); concentration spells also continue that long after you stop concentrating.
Focus Caster (Divination)	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard Focus Caster (DMC) ~ Divination	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WizardACFFocusCaster.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Divination|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.569	DESC:Usually a large crystal or an ornate holy symbol: +1 caster level for divination spells (applied); from 7th level divination durations double; from 15th a bonus to resist divinations equal to 1 + Intelligence modifier (minimum +1).
Focus Caster (Enchantment)	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard Focus Caster (DMC) ~ Enchantment	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WizardACFFocusCaster.SpecialQuality	BONUS:DC|SCHOOL.Enchantment|2|PREVARGTEQ:WizardLVL,15	SOURCEPAGE:p.569	DESC:Usually an ornate, nonfunctional piece of clothing (sash, hair ribbon): enchantment spells last 1 round longer (2 at 7th); concentration spells also continue that long after you stop; from 15th level +2 to the DC of your enchantment spells (applied).
Focus Caster (Evocation)	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard Focus Caster (DMC) ~ Evocation	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WizardACFFocusCaster.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.569	DESC:Usually a bladed weapon (longsword, dagger): +1 damage on evocation spells (a single target of multi-target spells such as magic missile); from 7th level they ignore the first 5 points of energy resistance (not immunity); from 15th, once per day, ignore a creature's immunity with an evocation spell.
Focus Caster (Illusion)	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard Focus Caster (DMC) ~ Illusion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WizardACFFocusCaster.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Illusion|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.569	DESC:Usually a mask, shroud or cloak: +1 caster level for illusion spells (applied); from 7th level a bonus equal to half your caster level on caster level checks against spell resistance with illusions; from 15th, personal illusion spells can be cast as touch spells.
Focus Caster (Necromancy)	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard Focus Caster (DMC) ~ Necromancy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WizardACFFocusCaster.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.569	DESC:Usually a flail, kama, sickle or scythe: +25% range for necromancy spells; from 7th level spells dealing ability damage or drain or an ability penalty deal 1 more; from 15th, living creatures failing the Fortitude save against your necromancy spells also become fatigued.
Focus Caster (Transmutation)	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard Focus Caster (DMC) ~ Transmutation	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WizardACFFocusCaster.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.569	DESC:Usually tools of creation (thieves' tools, a musical instrument, artisan's tools): nonpersonal transmutation spells with one or more targets gain one additional target for half the duration (full duration from 7th level); from 15th, once per day, a transmutation spell granting an ability bonus doubles it.
Imbued Staff	KEY:Wizard ACF ~ Imbued Staff (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.WizardACF.WizardFamiliar.WizardSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Wizard=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Wizard Imbued Staff (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.571	DESC:Alternative class feature (wizard, 1st level). Instead of a familiar, a quarterstaff-length masterwork staff (never enchanted before; 500 gp of materials, usually a gem finial; 24-hour ritual) is imbued with part of your soul and becomes a magic item linked to you: hardness %1, %2 hit points, saves as you even unattended. Powers by your wizard level: cantrips (light 3/day, one stored cantrip 1/day, save DC 10) and deliver touch spells through it against normal AC (1st); enhanced weapon +%3 for you only (3rd, +2 at 11th, +3 at 19th); remote viewing - clairvoyance through its finial while concentrating, same plane (5th); vital transfer - forgo natural healing to restore your character level in hit points to it (9th); perfect location - a full round to know its direction and distance (13th); mighty weapon - bane, defending, flaming, frost, merciful, shock or thundering, chosen once (15th); return - summon it to your hand as a standard action (17th). If broken: DC 15 Fortitude save or lose 500 XP per wizard level (half on a success), no new staff for a year and a day; it loses its powers if you die. Crafting staff powers into it costs 20% more (50 charges). (Also for sorcerers.) Replaces the familiar.
Imbued Staff	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard Imbued Staff (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Wizard Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.571	DESC:Instead of a familiar, a quarterstaff-length masterwork staff (never enchanted before; 500 gp of materials, usually a gem finial; 24-hour ritual) is imbued with part of your soul and becomes a magic item linked to you: hardness %1, %2 hit points, saves as you even unattended. Powers by your wizard level: cantrips (light 3/day, one stored cantrip 1/day, save DC 10) and deliver touch spells through it against normal AC (1st); enhanced weapon +%3 for you only (3rd, +2 at 11th, +3 at 19th); remote viewing - clairvoyance through its finial while concentrating, same plane (5th); vital transfer - forgo natural healing to restore your character level in hit points to it (9th); perfect location - a full round to know its direction and distance (13th); mighty weapon - bane, defending, flaming, frost, merciful, shock or thundering, chosen once (15th); return - summon it to your hand as a standard action (17th). If broken: DC 15 Fortitude save or lose 500 XP per wizard level (half on a success), no new staff for a year and a day; it loses its powers if you die. Crafting staff powers into it costs 20% more (50 charges). (Also for sorcerers.) Replaces the familiar.|5+5*floor((WizardLVL-1)/6)|15+5*floor((WizardLVL-1)/6)|(WizardLVL>=3)+(WizardLVL>=11)+(WizardLVL>=19)
Impromptu Metamagic	KEY:Wizard ACF ~ Impromptu Metamagic (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.WizardACF.WizardFamiliar.WizardSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Wizard=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Wizard Impromptu Metamagic (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.572	DESC:Alternative class feature (wizard, 1st level). Each day choose one metamagic feat you have: you can apply it spontaneously as you cast, without increasing the spell level or casting time, (5 - the feat's level adjustment) times that day (Quicken Spell once, Silent Spell four times); you may use no other metamagic feat that day, and you must still be able to cast spells of the level the spell would have with the feat. Prepared casters need not prepare the metamagic version. (Also for sorcerers, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
Impromptu Metamagic	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard Impromptu Metamagic (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Wizard Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.572	DESC:Each day choose one metamagic feat you have: you can apply it spontaneously as you cast, without increasing the spell level or casting time, (5 - the feat's level adjustment) times that day (Quicken Spell once, Silent Spell four times); you may use no other metamagic feat that day, and you must still be able to cast spells of the level the spell would have with the feat. Prepared casters need not prepare the metamagic version. (Also for sorcerers, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
School Mastery	KEY:Wizard ACF ~ School Mastery (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.WizardACF.WizardFamiliar.WizardSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Wizard=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Wizard School Mastery (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Alternative class feature (wizard, 1st level). Choose a school of magic (category below; a specialist wizard only her specialty): you cast its spells at +1 caster level and gain that school's benefit. (Also for sorcerers, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
School Mastery	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard School Mastery (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Wizard Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Wizard ACF School Mastery|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Choose a school of magic (category below; a specialist wizard only her specialty): you cast its spells at +1 caster level and gain that school's benefit. (Also for sorcerers, and hexblades at 4th level.) Replaces the familiar.
School Mastery (Abjuration)	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard School Mastery (DMC) ~ Abjuration	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WizardACFSchoolMastery.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Abjuration|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Mastery of abjuration: +1 caster level for spells of this school (applied). Any non-instantaneous, nonpermanent abjuration spell you cast on someone other than yourself that does not require concentration has double the duration (not combined with other duration changes such as Extend Spell).
School Mastery (Conjuration)	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard School Mastery (DMC) ~ Conjuration	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WizardACFSchoolMastery.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Conjuration|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Mastery of conjuration: +1 caster level for spells of this school (applied). Each creature you conjure with any summon spell gains a +2 enhancement bonus to Dexterity and Wisdom for the spell's duration.
School Mastery (Divination)	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard School Mastery (DMC) ~ Divination	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WizardACFSchoolMastery.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Divination|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Mastery of divination: +1 caster level for spells of this school (applied). Whenever you cast a divination spell you gain a +2 insight bonus on Listen and Spot checks for 1 hour per spell level (30 minutes for 0-level spells).
School Mastery (Enchantment)	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard School Mastery (DMC) ~ Enchantment	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WizardACFSchoolMastery.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Enchantment|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Mastery of enchantment: +1 caster level for spells of this school (applied). For 24 hours after an enchantment spell you cast expires, its target takes -2 on Will saves against your spells and spell-like abilities (one creature at a time).
School Mastery (Evocation)	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard School Mastery (DMC) ~ Evocation	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WizardACFSchoolMastery.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Evocation|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Mastery of evocation: +1 caster level for spells of this school (applied). Evocation spells you cast that deal hit point damage deal +1 point of damage.
School Mastery (Illusion)	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard School Mastery (DMC) ~ Illusion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WizardACFSchoolMastery.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Illusion|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Mastery of illusion: +1 caster level for spells of this school (applied). Your illusion (shadow) spells creating partially real effects are 10% more real (shadow conjuration creatures 30% as strong instead of 20%).
School Mastery (Necromancy)	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard School Mastery (DMC) ~ Necromancy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WizardACFSchoolMastery.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Necromancy|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Mastery of necromancy: +1 caster level for spells of this school (applied). Undead you create with any evil spell gain temporary hit points equal to your caster level, lasting until lost.
School Mastery (Transmutation)	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard School Mastery (DMC) ~ Transmutation	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WizardACFSchoolMastery.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Transmutation|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.576	DESC:Mastery of transmutation: +1 caster level for spells of this school (applied). The DC to resist your spells that alter a creature's form, kind or type increases by +1.
Wilderness Companion	KEY:Wizard ACF ~ Wilderness Companion (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.WizardACF.WizardFamiliar.WizardSummonFamiliar	PRECLASS:1,Wizard=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Wizard Wilderness Companion (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.577	DESC:Alternative class feature (wizard, 1st level). A sorcerer or wizard wanting a more durable companion in the wilderness (swap): an animal companion as a druid of half his class level (applied). Replaces the familiar.
Wilderness Companion	KEY:ACF ~ Wizard Wilderness Companion (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Wizard Class Feature	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Animal Companion	BONUS:VAR|AnimalCompanionLVL|floor(WizardLVL/2)	SOURCEPAGE:p.577	DESC:A sorcerer or wizard wanting a more durable companion in the wilderness (swap): an animal companion as a druid of half his class level (applied). Replaces the familiar.

###Block: Improved Domain Powers (p.163)
Improved Power	KEY:Improved Power (DMC)	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Improved Domain Power|1	PREMULT:1,[PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1],[PRECLASS:1,Paladin=4]	SOURCEPAGE:p.163	DESC:Through long devotion and hours of study you unlock one of the improved granted powers of one of your domains (chosen in the Improved Domain Power category; a paladin uses her deity's domains). You can take this feat multiple times, each time for a new domain; its effects do not stack.
Improved Air Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Air	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Air],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Air],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Air domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Far-Reaching Wind (Su): The touch of your holy symbol imbues a weapon with the essence of air. Air-imbued weapons are guided to their targets by gusts of wind, allowing supernatural accuracy over long distances. While under this effect, ranged weapons have their range increments doubled, and melee weapons may be hurled as thrown weapons with a range increment of 20 feet. Weapons enhanced in this way maintain their increased range for 1 minute. You may use this ability a number of times per day equal to your cleric level.
Improved Animal Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Animal	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Animal],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Animal],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Animal domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Totemic Spirit Companion (Sp): You can call upon the spirits of the natural world to aid you as a full-round action. This functions just like the spell summon nature's ally I using your cleric level as the caster level. All creatures summoned in this way have either the celestial or fiendish template as appropriate to the type of energy you channel. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1). Additional uses of this ability may be expended to summon more powerful creatures, with each additional use spent increasing the spell to the next highest level. For example, a 6th-level cleric could use this ability to cast summon nature's ally I three times per day or summon nature's ally III once per day (or any other combination).
Improved Chaos Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Chaos	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Chaos],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Chaos],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Chaos domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Chaos Curse (Su): A forking beam of multicolored light springs from your outstretched finger and strikes an enemy within 60 feet as a ranged touch attack. If your target fails a Will save (DC 10 + 1/2 your cleric level + your Charisma modifier), it becomes stricken with random misfortune for 1 minute. Each round, the target has a 50%% chance to drop what it is holding (if holding anything) or to provoke an attack of opportunity (if threatened and not holding anything). If neither condition applies, it falls prone. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1).
Improved Death Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Death	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Death],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Death],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Death domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Call of the Grave (Su): Creatures near you feel the inevitability of death and resist attempts to keep them among the living. When activated, all conjuration spells of the healing subschool cast within 30 feet of you heal half as much damage as normal. In addition, spells that restore life, such as raise dead, reincarnate, and resurrection do not function when cast within 30 feet of you. You may use this ability 1 round per day per cleric level you possess. These rounds need not be consecutive.
Improved Destruction Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Destruction	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Destruction],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Destruction],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Destruction domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Shattering Blow (Su): You may, as a free action, infuse your attacks with the destructive force of entropy for 1 round. While under this effect, your natural attacks and all weapons you use in melee are treated as adamantine for the purposes of bypassing damage reduction and object hardness. You may use this ability 1 round per day per cleric level you possess and these rounds need not be consecutive.
Improved Earth Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Earth	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Earth],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Earth],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Earth domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Tremor Step (Su): While standing on a solid, natural surface (caves or fields would both work; the upper floors of a tower would not) you may strike the earth to produce highly localized seismic vibrations. All creatures except you standing on the ground within 20 feet of you must make Balance checks (DC 10 + your cleric level + your Charisma modifier) or fall prone. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1).
Improved Evil Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Evil	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Evil],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Evil],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Evil domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Torture Strike (Su): One living creature touched (requiring a successful melee touch attack) is wracked by agonizing pain, as if a branding iron had struck bare flesh. You gain a bonus on Intimidate checks against an affected creature equal to your cleric level for 1 minute. In addition, the target creature also takes 1d4 points of Strength damage and is nauseated for 1 round. A successful Fortitude save (DC 10 + 1/2 your cleric level + your Charisma modifier) reduces the condition to sickened and negates the Strength damage. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1).
Improved Fire Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Fire	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Fire],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Fire],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Fire domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Flame-Guiding Song (Su): Your voice has a hypnotic power over fire. You can cause flames to lash out at those nearby, attacking one foe within 10 feet of an existing blaze. These hungry flames deal 2d6 points of fire damage and might cause the target to catch fire. The Reflex save DC to avoid catching on fire or to extinguish these flames equals 10 + 1/2 your cleric level + your Charisma modifier. You may also use this ability to automatically extinguish nonmagical fires no larger than a bonfire. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1).
Improved Good Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Good	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Good],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Good],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Good domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Saving Grace (Su): You can grant a divine boon to your allies, assisting them in their endeavors. You can bestow this boon upon an ally within 30 feet as a move action. This boon grants a sacred bonus equal to your Charisma modifier on the next saving throw, attack roll, skill check, or ability check he attempts within the next minute. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1).
Improved Healing Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Healing	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Healing],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Healing],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Healing domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Healing Light (Su): You may channel divine energy as a free action to enhance a spell of the healing subschool. When using this ability, such spells with a range of touch may be cast with a range of close (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels). You may use this ability a number of times per day equal to your cleric level.
Improved Knowledge Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Knowledge	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Knowledge],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Knowledge],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Knowledge domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Divine Inspiration (Su): You can glimpse into the mind of your deity, granting you unsurpassed powers of recall and intuition. You can channel divine energy to take to on any Knowledge skill check as if you had ranks in it, even if you are untrained, as a free action. You may add your Charisma bonus to the check in addition to your Intelligence bonus. You may use this ability a number of times per day equal to you cleric level.
Improved Law Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Law	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Law],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Law],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Law domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Zone of Enforced Order (Su): You can emit an aura that makes chaotic creatures uncomfortable. When in effect, all chaotic creatures within 30 feet of you take a -2 penalty on attack rolls, saving throws, skill checks, and ability checks. You may use this ability 1 round per day per cleric level you possess. These rounds need not be consecutive.
Improved Luck Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Luck	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Luck],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Luck],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Luck domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Charmed Existence (Su): You may, as an immediate action, use this ability to gain a +2 luck bonus on an attack roll, saving throw, skill check, or ability check. You must decide to use this ability before you roll and may only use this ability once per round. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1).
Improved Magic Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Magic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Magic],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Magic],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Magic domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Power Magical Device (Su): You can channel divine energy through a wand, staff, or other charged magical item, powering it with faith rather than the item's own internal reserves. Doing so requires only as much time as is required to activate the item normally (typically a standard action). The magic item produces all its normal effects, but no charge is drained. To power an item, your caster level must be at least equal to the caster level of the item. You cannot use this ability to duplicate spells with an XP or costly material component. Abilities that require multiple charges require you to spend an equal number of uses of this ability. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1).
Improved Protection Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Protection	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Protection],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Protection],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Protection domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Shield of the Martyr (Su): You can prevent harm to others at the cost of your own safety. Whenever an ally within 30 feet takes damage, you can channel divine energy as an immediate action to split the wounds between the target and yourself (each taking half damage; if an odd number you take the extra point of damage). This ability can only be used once per round and only against a single damage source. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1).
Improved Strength Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Strength	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Strength],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Strength],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Strength domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Tremendous Might (Su): You can channel divine power into feats of truly superhuman might. You may add a +6 morale bonus on any Strength-based skill check or Strength check required to break, lift, drag, or push on object. This does not apply to attack or damage rolls, including grapple, sunder, or bull rush attempts. You may use this ability a number of times per day equal to your cleric level.
Improved Sun Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Sun	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Sun],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Sun],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Sun domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Vengeance of Day (Su): Rays of light brighter than the noon sun burst from your raised holy symbol. All within a 30 foot cone must make Will saves (DC 10 + 1/2 your cleric level + your Charisma modifier) or be dazzled for a number of rounds equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum 1 round). Undead and creatures with light blindness or light sensitivity, such as kobolds or drow, are blinded instead on a failed save. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1).
Improved Travel Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Travel	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Travel],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Travel],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Travel domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Second Wind (Su): You touch your holy symbol to a creature, imbuing it with renewed vigor for travel and great speed. You can remove the fatigued condition or make an exhausted creature merely fatigued. If the target creature has neither of these conditions, this ability instead increases the creature's base speed by +30 feet for 1 round. You may use this ability a number of times per day equal to your cleric level.
Improved Trickery Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Trickery	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Trickery],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Trickery],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Trickery domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Miraculous Deception (Su): You can channel divine power to improve the skills you naturally develop in service of your trickster deity. Using this ability grants you a +4 divine bonus on a single Bluff, Disguise, or Hide skill check. You may use this ability a number of times per day equal to your cleric level.
Improved War Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ War	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,War],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,War],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the War domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Piercing Steel Talon (Su): When wielding your deity's chosen weapon, you can channel divine energy into a single deadly blow. You instinctively attack the weakest points of your target's defenses, allowing you to, as a free action, ignore either the target's armor or shield bonus to AC for a single attack. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1), but no more than once per round.
Improved Water Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Water	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Water],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Water],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Water domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Waves Protect Their Own (Su): When at least waist deep in water, you can summon a vortex of swift currents and crashing waves to aid your allies and buffet your enemies. Allies within 30 feet suffer no penalties for underwater combat (as if under a freedom of movement effect) and suffer no risk of drowning in even the roughest seas (although if they choose to dive below the waves they can hold their breath no longer than normal). Enemies in the area take a penalty on attack rolls equal to your Charisma modifier due to the impeding flow of the water (having a swim speed does not negate this penalty, although a freedom of movement effect does). You may use this ability 1 round per day per cleric level you possess. These rounds need not be consecutive.
Beast-Wrestling Combat Style	KEY:Combat Style ~ Beast-Wrestling (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.478	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class Feature.Ranger Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RangerCombatStyle	VISIBLE:YES	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Improved Unarmed Strike|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,1],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Improved Grapple|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,2],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Stunning Fist|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,3],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	DESC:Fighting with bare hands and brute strength, originally to capture dangerous animals (such as crocodiles) without harming them. Combat style (2nd): Improved Unarmed Strike; improved combat style (6th): Improved Grapple; combat style mastery (11th): Stunning Fist - only in light or no armor, as the ranger's other combat styles.
Mounted-Combat Combat Style	KEY:Combat Style ~ Mounted-Combat (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.478	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class Feature.Ranger Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RangerCombatStyle	VISIBLE:YES	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Ride-By Attack|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,1],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Spirited Charge|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,2],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Trample|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,3],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	DESC:Using a mount in combat, typically a horse, riding dog or exotic mount as animal companion. Combat style (2nd): Ride-By Attack; improved combat style (6th): Spirited Charge; combat style mastery (11th): Trample - only in light or no armor, as the ranger's other combat styles.
Piscator Combat Style	KEY:Combat Style ~ Piscator (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.478	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class Feature.Ranger Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RangerCombatStyle	VISIBLE:YES	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Exotic Weapon Proficiency(Net)|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,1],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Improved Trip|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,2],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Improved Critical(Trident)|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,3],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	DESC:A net in one hand and a melee weapon (typically a trident) in the other, entangling or tripping foes before striking; Improved Critical is granted for the trident (change the weapon by hand). Combat style (2nd): Exotic Weapon Proficiency (Net); improved combat style (6th): Improved Trip; combat style mastery (11th): Improved Critical (Trident) - only in light or no armor, as the ranger's other combat styles.
Strong-Arm Combat Style	KEY:Combat Style ~ Strong-Arm (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.478	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class Feature.Ranger Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RangerCombatStyle	VISIBLE:YES	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Power Attack|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,1],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Improved Sunder|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,2],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Great Cleave|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,3],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	DESC:Wading into battle wielding the largest weapon she can, relying on strength and the weight of steel. Combat style (2nd): Power Attack; improved combat style (6th): Improved Sunder; combat style mastery (11th): Great Cleave - only in light or no armor, as the ranger's other combat styles.
Throwing Combat Style	KEY:Combat Style ~ Throwing (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.478	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class Feature.Ranger Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RangerCombatStyle	VISIBLE:YES	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Quick Draw|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,1],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Point Blank Shot|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,2],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Far Shot|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,3],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	DESC:Thrown weapons (favored by halflings, some nomadic humans and barbaric humanoids), keeping distance like the archery style. Combat style (2nd): Quick Draw; improved combat style (6th): Point Blank Shot; combat style mastery (11th): Far Shot - only in light or no armor, as the ranger's other combat styles.
Natural Attack Combat Style	KEY:Combat Style ~ Natural Attacks (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.481	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class Feature.Ranger Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RangerCombatStyle	VISIBLE:YES	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Fangshields Ranger ~ Natural Attack Style	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Multiattack|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,1],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	DESC:Fangshields rangers only: Multiattack at 2nd level (Improved Natural Attack instead with only one kind of natural attack - by hand), Weapon Focus with one natural attack at 6th, and at 11th Weapon Focus with a second natural weapon or Greater Weapon Focus with the only one (by hand), without prerequisites.
Accurate Fall	KEY:Rogue Special Ability ~ Accurate Fall (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Class Feature.Rogue Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RogueSpecialAbilitySelection	PRETEXT:Must have survived taking 20d6 points of damage from falling.	SOURCEPAGE:p.516	DESC:New rogue special ability (10th level and higher, in place of a special ability). Dancing upon currents and eddies in the air the rogue may aim where she falls, often managing to land in just the right spot to minimize injury. Whenever the rogue falls she may attempt a Reflex save to convert half the damage from the fall into nonlethal damage. The DC of the save depends upon the type of surface upon which the rogue falls. Surface DC Liquid (water, quicksand) 18 Soft (lava, mud, haystack) 20 Yielding (underbrush, tent canopy) 22 Hard (stone, building roof) 24 Uneven (spikes, stalagmites) 26 The rogue may also make a Tumble check in order to reduce the lethal damage further. Prerequisite: Must have survived taking 20d6 points of damage from falling.
Adrenaline Rush	KEY:Rogue Special Ability ~ Adrenaline Rush (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Class Feature.Rogue Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RogueSpecialAbilitySelection	PRETEXT:Must have succeeded at a Fortitude save to avoid death due to massive damage.	SOURCEPAGE:p.516	DESC:New rogue special ability (10th level and higher, in place of a special ability). Brought to the brink of death by massive trauma the rogue somehow survived. As a result, she developed a talent for pushing her body beyond its normal limits. Once per day, the rogue may choose to treat a Strength-based skill check as if she had rolled a natural 20. The rogue must declare she is using this ability before the die roll, thereby negating the necessity of the check. Prerequisite: Must have succeeded at a Fortitude save to avoid death due to massive damage.
Cartilaginous Skeleton	KEY:Rogue Special Ability ~ Cartilaginous Skeleton (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Class Feature.Rogue Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RogueSpecialAbilitySelection	PRETEXT:Must have been reduced to fewer than 0 hit points by bludgeoning damage or a crushing attack.	BONUS:SKILL|Escape Artist|4	SOURCEPAGE:p.516	DESC:New rogue special ability (10th level and higher, in place of a special ability). The rogue's shattered bones knit back together under a sheath of flexible cartilage, allowing her to contort herself in remarkable ways. The rogue gains a +4 bonus on Escape Artist checks and an additional +2 bonus when at tempting to escape a grapple. Further, if subject to a grapple she may make an attack of opportunity against the grappling opponent even if it has the Improved Grapple feat or the improved grab special attack. Prerequisite: Must have been reduced to fewer than 0 hit points by bludgeoning damage or a crushing attack.
Enriched Bone Marrow	KEY:Rogue Special Ability ~ Enriched Bone Marrow (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Class Feature.Rogue Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RogueSpecialAbilitySelection	PRETEXT:Constitution must have been reduced below 3 by blood-draining attacks.	SOURCEPAGE:p.516	DESC:New rogue special ability (10th level and higher, in place of a special ability). The rogue's recovery from near-fatal blood loss left her better able to recuperate from physical disability. Each day in which the rogue attempts to recover ability damage to her Strength, Dexterity, or Constitution, she may attempt a Fortitude save (DC 15 + current amount of ability damage) to recover an extra point of ability damage. Prerequisite: Constitution must have been reduced below 3 by blood-draining attacks.
Façade	KEY:Rogue Special Ability ~ Façade (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Class Feature.Rogue Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RogueSpecialAbilitySelection	SOURCEPAGE:p.516	DESC:New rogue special ability (10th level and higher, in place of a special ability). When the rogue disguises himself, he delves so deeply into character that he fools even divination magic. Whenever a creature casts a divination spell (or uses an ability that reproduces the effect of such a spell) that affects the rogue while he's disguised, the creature must make a Spot check opposed by the rogue's Disguise check. If the Spot check fails, the divination spell perceives the rogue as radiating the aura and thoughts that the rogue wishes the effect to detect. For instance, a rogue disguised as a zombie might radiate a neutral evil aura, detect as undead, and would have no discernible thoughts for a detect thoughts spell to pick up. Such a rogue would not suffer any ill effects from such a perfect disguise, such as extra harm from a holy or bane weapons.
Face in the Crowd	KEY:Rogue Special Ability ~ Face in the Crowd (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Class Feature.Rogue Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RogueSpecialAbilitySelection	SOURCEPAGE:p.516	DESC:New rogue special ability (10th level and higher, in place of a special ability). The rogue develops an uncanny ability to blend in while among large numbers of people. When within a crowd, the rogue may use the Hide skill even while being observed. For the purposes of this effect, a crowd consists of at least ten creatures at least half the rogue's size within a 10-foot radius of the rogue.
Fear Mirror	KEY:Rogue Special Ability ~ Fear Mirror (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Class Feature.Rogue Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RogueSpecialAbilitySelection	PRETEXT:Must have succeeded at a Fortitude save to resist phantasmal killer.	SOURCEPAGE:p.516	DESC:New rogue special ability (10th level and higher, in place of a special ability). Having faced and overcome the most terrifying thing she can imagine, the rogue may reflect similar horrors back at her foes. When targeted by a fear effect the rogue instinctively projects the attack back to its source. Both the rogue and the source of the fear effect must make any applicable saving throws to resist the effects of the attack. Any immunities possessed by the source of the attack still apply. Prerequisite: Must have succeeded at a Fortitude save to resist phantasmal killer.
Frostfell Terrain Mastery	KEY:Rogue Special Ability ~ Frostfell Terrain Mastery (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Class Feature.Rogue Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RogueSpecialAbilitySelection	SOURCEPAGE:p.516	DESC:New rogue special ability (10th level and higher, in place of a special ability). The rogue can move about in frostfell environments with great ease and quickness. As long as she is in a cold terrain or region of frostfell (or in a city located in such a region), the rogue gains a +2 competence bonus on initiative checks and a +10-foot bonus to her land speed. She loses these bonuses when she is wearing medium or heavy armor, or is carrying a medium or heavy load.
Handwriting Analysis	KEY:Rogue Special Ability ~ Handwriting Analysis (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Class Feature.Rogue Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RogueSpecialAbilitySelection	SOURCEPAGE:p.516	DESC:New rogue special ability (10th level and higher, in place of a special ability). Trained to scrutinize the whorls and loops of a person's writing along with choices of words and imagery, the rogue may make startlingly accurate deductions about a person from handwriting alone. Upon making a successful Decipher Script check, the rogue may attempt to learn further information about the writer. The result of this Decipher Script check reveals specific traits and all facts of a lesser DC as noted in the following table. For example, a rogue who makes a Decipher Script check and exceeds the DC by 5 reveals the relative age, race, and gender of the writer. When attempting to use this ability to sniff out a forgery (for instance, to see if a love letter purportedly written by a princess was actually composed by a female of her age, race, and gender) use the Forgery skill check of the forger in lieu of a Decipher Script DC. By succeeding at a Decipher Script check opposed by the forger's Forgery check, the rogue may attempt to reveal information about the forger as normal. Decipher Script Fact Check Gender Meets DC Race Exceeds the DC by 2 Relative age* Exceeds the DC by 5 Highest level class Exceeds the DC by 10 Law vs. chaos Exceeds the DC by 15 alignment axis Good vs. evil alignment Exceeds the DC by 20 axis * Child, adult, middle aged, old, or venerable.
Happier Days	KEY:Rogue Special Ability ~ Happier Days (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Class Feature.Rogue Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RogueSpecialAbilitySelection	PRETEXT:Must have made a saving throw to resist a death effect.	SOURCEPAGE:p.516	DESC:New rogue special ability (10th level and higher, in place of a special ability). At the moment of crisis the rogue's life did indeed pass before her eyes, and now she may draw upon memories of better times to sustain her when enemies assault her psyche. Once per day, if the rogue must attempt a Will save she may instead choose to cast her mind adrift among her memories rather then suffer the effects of a possible failed save. She must decide to use this ability before she attempts the Will save, negating the need for the saving throw. While lost in her memories she is oblivious to her surroundings and becomes helpless. Each round, at the end of her turn, the rogue may attempt to pull her thoughts back to the present attempting a Will save (at the same DC of the original Will save). For each round she fails this save she remains helpless. Prerequisite: Must have made a saving throw to resist a death effect.
Heart of Stone	KEY:Rogue Special Ability ~ Heart of Stone (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Class Feature.Rogue Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RogueSpecialAbilitySelection	PRETEXT:Must have successfully resisted a petrification attack.	SOURCEPAGE:p.516	DESC:New rogue special ability (10th level and higher, in place of a special ability). A brush with petrification left the rogue's organs stronger and more resilient, offering her protection from certain kinds of injuries. The rogue gains DR 5/-, but only against the extra damage from critical hits and sneak attacks. In addition, the rogue adds her class level to the amount of damage required to trigger a Fortitude save to resist death due to massive damage. Prerequisite: Must have successfully resisted a petrification attack.
Ice in the Veins	KEY:Rogue Special Ability ~ Ice in the Veins (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Class Feature.Rogue Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RogueSpecialAbilitySelection	PRETEXT:Must have been reduced to fewer than 0 hit points by a cold attack.	SOURCEPAGE:p.516	DESC:New rogue special ability (10th level and higher, in place of a special ability). Intense cold brings with it a strange lethargy and somehow, to the detriment of her enemies, the experience lingers within the rogue's bloodstream. Any creature not immune to cold or sleep effects that bites the rogue must make a Fortitude save (DC 10 + half the rogue's class level + the rogue's Constitution modifier) or become fatigued for 1 round per 2 rogue class levels. Once affected by this ability, further bites extend the duration but do not otherwise stack. Prerequisite: Must have been reduced to fewer than 0 hit points by a cold attack.
Knockout Blow	KEY:Rogue Special Ability ~ Knockout Blow (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Class Feature.Rogue Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RogueSpecialAbilitySelection	SOURCEPAGE:p.516	DESC:New rogue special ability (10th level and higher, in place of a special ability). When a rogue would make a sneak attack that deals nonlethal damage, she may instead attempt to stun her opponent before rolling her attack. If she hits, her opponent must succeed at a Fortitude save (DC 15 + per die of sneak attack damage) or be stunned for 1d3 rounds.
Light Sleeper	KEY:Rogue Special Ability ~ Light Sleeper (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Class Feature.Rogue Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RogueSpecialAbilitySelection	SOURCEPAGE:p.516	DESC:New rogue special ability (10th level and higher, in place of a special ability). The rogue's sensitivity to the slightest sound becomes so acute that it is almost impossible for him to fail to react to danger. The rogue no longer suffers a -10 penalty to Listen checks while asleep. Painful Strike: The rogue's knowledge of anatomy allows her to inflict tremendous pain. The rogue must make a sneak attack attempt with an unarmed strike. If she hits, her target must make a Fortitude save (DC 10 + 1 per die of sneak attack damage + Intelligence modifier). If the target fails this save, he must make a Concentration check (DC 15 + 1 per die of sneak attack damage + spell level) to cast a spell or use a spell-like ability for the next 1d6 rounds. The target suffers only normal damage for the unarmed strike, not sneak attack damage, when a rogue uses this ability.
Rainbow Stare	KEY:Rogue Special Ability ~ Rainbow Stare (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Class Feature.Rogue Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RogueSpecialAbilitySelection	PRETEXT:Must have survived passing through at least four layers of either a prismatic sphere or a prismatic wail.	SOURCEPAGE:p.516	DESC:New rogue special ability (10th level and higher, in place of a special ability). Somehow, while enduring a nearly overwhelming array of colors and light the rogue learned how to screen out dangerous images. She gains a +2 bonus on saving throws against figments and glamers and is completely immune to patterns. Prerequisite: Must have survived passing through at least four layers of either a prismatic sphere or a prismatic wail.
Saboteur	KEY:Rogue Special Ability ~ Saboteur (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Class Feature.Rogue Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RogueSpecialAbilitySelection	SOURCEPAGE:p.516	DESC:New rogue special ability (10th level and higher, in place of a special ability). The rogue's perception becomes so honed that he instantly notices even the most minute flaws in objects, enabling him to strike at their vulnerable points. When attacking objects or making a sunder attack action, the rogue may ignore an amount of hardness up to half his rogue class level. Further, constructs are no longer immune to the rogue's sneak attacks.
Swift Kick	KEY:Rogue Special Ability ~ Swift Kick (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Class Feature.Rogue Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RogueSpecialAbilitySelection	SOURCEPAGE:p.516	DESC:New rogue special ability (10th level and higher, in place of a special ability). Effortlessly examining mechanical devices, the rogue may affect them with a vigorous jolt. The rogue no longer needs tools to use the Disable Device skill (although he still gains the +2 circumstance bonus when using masterwork thieves' tools). In addition, the time it takes the rogue to use the Disable Device skill is reduced by one step. Difficult and wicked devices now require 1d4 rounds to disable, tricky devices require 1 round, and a simple device can be disabled as a free action.
Toxic Blood	KEY:Rogue Special Ability ~ Toxic Blood (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Class Feature.Rogue Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RogueSpecialAbilitySelection	PRETEXT:Constitution must have been reduced below 3 by poison.	SOURCEPAGE:p.516	DESC:New rogue special ability (10th level and higher, in place of a special ability). A permanent residue of poison courses through the rogue's veins. Any creature not immune to poison that bites the rogue must make a Fortitude save (DC 10 + half the rogue's class level + the rogue's Constitution modifier) or immediately take 1 point of Constitution damage. Once triggered, this ability does not function again for 1 hour. Prerequisite: Constitution must have been reduced below 3 by poison.
Point Blank Shot	KEY:Monk Bonus Feat ~ Point Blank Shot (Golarion Monk)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkBonusFeat.MonkBonusFeatLVL1	VISIBLE:DISPLAY	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=ACF,Monk ACF ~ Golarion Monk (DMC)	PREVARGTEQ:MonkBonusFeatLVL,1	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Point Blank Shot	SOURCEPAGE:p.366	DESC:Golarion monk bonus feat option at 1st level (no prerequisites needed, as other monk bonus feats).
Stunning Fist	KEY:Monk Bonus Feat ~ Stunning Fist (Golarion Monk)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkBonusFeat.MonkBonusFeatLVL2	VISIBLE:DISPLAY	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=ACF,Monk ACF ~ Golarion Monk (DMC)	PREVARGTEQ:MonkBonusFeatLVL,2	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Stunning Fist	SOURCEPAGE:p.366	DESC:Golarion monk bonus feat option at 2nd level (no prerequisites needed, as other monk bonus feats).
Rapid Shot	KEY:Monk Bonus Feat ~ Rapid Shot (Golarion Monk)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkBonusFeat.MonkBonusFeatLVL6	VISIBLE:DISPLAY	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=ACF,Monk ACF ~ Golarion Monk (DMC)	PREVARGTEQ:MonkBonusFeatLVL,6	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Rapid Shot	SOURCEPAGE:p.366	DESC:Golarion monk bonus feat option at 6th level (no prerequisites needed, as other monk bonus feats).
Resistant Body (Acid)	KEY:Planar Monk ~ Resistant Body (Acid)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:PlanarMonkResistantBody.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|AcidResistanceBonus|5	SOURCEPAGE:p.373	DESC:The planar monk hardens her body against acid: resistance 5.
Resistant Body (Cold)	KEY:Planar Monk ~ Resistant Body (Cold)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:PlanarMonkResistantBody.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|ColdResistanceBonus|5	SOURCEPAGE:p.373	DESC:The planar monk hardens her body against cold: resistance 5.
Resistant Body (Electricity)	KEY:Planar Monk ~ Resistant Body (Electricity)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:PlanarMonkResistantBody.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|ElectricityResistanceBonus|5	SOURCEPAGE:p.373	DESC:The planar monk hardens her body against electricity: resistance 5.
Resistant Body (Fire)	KEY:Planar Monk ~ Resistant Body (Fire)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:PlanarMonkResistantBody.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|FireResistanceBonus|5	SOURCEPAGE:p.373	DESC:The planar monk hardens her body against fire: resistance 5.
Resistant Body (Sonic)	KEY:Planar Monk ~ Resistant Body (Sonic)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:PlanarMonkResistantBody.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|SonicResistanceBonus|5	SOURCEPAGE:p.373	DESC:The planar monk hardens her body against sonic: resistance 5.
Janissary Knowledge Skills	KEY:Janissary Knowledge Skills	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	MULT:YES	CHOOSE:NUMCHOICES=2|SKILL|TYPE=Knowledge	CSKILL:LIST	SOURCEPAGE:p.285	DESC:Two Knowledge skills of his choice are class skills (janissary).
